WEBVTT

02:57.980 --> 03:01.703
So, good evening and welcome to our council meeting on April 23,

03:01.930 --> 03:05.074
2025. I'll now call on William Short,

03:05.242 --> 03:08.754
Regional Clerk, to do the roll call. Thank you, Chair Redman. Chair Redman.

03:08.802 --> 03:12.274
Present. Councillor Craig. Present. Councillor Erb. Councilor Foxton.

03:12.322 --> 03:15.538
Present. Councillor Huinink. Here. Councillor James.

03:15.634 --> 03:18.786
Present. Councillor Liggett. Councillor McCabe.

03:18.898 --> 03:22.034
Present. Councillor Nowak. Councillor Rodrigues.

03:22.082 --> 03:25.442
Present. Councillor Salonen. Councilor Shantz.

03:25.506 --> 03:28.706
Present. Councillor Vrbanovic. Councillor Wolf. Present.

03:28.738 --> 03:32.172
And we have regrets from Councillor Harris and Councillor Williams. Thank you,

03:32.196 --> 03:35.612
Chair. Thank you. I would like to acknowledge that the land on which we gather

03:35.676 --> 03:39.036
today is the traditional territory of the Haudenosaunee, the Anishinaabe

03:39.068 --> 03:42.124
and the Chonnonton Peoples. In doing so, I want to reflect

03:42.172 --> 03:46.092
on what it means to be doing important community work like we're engaging in collectively

03:46.156 --> 03:49.880
today And also in my own personal relationship to this land.

03:50.260 --> 03:53.708
We need to acknowledge the enduring presence of the Indigenous people with whom

03:53.724 --> 03:56.940
we share this land today, their achievements and their contributions

03:57.020 --> 04:00.572
to our community. I want to share a prayer that was written by

04:00.596 --> 04:05.176
Chief Stacey Laforme, who is an Anishinaabe author.

04:05.328 --> 04:09.304
And this comes from Living in the Tall Grass. We give thanks to

04:09.312 --> 04:12.792
the Creator for allowing this gathering. We ask that he guide us

04:12.816 --> 04:16.792
and forgive us when we falter and disappoint. For though we aspire

04:16.856 --> 04:20.500
to greatness, we are, after all, only human.

04:21.040 --> 04:24.776
Grant us clear mind, a pure heart and courage. A clear

04:24.848 --> 04:28.394
mind to make well thought out intelligent decisions. A pure

04:28.442 --> 04:32.170
heart to make decisions that are without personal bias or desire.

04:32.330 --> 04:36.250
And the courage to use both a clear mind and a pure heart in our

04:36.290 --> 04:40.634
lives. Let us set aside small differences. Let us concentrate

04:40.682 --> 04:44.298
on the real issues. Let us not be bogged down

04:44.354 --> 04:48.074
in rhetoric. Let us live each day with a feeling of accomplishment

04:48.122 --> 04:52.010
and pride. Most important, let us remember we are

04:52.050 --> 04:55.060
not enemies, nor are we adversaries.

04:55.220 --> 04:58.612
We share a similar past, a kindred spirit and

04:58.636 --> 05:02.388
a common heritage. We must always remember the real reason

05:02.444 --> 05:05.476
we gather is to do the right thing for our people,

05:05.628 --> 05:09.252
our children, and for our future. I hope that

05:09.276 --> 05:12.320
this puts us in a good mindset for a good meeting.

05:12.700 --> 05:16.532
Thank you, colleagues. I would now entertain a

05:16.556 --> 05:21.124
motion to go into closed and we have four reasons,

05:21.172 --> 05:24.932
as you can see up on the screen. Moved by Councillor Craig, seconded by

05:24.956 --> 05:26.200
Councillor Nowak.

05:28.460 --> 05:32.404
So I'd ask you to use eScribe to cast your ballot. I'm sorry,

05:32.452 --> 05:35.680
Chair, I don't have eScribe, but I'm in favor. Thank you.

05:53.190 --> 05:56.210
Councillor Salonen, are you in favor of going into closed.

05:57.590 --> 06:01.422
Thank you. That is

06:01.446 --> 06:04.570
carried Colleagues, we will now retire to the Waterloo Room.

01:37:48.390 --> 01:37:52.126
Colleagues, I'll now entertain a motion to reconvene

01:37:52.158 --> 01:37:55.566
in open session. If I could have a mover, Moved by Councillor

01:37:55.598 --> 01:37:59.150
Shantz. Seconded by Councillor Huinink. Please use your eScribe to

01:37:59.190 --> 01:38:03.250
vote and that the council will resume in open session.

01:38:05.600 --> 01:38:34.594
Colleagues,

01:38:34.642 --> 01:38:38.274
that is carried. We start this evening

01:38:38.322 --> 01:38:42.162
off with a wonderful function. I am delighted

01:38:42.226 --> 01:38:45.874
to welcome our newest councillor,

01:38:46.002 --> 01:38:49.650
Matt Rodrigues. So I will call on

01:38:49.690 --> 01:38:53.362
Tim Brubacher, Deputy Clerk and Manager of Legislative Services,

01:38:53.466 --> 01:38:56.594
to swear in our newest member of council, Councillor Matt

01:38:56.642 --> 01:38:59.830
Rodrigues. Please proceed to the roundtable Matt.

01:39:06.400 --> 01:39:09.816
I, Matt Rodrigues, have been appointed to the office of Regional

01:39:09.848 --> 01:39:13.656
Councillor in the Regional Municipality of Waterloo, Do solemnly

01:39:13.688 --> 01:39:17.672
promise and declare that I will truly, faithfully and

01:39:17.696 --> 01:39:20.840
impartially exercise this office to the best of my knowledge and

01:39:20.880 --> 01:39:24.824
ability. I have not received and will not receive any payment

01:39:24.872 --> 01:39:28.042
or reward or promise thereof for the exercise of

01:39:28.066 --> 01:39:31.658
this office in a biased, corrupt or any other

01:39:31.714 --> 01:39:35.194
improper manner. I will disclose any pecuniary

01:39:35.242 --> 01:39:38.442
interest, direct or indirect, in accordance with the

01:39:38.466 --> 01:39:42.746
Municipal Conflict of Interest Act. I will be faithful and bear true allegiance

01:39:42.778 --> 01:39:46.394
to His Majesty King Charles III and I make this solemn

01:39:46.442 --> 01:39:49.914
promise and declaration conscientiously believing it to

01:39:49.922 --> 01:39:53.370
be true and knowing that it is of the same force and effect as

01:39:53.410 --> 01:39:54.670
if made under oath.

01:40:03.090 --> 01:40:04.710
Congratulations. Thank you.

01:40:39.580 --> 01:40:43.556
Colleagues, are there any declarations of pecuniary interest under the Municipal Conflict

01:40:43.588 --> 01:40:47.594
of Interest Act? Seeing none,

01:40:47.722 --> 01:40:51.210
we're going to start this evening off with a presentation. I'd like to call

01:40:51.250 --> 01:40:55.034
on Doug Spooner, Acting Commissioner of Transport Services,

01:40:55.122 --> 01:40:59.178
Peter Sweeney, Commissioner Community services and Fiona McCrae,

01:40:59.274 --> 01:41:02.634
Regional Solicitor, provide a presentation on 100 Victoria

01:41:02.682 --> 01:41:05.790
Street North Kitchener Site specific bylaw.

01:41:09.250 --> 01:41:12.842
through you Chair, Good evening Regional Council. My colleagues Peter and Fiona will

01:41:12.866 --> 01:41:16.428
join me in speaking to this presentation shortly. I'll

01:41:16.444 --> 01:41:19.452
introduce the report and recommendations for your consideration.

01:41:19.596 --> 01:41:23.468
Next slide please. The Kitchener Central Transit

01:41:23.484 --> 01:41:27.644
Hub is a long term community infrastructure project for the region. Our new GRT

01:41:27.692 --> 01:41:31.052
business plan builds off the success of the ION light rail and its

01:41:31.076 --> 01:41:34.572
transformative impact and now focuses on increasing the speed and

01:41:34.596 --> 01:41:37.932
reliability of service, providing more service to new areas and

01:41:37.956 --> 01:41:41.676
making transit easier to use for residents. The Integrated Transit

01:41:41.708 --> 01:41:44.320
Hub also helps us achieve all of these priorities.

01:41:45.020 --> 01:41:48.276
KCTH will be a central easy to access integrated transit

01:41:48.308 --> 01:41:51.492
hub. A center point where all modes intersect.

01:41:51.636 --> 01:41:54.484
We'll have GRT buses, ION trains, Via Rail,

01:41:54.532 --> 01:41:58.532
GO transit trains and buses, car share, Neuron bikes and E-scooters,

01:41:58.676 --> 01:42:01.760
pedestrian and multi use trails, all connecting in one place.

01:42:02.540 --> 01:42:05.892
Investing in KCTH will drive significant economic impact by

01:42:05.916 --> 01:42:09.492
boosting local businesses, attracting private investment and connecting people effectively

01:42:09.556 --> 01:42:13.226
to jobs, services and opportunities across the region and beyond

01:42:13.338 --> 01:42:17.306
Along the Toronto Waterloo Innovation Corridor. The full vision

01:42:17.338 --> 01:42:20.522
for the site is a large scale mixed use, multi block development that

01:42:20.546 --> 01:42:23.722
spans from King street to Ahrens street that will include housing,

01:42:23.786 --> 01:42:27.402
commercial space and community uses. This vision will come together over

01:42:27.426 --> 01:42:31.082
the next 10 plus years with lots of public consultation to come along the

01:42:31.106 --> 01:42:34.794
way. Next slide please. Planning for

01:42:34.842 --> 01:42:38.282
KCTH has been underway for over a decade. Over that time we

01:42:38.306 --> 01:42:41.738
have acquired multiple adjacent properties along Victoria street to create

01:42:41.794 --> 01:42:45.766
one large site for the Transit Hub and long term KCTH mixed

01:42:45.798 --> 01:42:49.558
use project. We've also had significant community

01:42:49.614 --> 01:42:52.982
conversation around the Transit Hub. We've worked with design partners to

01:42:53.006 --> 01:42:57.126
develop the conceptual drawings of the Transit Hub and we've worked with Metrolinx

01:42:57.158 --> 01:43:01.414
to establish timing and construction work plans. The project is now entering

01:43:01.462 --> 01:43:05.094
its next phase, construction. this year preliminary

01:43:05.142 --> 01:43:08.230
work will begin on Victoria street along

01:43:08.270 --> 01:43:11.542
with the demolition of the proportion of Rumpel Felt building that does not have a

01:43:11.566 --> 01:43:15.042
heritage designation. specific to 100 Victoria,

01:43:15.106 --> 01:43:18.642
Metrolinx will require the property by March of 2026 in

01:43:18.666 --> 01:43:22.274
order to begin their construction. This work includes construction

01:43:22.322 --> 01:43:26.866
on the rail corridor of track that will be incorporated into the rail system immediately

01:43:26.898 --> 01:43:30.498
behind 100 Victoria Street North. They will also need to relocate

01:43:30.514 --> 01:43:33.682
the platforms from their current location down to KCTH and add

01:43:33.706 --> 01:43:37.458
a diversion track. The 100 Victoria site provides access

01:43:37.514 --> 01:43:40.962
to the corridor and will be used for construction preparation

01:43:41.026 --> 01:43:44.870
and you can appreciate the many safety aspects of working in a live rail corridor.

01:43:45.350 --> 01:43:49.182
There is much to be done between now and March of 2026 including important work

01:43:49.206 --> 01:43:52.542
with those who currently reside at 100 Victoria. Peter will speak to this in a

01:43:52.566 --> 01:43:56.270
moment. We also have to do site remediation that will take up to three

01:43:56.310 --> 01:44:00.398
months. This includes site cleanup and soil scraping, removal of any fuel leaks

01:44:00.414 --> 01:44:03.950
in the soil and environmental testing. These are standard practices

01:44:04.030 --> 01:44:07.406
for any site prep for a use of this type. This work

01:44:07.478 --> 01:44:11.504
and the Metrolinx timeline means that the region requires the property on December 1.

01:44:11.662 --> 01:44:14.892
This will allow us to meet our commitments to construction schedules with

01:44:14.916 --> 01:44:19.036
our partners including Metrolinx. And I will now hand things over to my colleague Peter

01:44:19.068 --> 01:44:21.880
who will speak to the support for those residing at the site.

01:44:24.340 --> 01:44:28.200
Thanks Doug and through you Chair and to Regional Council and to the community,

01:44:29.540 --> 01:44:33.548
Based on what you just heard and now that we have clarity on

01:44:33.684 --> 01:44:36.940
when the site is required for

01:44:37.060 --> 01:44:40.642
the Transit Hub, we can turn our attention and our focus

01:44:40.796 --> 01:44:44.710
over the coming months to support those who are currently residing at 100

01:44:44.750 --> 01:44:48.054
Victoria. Should council approve

01:44:48.182 --> 01:44:51.254
the report and the recommendation this evening,

01:44:51.382 --> 01:44:55.830
additional resources will be allocated to accommodate this transition

01:44:55.990 --> 01:45:00.054
to safer options. This will include enhanced site supports,

01:45:00.102 --> 01:45:03.526
which focus efforts and resources on current residents for available housing

01:45:03.558 --> 01:45:07.872
and shelter options and ongoing site management. Our unsheltered

01:45:07.936 --> 01:45:11.808
support workers are on site regularly working with each resident

01:45:11.984 --> 01:45:15.900
on their individual housing plan That will continue throughout this process.

01:45:16.440 --> 01:45:20.432
I want to acknowledge that our unsheltered support workers are all registered

01:45:20.496 --> 01:45:24.240
social workers. They have professional obligations to their

01:45:24.280 --> 01:45:27.600
college and to their work and to the people they serve.

01:45:27.760 --> 01:45:31.136
They will be on site for one job and one job only.

01:45:31.288 --> 01:45:34.592
That is to develop, build and enhance relationships on a

01:45:34.616 --> 01:45:38.508
one on one basis, Develop case plans based

01:45:38.564 --> 01:45:41.996
on the unique needs identified by individuals

01:45:42.028 --> 01:45:45.548
they interact with. I want to also acknowledge that in recent

01:45:45.604 --> 01:45:49.372
years we have made significant investments across

01:45:49.476 --> 01:45:53.356
the system, including enhanced shelter capacity

01:45:53.468 --> 01:45:57.292
across this community. We've created 2,700 more affordable homes under

01:45:57.316 --> 01:46:01.436
the Building Better Futures plan. This includes 600 more units alone

01:46:01.468 --> 01:46:05.436
for Waterloo Regional Housing. And of course, we've also worked closely

01:46:05.468 --> 01:46:09.756
with the community to create a plan to end chronic homelessness by 2030.

01:46:09.908 --> 01:46:12.604
And with that, I'll hand it over to my colleague Fiona to speak about the

01:46:12.612 --> 01:46:13.440
bylaw.

01:46:16.980 --> 01:46:19.560
Thank you, Peter. Through you, Chair and to Council,

01:46:20.420 --> 01:46:23.160
there are two components to the proposed approach.

01:46:23.460 --> 01:46:26.988
The first is a recommendation for a site specific bylaw for

01:46:27.044 --> 01:46:31.069
100 Victoria requiring the site to be vacant by December

01:46:31.210 --> 01:46:34.660
1, 2025. This is before you this evening for your

01:46:34.700 --> 01:46:38.036
consideration. As Doug mentioned,

01:46:38.068 --> 01:46:42.116
the region is required to complete due diligence and site preparation prior

01:46:42.148 --> 01:46:45.540
to handover of the property to Metrolinx. This work

01:46:45.580 --> 01:46:49.492
will take approximately three months to complete and cannot be undertaken

01:46:49.556 --> 01:46:51.960
with an encampment present on the property.

01:46:52.540 --> 01:46:56.052
Further, as Peter mentioned, the second recommendation that

01:46:56.076 --> 01:47:01.870
forms part of the report is is an addition of $814,333

01:47:01.950 --> 01:47:06.142
to the 2025 Regional Housing Budget to

01:47:06.166 --> 01:47:09.450
support the transition of current residents from the site.

01:47:10.230 --> 01:47:13.246
And finally, in the context of the decision of Mr.

01:47:13.278 --> 01:47:16.782
Justice Valente in the region versus persons unknown and

01:47:16.806 --> 01:47:20.862
to be ascertained, Region staff intend to seek further direction

01:47:20.926 --> 01:47:24.798
from the Superior Court of Justice to the extent this is feasible and

01:47:24.854 --> 01:47:27.970
compatible with the anticipated construction schedule.

01:47:30.710 --> 01:47:33.810
With that, we're here to answer questions.

01:47:35.110 --> 01:47:38.062
There'll be no questions at this point in time. We are now going to go

01:47:38.086 --> 01:47:42.450
to delegations. Thank you. We have no petitions tonight.

01:47:43.430 --> 01:47:47.310
so to the delegations tonight, We have

01:47:47.350 --> 01:47:51.038
received a few late registrations, so they're, I think

01:47:51.094 --> 01:47:54.670
we're up to 27 or 28. I'd like to remind all

01:47:54.710 --> 01:47:57.730
delegations of some guidelines for participation.

01:47:58.120 --> 01:48:01.648
For those who are joining us in person, please proceed to the podium

01:48:01.744 --> 01:48:05.104
When you're called upon to speak, please press the button at

01:48:05.112 --> 01:48:08.704
the base of the microphone to turn it on. If the light is green,

01:48:08.752 --> 01:48:12.688
the microphone is on. For those who are joining us electronically,

01:48:12.784 --> 01:48:16.480
please leave your video or camera off and your

01:48:16.520 --> 01:48:20.320
microphone muted until you're called upon to speak. You will

01:48:20.360 --> 01:48:24.364
have five minutes for anyone who registered before the deadline

01:48:24.512 --> 01:48:28.228
and three minutes for anyone who registered after the deadline.

01:48:28.404 --> 01:48:32.180
If you conduct yourself in any of the following manners, it will result in

01:48:32.220 --> 01:48:35.972
immediate removal from the meeting. interrupting councillors,

01:48:36.036 --> 01:48:39.924
staff, or other delegations. derogatory statements

01:48:39.972 --> 01:48:43.380
about councillors, staff or others. turning your

01:48:43.420 --> 01:48:47.124
camera on at inappropriate times and hate speech

01:48:47.172 --> 01:48:50.596
or defamatory comments. One last reminder

01:48:50.628 --> 01:48:54.308
for delegations, please do not take offense if your presentation

01:48:54.404 --> 01:48:58.240
has no questions from Council. This is Council's time to really

01:48:58.280 --> 01:49:01.760
listen and reflect upon the opinions and the ideas that have been shared with

01:49:01.800 --> 01:49:05.376
us from the community. Our first registered delegate

01:49:05.408 --> 01:49:07.700
is Chloe Young from Waterloo.

01:49:08.200 --> 01:49:11.792
Chloe, welcome, Come to the

01:49:11.816 --> 01:49:15.456
podium and you have five minutes

01:49:15.488 --> 01:49:16.260
to speak.

01:49:24.930 --> 01:49:28.586
There should be a presentation pulled up, if possible. Did you provide

01:49:28.658 --> 01:49:31.870
slides? Yeah, I just checked in with the. Okay.

01:49:40.050 --> 01:49:44.042
Okay. So I represent myself as an individual with

01:49:44.066 --> 01:49:47.402
reconnections to the Waterloo region. And I wanted to open up

01:49:47.426 --> 01:49:51.318
with the realities of cancer first. Two in five

01:49:51.374 --> 01:49:54.966
Canadians will have or have had some form of cancer

01:49:54.998 --> 01:49:58.166
at some point in their lives and one of four of those individuals will die

01:49:58.198 --> 01:50:01.654
from it. My grandfather, for instance, used to go to

01:50:01.662 --> 01:50:05.366
the St Jacobs Market weekly to sell magnetic jewellery

01:50:05.478 --> 01:50:08.518
until he passed away five years ago, the same year he was diagnosed.

01:50:08.694 --> 01:50:12.630
On a population level, however, fewer people personally know people

01:50:12.670 --> 01:50:16.028
who inject drugs and people who use illicit drugs. And this has left their health

01:50:16.084 --> 01:50:19.980
care to be the nice thing to do rather than the shared responsibility

01:50:20.060 --> 01:50:23.708
that all of us bear, even as we sat before the brave people who showed

01:50:23.724 --> 01:50:27.036
up earlier this month and today to tell you why they and their loved ones

01:50:27.068 --> 01:50:30.844
deserve to live. I'll start by presenting the findings, as you see on the

01:50:30.852 --> 01:50:34.236
slide, from the Auditor General of Ontario regarding the opioid

01:50:34.268 --> 01:50:37.612
crisis strategy and as a person who has or an

01:50:37.636 --> 01:50:41.588
entity that has no stake in whatever happens to CTSs from a funding perspective.

01:50:41.724 --> 01:50:45.476
Next slide. So in investigating those decisions on CTSs,

01:50:45.508 --> 01:50:49.492
they identified that the Ministry was well aware of the risks, including emergency

01:50:49.556 --> 01:50:53.332
department visits, public use and risk of death. Next slide.

01:50:53.476 --> 01:50:56.756
In response, they provide some recommendations in an open ended manner,

01:50:56.868 --> 01:51:00.340
asking to develop risk plans and work with Stakeholders of those

01:51:00.380 --> 01:51:04.276
who would be affected by the closures. Next slide. And so the ministry responded

01:51:04.388 --> 01:51:08.388
by saying that we will deliver on these recommendations, but with a focus

01:51:08.444 --> 01:51:12.176
on transitioning away from and converting existing

01:51:12.288 --> 01:51:16.096
services to HART hubs. Shifting away again from harm

01:51:16.128 --> 01:51:20.192
reduction and, Next slide, I will now present my understanding

01:51:20.256 --> 01:51:24.160
of Ontario's viewpoint so far, based on public statements, the auditor report and

01:51:24.200 --> 01:51:27.744
the data from the committee meeting, is we see what CTSs

01:51:27.792 --> 01:51:31.504
have to offer, but we'll give you four times funding for HART hubs instead.

01:51:31.632 --> 01:51:35.200
While CTSs decrease risk of death and public drug use, they should

01:51:35.240 --> 01:51:38.538
provide different services from the ones that decrease risk of death

01:51:38.594 --> 01:51:42.810
and public drug use. In fact, we'll withhold money for HART hubs if CTSs continue

01:51:42.850 --> 01:51:47.130
to operate. So consider this same argument Other healthcare measures

01:51:47.210 --> 01:51:51.050
say, Next slide, Psychotherapy and antidepressants

01:51:51.210 --> 01:51:55.178
or, Next slide, Chemotherapy and immunotherapy.

01:51:55.274 --> 01:51:59.870
We can recognize that a one size fits all approach that recognizes.

01:52:00.930 --> 01:52:04.410
Sorry, a one size fits all approach is inadequate for depression and cancer.

01:52:04.490 --> 01:52:08.354
Why can't we do the same for addiction? We know that the justification of protecting

01:52:08.402 --> 01:52:12.002
communities doesn't come as an isolated policy, but as a piece in other proposed measures

01:52:12.066 --> 01:52:15.698
like, Next slide, This proposed legislation where people

01:52:15.754 --> 01:52:20.034
using illegal substances in public, including in encampments, and not complying with police

01:52:20.122 --> 01:52:23.650
orders to stop using or to leave the space, can be arrested without

01:52:23.690 --> 01:52:26.754
a warrant, fined or jailed for up to six months.

01:52:26.922 --> 01:52:31.330
So not only are we needlessly piling vulnerable people into our already strained hospitals,

01:52:31.410 --> 01:52:35.084
Next slide, We're also going to overcrowd, already overcrowded

01:52:35.132 --> 01:52:38.252
provincial jails where 81% of individuals are just

01:52:38.276 --> 01:52:41.516
waiting for their trial. It's transferring responsibility one after another

01:52:41.588 --> 01:52:44.300
And underpinning all of this is the devaluation of human life.

01:52:44.420 --> 01:52:47.852
It's treating people's lives like hot potatoes, tossing them from one place

01:52:47.876 --> 01:52:51.804
to another. And the belief that if you, some of the most marginalized and vulnerable

01:52:51.852 --> 01:52:55.132
people of our society, don't pay for your health care, you take what you can

01:52:55.156 --> 01:52:57.452
get. And if you don't take what you can get, then you will go to

01:52:57.476 --> 01:53:00.732
jail because, And that will be your fault too, because you didn't go to the

01:53:00.756 --> 01:53:03.852
services that we funded. And even if you did, it was your fault if you

01:53:03.876 --> 01:53:07.548
relapsed or your fault for not having somewhere to use away from the public

01:53:07.604 --> 01:53:11.500
eye. No one chooses to get cancer, mental illness or addiction.

01:53:11.580 --> 01:53:14.844
Yes, people can choose whether they can get better. And people have been choosing in

01:53:14.852 --> 01:53:19.068
a way that has actually, Next slide, Saved their lives 179

01:53:19.124 --> 01:53:22.460
times here in 150 Duke street within the span of one year.

01:53:22.580 --> 01:53:26.296
Not everyone will use antidepressants. Not everyone will use psychotherapy.

01:53:26.408 --> 01:53:29.848
Some will use both, some will use neither. It's the same for chemotherapy

01:53:29.864 --> 01:53:33.064
and immunotherapy, and it's the same for CTSs and HART hubs.

01:53:33.192 --> 01:53:36.680
It is not a trolley problem of killing one person to avoid killing five others,

01:53:36.720 --> 01:53:39.864
but a question of why this train is existing in the first place.

01:53:39.952 --> 01:53:43.656
Chloe you have one minute remaining. Okay, thank you. At the end of the day, the requested

01:53:43.688 --> 01:53:47.528
motion is to send a letter requesting for additional funding for life saving services.

01:53:47.664 --> 01:53:51.336
Next slide. I don't believe that anyone here

01:53:51.408 --> 01:53:55.502
would entertain the stance or be as fearful of reprisal

01:53:55.646 --> 01:53:58.878
if the stance was as ridiculous

01:53:58.894 --> 01:54:02.638
as this one here. So why are we entertaining them for CTSs?

01:54:02.734 --> 01:54:06.446
It is ultimately concession towards rigid ideals of what addiction recovery

01:54:06.478 --> 01:54:09.410
looks like. And concession is not going to prevent people from dying.

01:54:09.750 --> 01:54:13.422
Funding life saving health care services like CTS cannot be treated as an act of

01:54:13.446 --> 01:54:17.070
charity nor as a perverse incentive. It is a moral imperative of

01:54:17.110 --> 01:54:20.334
the province. And I ask the council today to engage with them

01:54:20.502 --> 01:54:23.534
at a minimum and ask them to uphold this duty in the spirit of the

01:54:23.542 --> 01:54:27.134
Ontario Superior Court's injunction by continuing to fund CTSs.

01:54:27.262 --> 01:54:30.990
Don't bite the hand that feeds, but don't allow it to keep it under its

01:54:31.030 --> 01:54:34.650
thumb. Please vote yes on Councillor Wolf's motion. Thank you.

01:54:35.830 --> 01:54:39.550
Thank you, Chloe. Great timing. I see No questions. The next

01:54:39.590 --> 01:54:42.850
delegation is Anne Loeffler from New Hamburg.

01:54:44.390 --> 01:54:47.490
And welcome. You have the podium and you have five minutes.

01:54:49.110 --> 01:54:52.130
Thank you. There should be a PowerPoint presentation.

01:54:58.790 --> 01:55:02.570
Do we have the PowerPoint? They're getting it up, I think.

01:55:06.870 --> 01:55:09.902
Okay. Thank you. Good evening. My name is Anne Loeffler.

01:55:09.966 --> 01:55:14.208
I'm a retired conservation specialist and professional agrologist.

01:55:14.374 --> 01:55:18.720
And I worked in the conservation authority system for my entire career.

01:55:19.060 --> 01:55:22.412
First of all, did you know that this week is actually National Soil

01:55:22.476 --> 01:55:25.756
Conservation Week? I'm here as a concerned

01:55:25.788 --> 01:55:29.532
citizen of Wilmot Township to raise an urgent concern about escalating

01:55:29.596 --> 01:55:33.372
soil erosion on the Bleams Road Property purchased by the region

01:55:33.476 --> 01:55:37.452
last summer as part of the Wilmot Land Assembly. You remember

01:55:37.516 --> 01:55:40.720
that while conducting due diligence on the land purchase,

01:55:40.860 --> 01:55:44.920
the region hired a contractor to destroy the standing corn crop.

01:55:45.080 --> 01:55:48.728
The contractor repeatedly tilled the land and this

01:55:48.784 --> 01:55:51.944
left the soil bare, shattered and highly vulnerable

01:55:51.992 --> 01:55:55.208
to erosion. Last November, I wrote to this

01:55:55.264 --> 01:55:59.448
council warning of the potential for serious soil erosion.

01:55:59.624 --> 01:56:03.496
I provided recommendations for best management practices to mitigate

01:56:03.528 --> 01:56:07.160
the risk. Unfortunately, the region did not take any

01:56:07.200 --> 01:56:10.180
actions to address the potential erosion from the site.

01:56:10.540 --> 01:56:13.908
The current slide shows an aerial photo of the site.

01:56:14.044 --> 01:56:17.444
The red polygon shows the property lines of the parcel

01:56:17.492 --> 01:56:20.868
purchased by the region. Note that there are at least three

01:56:20.924 --> 01:56:24.548
catch basins on the property line between the region's farm

01:56:24.604 --> 01:56:28.756
and the neighbouring farm. Surface flow direction is to the southwest

01:56:28.868 --> 01:56:32.436
or lower left of the map. Also note the open creek

01:56:32.468 --> 01:56:36.372
at Bleams Road. Earlier this month I walked back to

01:56:36.396 --> 01:56:40.510
view the property in question From across the fence line. I

01:56:40.550 --> 01:56:44.238
saw significant erosion damage. I'm here tonight to show you

01:56:44.294 --> 01:56:47.918
photos of the consequences of the region's inaction.

01:56:48.094 --> 01:56:53.198
Next slide please. The entire 160

01:56:53.254 --> 01:56:56.910
acre farm remains barren with virtually no living

01:56:56.990 --> 01:57:00.046
or dead plant material to protect the soil.

01:57:00.238 --> 01:57:04.046
Large silt deposits are visible in close proximity to the catch

01:57:04.078 --> 01:57:08.074
basins and property line. It's apparent that soil erosion

01:57:08.122 --> 01:57:10.986
is actively occurring during heavy rainfalls.

01:57:11.178 --> 01:57:15.082
Sediment laden runoff is likely flowing into at least three or four

01:57:15.106 --> 01:57:18.186
catch basins that connect directly to a closed

01:57:18.218 --> 01:57:22.390
municipal drain that was installed in fall of 2023.

01:57:22.770 --> 01:57:26.442
The sediment is being transported 200 meters into a

01:57:26.466 --> 01:57:30.042
Nith river tributary which feeds into the Grand and

01:57:30.066 --> 01:57:34.290
which is the drinking water source for over 100,000 people downstream,

01:57:34.410 --> 01:57:38.194
including Brantford and Six Nations. There's evidence

01:57:38.322 --> 01:57:42.370
of off site sediment deposition on neighboring farmland in

01:57:42.410 --> 01:57:46.190
the floodplain around the municipal tile. Next slide please.

01:57:47.290 --> 01:57:51.170
So to be clear, this is not a normal amount of soil erosion.

01:57:51.330 --> 01:57:54.626
This is absolutely appalling. This is what happens

01:57:54.658 --> 01:57:58.466
when soil gets pulverized by repeated tillage and is then left

01:57:58.538 --> 01:58:02.384
without any protective cover. In my 30 year career

01:58:02.432 --> 01:58:06.384
as a conservation specialist, this is easily the worst erosion

01:58:06.432 --> 01:58:10.272
that I have seen on flat land. What you see here is

01:58:10.296 --> 01:58:13.552
soil left behind. We don't know exactly how

01:58:13.576 --> 01:58:17.152
many tons of soil were washed away into the watercourse, but we

01:58:17.176 --> 01:58:20.448
know it was a substantial loss. The key point

01:58:20.504 --> 01:58:24.672
here is that large amounts of sediment entering a watercourse

01:58:24.736 --> 01:58:28.520
increase the cost of treating drinking water for the municipalities

01:58:28.600 --> 01:58:32.664
downstream. Ironically, the region destroyed

01:58:32.712 --> 01:58:36.392
a standing corn crop in the name of due diligence to complete a real

01:58:36.416 --> 01:58:40.248
estate transaction, but hasn't taken any action on

01:58:40.384 --> 01:58:42.220
environmental due diligence.

01:58:44.080 --> 01:58:47.432
In this context, that would include taking proactive steps to

01:58:47.456 --> 01:58:51.048
prevent soil erosion from negatively impacting

01:58:51.224 --> 01:58:53.980
surrounding water bodies and downstream communities.

01:58:54.820 --> 01:58:57.900
I'm calling on the region to take immediate corrective action

01:58:57.940 --> 01:59:01.324
on the Bleams road property, including installing

01:59:01.372 --> 01:59:05.356
silt fences or other barriers to protect hatch basins from further sediment

01:59:05.388 --> 01:59:08.956
entry and establishing a crop or cover crop across

01:59:09.028 --> 01:59:12.236
the entire farm as soon as possible. Anne you have a minute

01:59:12.268 --> 01:59:15.884
remaining. The region might also Want to consider their potential legal

01:59:15.932 --> 01:59:20.012
exposure. Specifically with regards to the Federal Fisheries act and

01:59:20.036 --> 01:59:23.452
a number of provincial laws that deal with pollution discharges and

01:59:23.476 --> 01:59:27.948
drainage. You have an opportunity here to lead by example

01:59:28.124 --> 01:59:31.804
in responsible land stewardship. Currently, the region's

01:59:31.852 --> 01:59:35.400
inaction pollutes drinking water, damages the environment,

01:59:35.700 --> 01:59:39.452
leaves the region vulnerable to legal action and undermines

01:59:39.516 --> 01:59:42.320
public confidence in how public lands are managed.

01:59:42.820 --> 01:59:46.332
You're aware that the region of Waterloo gets part of their water supply

01:59:46.396 --> 01:59:49.878
from the Grand River and therefore is vulnerable to land use

01:59:49.934 --> 01:59:54.214
decisions made by those upstream. I ask you tonight to consider

01:59:54.302 --> 01:59:57.622
our vulnerability here in the region of Waterloo and

01:59:57.646 --> 02:00:01.142
remember the Golden Rule. Do unto others as you would

02:00:01.166 --> 02:00:05.334
have others do unto you. Or in this case, treat downstream

02:00:05.382 --> 02:00:09.126
municipalities the way you'd like upstream municipalities to treat

02:00:09.198 --> 02:00:12.598
you. Thank you. Anne thank you. And we have a question

02:00:12.654 --> 02:00:15.812
from Councillor Salonen. Thank you very much. Through you, Chair,

02:00:15.916 --> 02:00:19.092
Anne, just as a Wilmot resident, I want to say thank you very much for

02:00:19.116 --> 02:00:22.516
coming out and for your presentation this evening. And I was just curious

02:00:22.548 --> 02:00:26.644
if staff can follow up with council via email on the concerns raised,

02:00:26.772 --> 02:00:30.372
if that could be direction. Rod?

02:00:30.436 --> 02:00:33.908
Yes, certainly. We'd be happy to. Thank you. Thanks again Anne.

02:00:34.044 --> 02:00:37.972
Thank you. Thanks, Anne. Next delegation

02:00:38.036 --> 02:00:40.600
is Krista Straus from New Hamburg.

02:00:41.630 --> 02:00:45.350
Krista, welcome. And you have the floor and five minutes.

02:00:45.510 --> 02:00:49.254
Good evening, Chair Redman. Council and members of the public.

02:00:49.422 --> 02:00:53.110
I'm here as a granddaughter of farmers. I'm here as somebody that has worked on

02:00:53.150 --> 02:00:56.422
farms in the past and currently work in a related field. I went

02:00:56.446 --> 02:00:59.990
to Waterloo Oxford Secondary School and graduated from the University of

02:01:00.030 --> 02:01:03.798
Guelph. I am not a part of Fight for Farmland or Wilmot Can,

02:01:03.934 --> 02:01:08.090
but I support them both. I'm here as a resident of New Hamburg.

02:01:08.600 --> 02:01:12.160
I'm here representing those voices in my town that you have not

02:01:12.200 --> 02:01:15.232
heard from yet. It's nerve wracking to come up

02:01:15.256 --> 02:01:18.992
here. as

02:01:19.016 --> 02:01:22.660
well as friends and families that are farmers or work in Agriculture.

02:01:23.320 --> 02:01:27.232
The 770 acres, This is not how we should treat our farmers or

02:01:27.256 --> 02:01:28.460
people in my community.

02:01:30.760 --> 02:01:34.640
These farmers in Wilmot, they want to keep farming on their land. They bring

02:01:34.680 --> 02:01:38.702
a strong spirit of entrepreneurship and that's what we're known for

02:01:38.726 --> 02:01:41.850
around the region, In the region, even around Canada.

02:01:42.950 --> 02:01:46.814
They support our local economy and other businesses.

02:01:46.862 --> 02:01:50.174
They produce local food and give back to the community in many ways.

02:01:50.302 --> 02:01:53.870
Not only are they committed to the community, they bring passion to

02:01:53.910 --> 02:01:57.886
agriculture and they're good stewards of this land. They have survived

02:01:57.918 --> 02:02:01.406
the 2008 financial crisis. They've survived

02:02:01.518 --> 02:02:04.916
Covid and they'll probably survive these tariffs granted

02:02:04.948 --> 02:02:08.676
They still have this land. and because they're

02:02:08.708 --> 02:02:12.884
Ontario businesses producing Ontario products for Ontario

02:02:12.932 --> 02:02:16.852
consumers. And right now that has never been more

02:02:16.876 --> 02:02:20.920
important than right now to support Canadian, to buy Canadian.

02:02:21.900 --> 02:02:25.220
And if you pressure them into selling, first of all, this is

02:02:25.260 --> 02:02:29.172
prime agricultural land. I don't know why there's any debate about that. This is

02:02:29.196 --> 02:02:32.900
good land. And if you pressure them into selling, it's going to affect their business

02:02:33.020 --> 02:02:36.174
as well as all the farmers around, If a mega site goes

02:02:36.182 --> 02:02:39.934
in. many who want to invest back in their business or expand

02:02:40.062 --> 02:02:44.158
but are wondering who will be next and how will you protect these other

02:02:44.214 --> 02:02:47.582
farmers. There'll be no way to do that because this is going to set a

02:02:47.606 --> 02:02:50.850
dangerous precedent even in Ontario.

02:02:51.510 --> 02:02:54.494
And I am told that we have tons of farmland in the region,

02:02:54.662 --> 02:02:58.350
but how much of it is actually owned by developers? How much

02:02:58.390 --> 02:03:01.740
is actually owned by those wanting to,

02:03:02.120 --> 02:03:05.712
or waiting to mine it for aggregates. and

02:03:05.736 --> 02:03:09.360
this 770 acres, This was the first

02:03:09.400 --> 02:03:13.488
question asked at the New Hamburg Board of Trade debate where all

02:03:13.544 --> 02:03:16.880
federal candidates were concerned and they agreed that

02:03:16.920 --> 02:03:20.576
farmers should not be pressured into selling this land or expropriate

02:03:20.608 --> 02:03:24.112
it. This was also another question that was asked at the

02:03:24.136 --> 02:03:26.820
provincial debate too in my town of New Hamburg.

02:03:28.190 --> 02:03:30.490
New Hamburg is so close to Stratford,

02:03:31.310 --> 02:03:34.774
every year hosts the Canadian Dairy Expo and it's the largest

02:03:34.822 --> 02:03:38.742
one in Canada. And it's no coincidence that it's in

02:03:38.766 --> 02:03:42.134
Stratford because this area, including New Hamburg,

02:03:42.182 --> 02:03:45.130
is known as the dairy heartland of Ontario.

02:03:45.550 --> 02:03:49.238
So if you're a dairy farmer or a farm to fork cheese producer,

02:03:49.334 --> 02:03:52.774
New Hamburg makes sense. We have a local high school that supports

02:03:52.822 --> 02:03:56.240
agriculture. And we are close to the University of Guelph

02:03:56.320 --> 02:03:59.472
where they have recently said that for every grad in agriculture

02:03:59.536 --> 02:04:03.040
there are four good paying jobs waiting for them. We're close to two

02:04:03.080 --> 02:04:06.832
universities and a college in which many of those grads end

02:04:06.856 --> 02:04:10.448
up going to agriculture as well. I think of the trades,

02:04:10.544 --> 02:04:14.016
I think of business and I think of the culinary school.

02:04:14.168 --> 02:04:17.552
And it's been said there may be no better place in the

02:04:17.576 --> 02:04:21.360
world than Waterloo region to enjoy the Farm to

02:04:21.400 --> 02:04:25.082
Fork experience. This was set on a show that was

02:04:25.106 --> 02:04:28.666
sponsored by Explore Waterloo Region. And if you watched

02:04:28.698 --> 02:04:32.150
the very first episode, you might recognize some of the farmers in that show.

02:04:33.170 --> 02:04:36.922
This powerful statement highlights that

02:04:36.946 --> 02:04:39.630
we have a thriving local food culture. And

02:04:40.050 --> 02:04:43.578
I heard one person say that this is the way that we've always

02:04:43.634 --> 02:04:46.310
assembled land for the last hundred years.

02:04:47.330 --> 02:04:51.108
However, we created the country sideline. So I don't

02:04:51.124 --> 02:04:54.320
agree with that. Krista, you have a minute remaining. Okay, thank you.

02:04:55.100 --> 02:04:58.676
And it was supposed to protect our prime farmland in a way that allowed

02:04:58.708 --> 02:05:02.772
farmers to thrive. The region has spent countless

02:05:02.836 --> 02:05:06.628
hours and resources on creating the country sideline. And I'm

02:05:06.644 --> 02:05:10.084
not mistaken, the region even went to court to defend this,

02:05:10.172 --> 02:05:13.284
which says a lot for a municipality to actually defend

02:05:13.332 --> 02:05:17.052
something in court. And it

02:05:17.076 --> 02:05:20.492
was, I really think the country sideline was supposed to protect,

02:05:20.636 --> 02:05:24.252
was supposed to prevent stuff like this from actually happening

02:05:24.316 --> 02:05:28.044
here. And I don't know what the country sideline

02:05:28.092 --> 02:05:32.300
means anymore, but I still believe Waterloo region residents

02:05:32.380 --> 02:05:36.348
still believe in it. And every planning document at

02:05:36.404 --> 02:05:40.332
every different levels of government talks about the need to protect farmland.

02:05:40.476 --> 02:05:43.532
And if we're really serious about that, we have to do more than just put

02:05:43.556 --> 02:05:46.906
words on paper. Protection only works if we act when it matters.

02:05:46.938 --> 02:05:50.810
And that time is now. The farmers on this land are feeding us,

02:05:50.850 --> 02:05:53.594
supporting local businesses and giving back to the community.

02:05:53.762 --> 02:05:57.322
This land isn't waiting to become developed. It already has

02:05:57.346 --> 02:06:01.306
a purpose. Thank you. Krista, Thank you very much.

02:06:01.458 --> 02:06:04.874
Councillor Salonen. Thank you. Through you, Chair, just quickly,

02:06:04.922 --> 02:06:08.282
thank you very much, Krista, for coming. It's always nice to see you at

02:06:08.306 --> 02:06:11.030
the chambers and I appreciate you bringing your thoughts forward.

02:06:12.450 --> 02:06:16.350
The next delegation is Sidney MacDonald from Kitchener.

02:06:19.970 --> 02:06:23.550
Sidney, welcome. You have the podium and you have five minutes.

02:06:27.330 --> 02:06:31.306
I think this is still on. Okay. Good evening, chair and councillors.

02:06:31.418 --> 02:06:34.682
My name is Sid and I am a local advocate for housing justice in our

02:06:34.706 --> 02:06:38.522
community and more specifically for gender equity in our local services

02:06:38.626 --> 02:06:42.394
for unhoused women and gender diverse folks. I'm thankful to have

02:06:42.402 --> 02:06:45.418
the opportunity to speak to you tonight. And I understand that I'm

02:06:45.434 --> 02:06:48.522
the first in a full night of delegations around this bylaw you are voting on

02:06:48.546 --> 02:06:51.850
today. I'm also so thankful to the delegates in this

02:06:51.890 --> 02:06:55.306
room who are standing up for the rights of our unhoused community members

02:06:55.458 --> 02:06:59.498
and those who are here to show their support of voting down this bylaw.

02:06:59.674 --> 02:07:03.242
I want to particularly highlight our women in leadership who sit at this

02:07:03.266 --> 02:07:06.986
horseshoe and those of which I have heard emphasize the needs

02:07:07.058 --> 02:07:10.520
of women and gender diverse folks experiencing homelessness in your

02:07:10.560 --> 02:07:14.360
public conversations in this room. I'm looking to

02:07:14.400 --> 02:07:17.832
you to consider the serious concerns around this bylaw and

02:07:17.856 --> 02:07:20.856
what it means for women and gender diverse individuals.

02:07:21.048 --> 02:07:25.144
The bylaw relies on the assertion that the region has greatly expanded accessible

02:07:25.192 --> 02:07:28.744
shelter beds and this is absolutely false for women and gender diverse

02:07:28.792 --> 02:07:32.584
individuals In particular. There are approximately 60

02:07:32.672 --> 02:07:36.472
shelter beds in this region designated specifically for

02:07:36.496 --> 02:07:40.392
women and gender diverse folks, which local research has highlighted is

02:07:40.416 --> 02:07:44.140
needed to ensure the safety and appropriate support of this demographic.

02:07:44.480 --> 02:07:47.944
This total of approximately 60 beds does not equal

02:07:47.992 --> 02:07:51.512
an increase of beds for women and gender diverse folks and is in fact a

02:07:51.536 --> 02:07:55.448
decrease, Considering we had 66 beds at the start of 2024

02:07:55.584 --> 02:07:59.576
before Mary's Place was closed for months. Appropriate and safe

02:07:59.608 --> 02:08:03.500
shelter for women and gender diverse individuals remains woefully inadequate.

02:08:03.930 --> 02:08:07.490
This bylaw also prohibits residents from moving their tents without

02:08:07.530 --> 02:08:11.910
the region's permission, restricting free movement with serious safety implications.

02:08:12.330 --> 02:08:15.810
for women and gender diverse individuals, The ability to move a tent

02:08:15.890 --> 02:08:19.138
is a way to increase visibility, have a light over their heads

02:08:19.154 --> 02:08:23.350
at night or distance themselves from someone who makes them feel unsafe.

02:08:23.850 --> 02:08:27.282
This clause is not only carceral, it is not at all trauma

02:08:27.346 --> 02:08:30.562
informed as it removes autonomy and safety

02:08:30.626 --> 02:08:33.970
from women and gender diverse folks who are residing there.

02:08:34.430 --> 02:08:37.654
Speaking of control, I ask that you consider the punitive measures

02:08:37.702 --> 02:08:41.766
in response to the list of prohibited activities. What happens

02:08:41.798 --> 02:08:45.350
under this bylaw If a woman defends herself against harassment and

02:08:45.390 --> 02:08:48.934
violence on site? Would she be considered in violation

02:08:48.982 --> 02:08:52.530
of the bylaw and removed from the encampment with nowhere else to go?

02:08:53.150 --> 02:08:56.598
Are contracted security guards and facilities workers

02:08:56.654 --> 02:09:00.490
informed and trained to handle that scenario safely and appropriately?

02:09:01.900 --> 02:09:05.668
If the region is committed to gender equity, if it is committed to human

02:09:05.724 --> 02:09:09.492
rights, this bylaw must not be passed. It criminalizes the

02:09:09.516 --> 02:09:12.916
survival and removes agency from women and gender diverse residents

02:09:13.028 --> 02:09:17.012
while also not having the safety net of available gender specific shelter

02:09:17.076 --> 02:09:20.660
beds. I ask that you do not pass this bylaw and I

02:09:20.700 --> 02:09:23.764
ask that you take this back to the plan to end chronic homelessness

02:09:23.812 --> 02:09:27.438
creators, co-creators. These are people with

02:09:27.494 --> 02:09:31.102
lived and professional expertise who can collectively apply

02:09:31.246 --> 02:09:35.454
a human rights and gender based analysis lens to a more equitable

02:09:35.502 --> 02:09:39.230
and humane path forward in preparation for your transit project.

02:09:39.350 --> 02:09:40.170
Thank you.

02:09:42.710 --> 02:09:46.398
Thank you very much. I see No questions. Thank you.

02:09:46.534 --> 02:09:49.838
The next delegation is Megan Walker from

02:09:49.894 --> 02:09:51.090
Kitchener. Megan.

02:10:05.120 --> 02:10:08.760
welcome. Megan, you have the floor and you have five minutes. Thank you.

02:10:08.800 --> 02:10:12.216
Through you, Madam Chair. Good evening. My name is Meg Walker

02:10:12.248 --> 02:10:15.464
and I'm here for myself on my own behalf. I am a housing advocate

02:10:15.512 --> 02:10:19.122
and organizer here in the region. Also, last year I was evicted for

02:10:19.146 --> 02:10:22.194
a parking lot. So I'm, But I'm one of the lucky few that actually can

02:10:22.202 --> 02:10:25.362
afford new market rent. I am delegating

02:10:25.426 --> 02:10:28.802
today on behalf of our neighbors at 100 Victoria street and against the

02:10:28.826 --> 02:10:32.194
proposed bylaw that will displace them. I am also here to

02:10:32.202 --> 02:10:35.970
explain to you how 100 Victoria and this proposed violation of residents' human

02:10:36.010 --> 02:10:39.602
rights is directly correlated to evictions of tenants and

02:10:39.706 --> 02:10:43.138
affordable housing locally. Sorry, I'm talking too fast

02:10:43.154 --> 02:10:46.862
and reading badly. Affordable housing that is

02:10:46.886 --> 02:10:50.450
at least partially the responsibility of the region As a housing provider.

02:10:50.870 --> 02:10:54.366
I organize with tenants who are undergoing mass bad faith

02:10:54.398 --> 02:10:57.886
or no fault evictions, many of whom cannot afford another place to live

02:10:57.958 --> 02:11:01.870
because market rent is untenable. Displaced residents have

02:11:01.910 --> 02:11:04.782
no place to go. And at the point where they've actually come to me and

02:11:04.806 --> 02:11:07.998
talked about living at the encampment. people end up living

02:11:08.014 --> 02:11:11.400
at 100 Victoria not because it's the best recourse. They live

02:11:11.440 --> 02:11:13.180
there because it's their only recourse.

02:11:14.480 --> 02:11:18.312
If you look realistically at the lack of affordable housing across the region and

02:11:18.336 --> 02:11:21.848
the lack of tenant protections, the fact that we are not building supportive infrastructure

02:11:21.864 --> 02:11:25.224
for tenants, up to a third of our region are tenants.

02:11:25.352 --> 02:11:28.872
Waterloo region is at risk of becoming homeless, A third of those people are

02:11:28.896 --> 02:11:32.952
at risk of becoming homeless, of being a resident in

02:11:32.976 --> 02:11:36.530
an encampment like 100 Victoria. That's about a third of us

02:11:36.650 --> 02:11:39.842
in a form of precarious housing with the potential to be

02:11:39.866 --> 02:11:43.070
unsheltered and without choice as to where they will end up.

02:11:43.690 --> 02:11:47.586
Many tenants are closer to being on the street than they are to owning

02:11:47.618 --> 02:11:51.042
a home, myself included. Not because of their own

02:11:51.066 --> 02:11:54.530
choices, but because of policy choices, including those

02:11:54.570 --> 02:11:58.002
made at the region and its municipalities. I am

02:11:58.026 --> 02:12:02.038
also concerned about this plan to transition 100 Vic residents into

02:12:02.094 --> 02:12:05.430
housing based on what I know, based on what I know about shelter space,

02:12:05.550 --> 02:12:07.930
especially for women and gender diverse folks.

02:12:08.750 --> 02:12:12.886
Where do you plan on finding this housing? Because the housing quoted earlier by

02:12:12.958 --> 02:12:15.250
Mr. Sweeney is not remotely enough.

02:12:16.190 --> 02:12:19.622
And everyone who works in housing in the region, people who work at not for

02:12:19.646 --> 02:12:23.094
Profits, people organize, know there is not enough shelter space or housing

02:12:23.142 --> 02:12:25.370
anywhere to transition anybody.

02:12:26.750 --> 02:12:30.182
Otherwise we wouldn't have these encampments to begin with, If we're being really

02:12:30.206 --> 02:12:34.022
honest with ourselves. A lack of transparency as well as

02:12:34.046 --> 02:12:37.110
my concern around this bylaw about the plans and communicating both

02:12:37.150 --> 02:12:40.614
to the public and housing advocates and to the residents

02:12:40.662 --> 02:12:43.862
themselves who have not been told. it was not clear

02:12:43.886 --> 02:12:47.254
to them what was going on. this indicates to me that there wasn't much of

02:12:47.262 --> 02:12:50.470
a plan for these people after all. And certainly

02:12:50.550 --> 02:12:53.622
the residents themselves will not be given a choice as to where they will end

02:12:53.646 --> 02:12:57.040
up. Much like a tenant being evicted from housing

02:12:57.120 --> 02:12:58.660
because they can't afford rent.

02:13:00.760 --> 02:13:04.080
So no choice as to where they end up living and who with or under

02:13:04.120 --> 02:13:08.192
what conditions, You're only reinforcing the harm and oppression that

02:13:08.216 --> 02:13:11.440
caused them to be unsheltered to begin with. You are punishing these

02:13:11.480 --> 02:13:14.992
people, The 100 Vic neighbors and residents that we support, for

02:13:15.016 --> 02:13:18.384
your own decisions. This is a message that you're sending to

02:13:18.392 --> 02:13:22.026
the residents of 100 Vic, to housing advocates and to supporters

02:13:22.058 --> 02:13:25.386
of unsheltered populations that again, the humanity of unsheltered

02:13:25.418 --> 02:13:28.630
people does not matter. Thank you.

02:13:31.170 --> 02:13:32.350
Thank you, Meg.

02:13:35.410 --> 02:13:38.750
Next delegation is Andrew Reeves from Kitchener.

02:13:43.730 --> 02:13:46.828
Andrew, welcome. You have the floor and you have five minutes.

02:13:46.994 --> 02:13:50.120
Thank you. I am Dr. Andrew Reeves,

02:13:50.200 --> 02:13:54.140
delegating as a volunteer at 100 Vic and community member generally.

02:13:54.560 --> 02:13:57.896
My wife and I are new homeowners in the Victoria Hills part of Kitchener,

02:13:57.928 --> 02:14:01.544
but we've lived in or I've lived in Waterloo region for over a decade

02:14:01.592 --> 02:14:05.100
and she's lived in the city since she was a baby.

02:14:06.160 --> 02:14:09.352
Although financially stable right now, I haven't always been on a

02:14:09.376 --> 02:14:13.154
stable footing here. I almost became homeless back in 2016,

02:14:13.352 --> 02:14:17.570
but the eviction notice thankfully was never filed by the negligent property manager.

02:14:18.070 --> 02:14:21.454
I mention this because I do not see unhoused folks as a separate part

02:14:21.462 --> 02:14:25.022
of our community and hope you don't either. I could have easily been homeless

02:14:25.086 --> 02:14:28.446
and you never know, I could someday be. in this housing market

02:14:28.518 --> 02:14:31.998
and the economy rife with precarity, Most of us working

02:14:32.054 --> 02:14:36.238
people are one disability, renoviction, or misfortune away from being forced onto

02:14:36.254 --> 02:14:40.158
the streets. In fact, many community members and volunteers

02:14:40.254 --> 02:14:43.654
supporting folks at 100 Victoria street have been homeless

02:14:43.702 --> 02:14:45.810
themselves. Some of them very recently.

02:14:47.070 --> 02:14:50.214
Something I've noticed is that the more relatable the struggle to survive on

02:14:50.222 --> 02:14:53.730
the streets is, the more empathy and solidarity there tends to be.

02:14:54.350 --> 02:14:57.766
Folks who live longer term at 100 Victoria St, Or folks

02:14:57.798 --> 02:15:00.902
who find themselves even temporarily homeless, use the

02:15:00.926 --> 02:15:04.742
site as a place of last resort. It's a place to shelter oneself

02:15:04.806 --> 02:15:08.486
stably and legally, as well as to find some connections to community

02:15:08.558 --> 02:15:11.962
resources. These folks are not some mysterious or

02:15:11.986 --> 02:15:15.834
criminal other to manage. They are our community

02:15:15.922 --> 02:15:17.590
members. They are us.

02:15:19.810 --> 02:15:23.242
Touchy aspects aside, I'd like to focus the rest of my delegation

02:15:23.306 --> 02:15:26.714
now on what the region has already been doing at the encampment in relation to

02:15:26.722 --> 02:15:30.590
the bylaw we are now discussing, which has not been passed, yet anyway.

02:15:31.170 --> 02:15:35.450
The 100 Victoria Street Bylaw was announced publicly around

02:15:35.490 --> 02:15:39.128
4pm last Wednesday, April 16. In the week leading

02:15:39.144 --> 02:15:42.552
up to its release, there had been an increase in the number of industrial sized

02:15:42.616 --> 02:15:46.376
rental waste bins, all from Riders Bin Rentals, in concert

02:15:46.408 --> 02:15:50.280
with efforts by the Barber Collins security workers to have residents start

02:15:50.320 --> 02:15:53.800
moving their tents and shelters to the outskirts of the site. The stated

02:15:53.840 --> 02:15:57.064
purpose was to make sure the bin's access was not blocked

02:15:57.192 --> 02:16:00.824
and for fire safety reasons. The irony

02:16:00.872 --> 02:16:04.680
of this is that the fire department had visited the site on multiple occasions during

02:16:04.720 --> 02:16:08.172
the winter to make sure tents stayed reasonably spaced out

02:16:08.276 --> 02:16:11.612
and not crowded into portions of the encampment since that's the best way for

02:16:11.636 --> 02:16:15.292
a tent fire to spread to the other tents. anyways,

02:16:15.356 --> 02:16:18.172
A few hours prior to the bylaw being posted,

02:16:18.316 --> 02:16:22.108
several workers, including a regional worker representing the region showed

02:16:22.124 --> 02:16:25.560
up on site. They initially lied about what they were doing

02:16:26.020 --> 02:16:30.044
on site, saying they were simply leveling ground for moving the porta potties.

02:16:30.172 --> 02:16:33.356
The site was then quickly filled with five industrial sized rental

02:16:33.388 --> 02:16:37.160
waste dumpsters and a mobile lease rental office.

02:16:38.100 --> 02:16:41.644
Not only were residents of 100 Vic not consulted about this,

02:16:41.812 --> 02:16:45.100
through the rushed process, residents and community members on

02:16:45.140 --> 02:16:48.812
site were repeatedly denied information about what was going on, who made

02:16:48.836 --> 02:16:52.332
these decisions and who to talk to about it other than quote

02:16:52.396 --> 02:16:55.468
the region. In the days that followed this,

02:16:55.524 --> 02:16:58.780
Barber Collins Security workers began enforcing the bylaw,

02:16:58.940 --> 02:17:02.332
which of course hasn't yet been passed, As far as I know. we

02:17:02.356 --> 02:17:05.772
have recorded a number of incidents where the security guards

02:17:05.836 --> 02:17:09.116
prevented and worked to prevent people from setting up tents

02:17:09.148 --> 02:17:13.084
at the encampment. When confronted by community members on multiple occasions

02:17:13.132 --> 02:17:16.572
about the fact that the bylaw had yet to be passed, security guards told them

02:17:16.596 --> 02:17:19.920
the bylaw was in effect and they were only following orders.

02:17:20.820 --> 02:17:24.080
After emailing Council on Friday evening about this pattern,

02:17:24.740 --> 02:17:28.428
I emailed Council, Councillor Matthew Rodrigues checked

02:17:28.444 --> 02:17:30.660
in with staff and thank you for that Matthew.

02:17:31.320 --> 02:17:34.832
Apparently no such order had been given by staff and they looked into it to

02:17:34.856 --> 02:17:38.336
make sure this wasn't the case. Afterwards, security stopped enforcing

02:17:38.368 --> 02:17:41.020
the bylaw that they that we are here tonight to discuss.

02:17:42.120 --> 02:17:45.424
From an outside perspective, it really seems many decisions have already been

02:17:45.432 --> 02:17:48.832
made to bypass the Valente Ontario Supreme Court ruling

02:17:48.976 --> 02:17:52.592
and at this bylaw and especially this council meeting are largely. One minute remaining.

02:17:52.656 --> 02:17:56.464
thank you. are largely window dressing, political window dressing to rationalize

02:17:56.512 --> 02:18:00.129
already made decisions in the name of expedience. in case

02:18:00.169 --> 02:18:02.641
members of council were not aware of what was going on, I thought I would

02:18:02.665 --> 02:18:05.389
at least read these events and perspectives into the record.

02:18:06.489 --> 02:18:09.649
Finally, I just want to reiterate the point that many others will make

02:18:09.689 --> 02:18:13.409
tonight. There does not need to be a choice between the moral and charter rights

02:18:13.449 --> 02:18:17.201
of homeless community members and improve public transit. Even if

02:18:17.225 --> 02:18:20.481
I were to accept the premise that there are truly no resources locally to

02:18:20.505 --> 02:18:24.081
house everyone, alternative sites or decriminalized camping on

02:18:24.105 --> 02:18:27.308
public land are all options that can move things forward

02:18:27.444 --> 02:18:31.436
while respecting the human right to shelter oneself safely and securely.

02:18:31.628 --> 02:18:35.580
I hope you all can agree on this and amend or

02:18:35.620 --> 02:18:38.920
reject the bylaw as it is currently written. Thank you all.

02:18:40.420 --> 02:18:43.804
Thank you very much, Andrew. The next delegation is David

02:18:43.852 --> 02:18:47.356
Alton, Social Development Center of Waterloo region. Welcome,

02:18:47.388 --> 02:18:50.560
David. You have the floor and you have five minutes.

02:19:00.349 --> 02:19:04.037
Is it on? Okay. I'm here from the Social Development

02:19:04.093 --> 02:19:07.621
Center and the Lived Expertise Program, a key partner in the plan to

02:19:07.645 --> 02:19:11.461
end chronic homelessness. 100 Victoria's future was identified

02:19:11.525 --> 02:19:14.629
as a priority during the drafting of the plan which

02:19:14.669 --> 02:19:17.909
you approved last year. It was seen in both call to

02:19:17.949 --> 02:19:21.950
action 19 of the live to Expertise prototyping report which called

02:19:21.990 --> 02:19:25.182
on you to update the transit hub plans to ensure the continuation

02:19:25.246 --> 02:19:28.910
of 100 Victoria as a sanctioned encampment until functional zero

02:19:28.950 --> 02:19:32.238
homelessness had been achieved, as well as negotiate with

02:19:32.294 --> 02:19:36.302
Metrolinx and the province to set aside transitional land and funding to

02:19:36.326 --> 02:19:39.290
ensure residents are provided with comparable land and support.

02:19:39.590 --> 02:19:43.406
This was also seen in action 1.2 of the plan document

02:19:43.518 --> 02:19:47.294
which said that the region will implement a housing focused street outreach

02:19:47.342 --> 02:19:50.290
framework and a human rights based approach to encampments.

02:19:50.950 --> 02:19:54.094
We were informed a year ago that the regional staff were exploring a plan to

02:19:54.102 --> 02:19:57.166
remove tent city community to make room for the transit hub.

02:19:57.278 --> 02:20:00.526
At that time, we advised staff of the conditions under the National Protocol

02:20:00.558 --> 02:20:04.174
on Homelessness encampments that would facilitate the transformation of an encampment

02:20:04.222 --> 02:20:07.662
community. Things like consent, transparency and fairness.

02:20:07.806 --> 02:20:11.890
But that conversation did not go further with community partners or encampment residents.

02:20:12.310 --> 02:20:16.014
We didn't hear anything until last Wednesday when we were called to the encampment

02:20:16.062 --> 02:20:19.566
to document the chaos and confusion that was created by the appearance of five dumpsters,

02:20:19.598 --> 02:20:23.066
a portable, and a Bobcat. We went back yesterday

02:20:23.178 --> 02:20:26.986
with members of the Lived Expertise roster to do a community based consultation.

02:20:27.098 --> 02:20:30.762
We interviewed 27 members of 100 Victoria community and asked them

02:20:30.786 --> 02:20:34.362
what they knew, how it impacted them and what they wanted you to know.

02:20:34.546 --> 02:20:38.122
From our conversations, no one could identify receiving information from

02:20:38.146 --> 02:20:41.626
regional staff. Some had heard from other sources or rumors,

02:20:41.738 --> 02:20:44.938
while 13 people had heard nothing and were informed by us

02:20:44.994 --> 02:20:48.822
during the interviews. The actions by regional staff last Wednesday and

02:20:48.846 --> 02:20:52.758
the contents the council report caused a range of emotions. People talked of fear,

02:20:52.854 --> 02:20:56.582
stress, confusion and sadness. While some people were happy for change and

02:20:56.606 --> 02:21:00.326
the prospect of housing, others felt like this was targeted harassment and

02:21:00.398 --> 02:21:03.878
trying to kill the homelessness, homeless people. They spoke of

02:21:03.934 --> 02:21:07.654
this causing an uproar, being inhumane and wrong, feeling pressured

02:21:07.702 --> 02:21:11.030
like a gun to their head and feeling like they were human trash.

02:21:11.190 --> 02:21:14.918
One person said, if you are putting bins full of garbage where people are living,

02:21:15.014 --> 02:21:18.486
how do you think they would feel. another person said, they are at the bottom

02:21:18.518 --> 02:21:22.150
and now you are just taking away the bottom. When it comes to what residents

02:21:22.230 --> 02:21:25.942
want from you, first and foremost they want you to understand that tent city is

02:21:25.966 --> 02:21:29.638
a community and a family. Residents were very concerned

02:21:29.654 --> 02:21:33.734
for the well being of everyone else in this process. A common sentiment

02:21:33.782 --> 02:21:36.854
was it's not right because folks at tent city have given

02:21:36.942 --> 02:21:40.070
so much to folks. They have been there for me and given me a space

02:21:40.110 --> 02:21:43.862
to live and at times that was all I had On the coldest nights in

02:21:43.886 --> 02:21:47.254
death gripping winters. residents are deeply concerned

02:21:47.302 --> 02:21:50.646
about who's being prioritized and who's not and most importantly,

02:21:50.678 --> 02:21:54.646
who's at risk of falling through the cracks in this process. Tent city members

02:21:54.718 --> 02:21:58.470
want housing. Some people are okay with motels and shelters.

02:21:58.550 --> 02:22:01.782
Some people are very much not okay with motels and shelters.

02:22:01.926 --> 02:22:04.646
Key considerations are what supports are available,

02:22:04.798 --> 02:22:08.534
how far are they from key services and how long and stable

02:22:08.662 --> 02:22:12.422
housing would that be, especially for people who are at risk of bans

02:22:12.486 --> 02:22:16.278
or service shut offs. Of key concern was how

02:22:16.334 --> 02:22:20.214
contracted housing services were allowing human trafficking to flourish

02:22:20.262 --> 02:22:23.462
in unsheltered communities. A person explained that there is

02:22:23.486 --> 02:22:27.062
a huge problem with human trafficking in Waterloo region because the

02:22:27.086 --> 02:22:30.838
services are privatized to contractors. I was almost trafficked because

02:22:30.894 --> 02:22:34.374
they were sending me into taxis to random shelters

02:22:34.422 --> 02:22:36.330
with no support or no coverage.

02:22:37.240 --> 02:22:40.784
Tent city members want an alternative location. They have built a

02:22:40.792 --> 02:22:44.416
community over these past two years. They feel like the region is breaking

02:22:44.448 --> 02:22:48.592
a promise to them to provide them with a safe space to be. Many people

02:22:48.616 --> 02:22:52.272
in the community are disabled. They want proximity to the hospital and

02:22:52.296 --> 02:22:56.288
to downtown services. The city makes the homeless people walk

02:22:56.344 --> 02:23:00.100
a mile and a half. to walk that on a cold night is terrible.

02:23:00.920 --> 02:23:04.848
People found these finds insulting given the lack of resources already. David,

02:23:04.864 --> 02:23:08.174
you have one minute remaining. These fines are just to scare us. We're going to

02:23:08.182 --> 02:23:11.678
fight for our freedom. This isn't right. It's degrading. People in the tent city

02:23:11.734 --> 02:23:15.118
community should have a voice. They want advance notice. They want clear explanations

02:23:15.134 --> 02:23:18.254
of what resources they will have access to and when. There are many people who

02:23:18.262 --> 02:23:21.582
are prepared to resist and who are worried that this will become violent because the

02:23:21.606 --> 02:23:25.470
community is deeply traumatized and is dealing with complex mental health. How many

02:23:25.510 --> 02:23:28.878
times can you bully and torture and belittle the most vulnerable population, Was another

02:23:28.934 --> 02:23:32.254
quote. It is very clear from talking to residents that 100 Victoria is

02:23:32.262 --> 02:23:35.508
a vital part of the homelessness ecosystem. We talked to people who

02:23:35.564 --> 02:23:39.316
just arrived from the warming centers because tent city is better in the summer

02:23:39.348 --> 02:23:43.092
than warming shelters. We talked to people from the Schwaben Club. We talked to people

02:23:43.116 --> 02:23:46.084
who were banned from other shelters and were concerned about how long they would be

02:23:46.092 --> 02:23:49.812
able to stay at a motel or another offer. We talked to folks who they

02:23:49.836 --> 02:23:53.508
were already planning on setting up tents in the backyards of houses and businesses.

02:23:53.684 --> 02:23:56.740
To remove this encampment means that all that pressure and

02:23:56.780 --> 02:23:59.680
that flow will go directly to already stressed community members.

02:24:00.230 --> 02:24:03.582
Because of the insights from tent city residents, we are recommending that council votes against

02:24:03.606 --> 02:24:06.958
the staff report and sends it back to the plan to end chronic, the

02:24:07.014 --> 02:24:10.462
plan to end chronic homelessness co-creators community because we

02:24:10.486 --> 02:24:13.662
find it not not in alignment with the plan to end chronic homelessness,

02:24:13.726 --> 02:24:16.414
the national protocol encampments or the wishes of residents.

02:24:16.542 --> 02:24:21.130
Thanks. Thank you, David. The next delegation is

02:24:21.510 --> 02:24:23.170
Jacara Droog.

02:24:28.900 --> 02:24:32.200
Welcome. You have the floor and you have five minutes. Thank you.

02:24:32.500 --> 02:24:36.412
Good evening, councillors. My name is Jacara. I'm a social worker and

02:24:36.436 --> 02:24:39.676
housing advocate and I'm here to speak in firm opposition to the proposed

02:24:39.708 --> 02:24:43.212
bylaw 25. Let's be clear. What the region is

02:24:43.236 --> 02:24:46.284
proposing is not just a bylaw. It's a violation.

02:24:46.412 --> 02:24:50.284
It violates the 2023 Ontario Superior

02:24:50.332 --> 02:24:53.964
Court ruling which found that the region cannot evict encampment

02:24:54.012 --> 02:24:58.268
residents without providing adequate accessible shelter alternatives.

02:24:58.444 --> 02:25:01.932
It violates the charter right to life, liberty and

02:25:01.956 --> 02:25:05.532
security of the person. And it undermines the national housing

02:25:05.596 --> 02:25:09.000
strategy which affirms that housing is a human right In Canada.

02:25:09.300 --> 02:25:13.180
bylaw 25 would forcibly displace residents of the 100

02:25:13.220 --> 02:25:16.860
Victoria street encampment, people with nowhere else to go,

02:25:16.980 --> 02:25:20.156
while threatening them with $5,000 fines for simply

02:25:20.188 --> 02:25:23.292
trying to survive. This is being proposed as

02:25:23.316 --> 02:25:27.276
the Ford government pushes forward with Bill 242, which would criminalize

02:25:27.308 --> 02:25:30.802
people further and limit municipalities' ability to

02:25:30.826 --> 02:25:33.906
protect their residents. Together, these measures leave

02:25:33.938 --> 02:25:37.682
people with no legal place to exist. We know the

02:25:37.706 --> 02:25:41.266
region does not have enough shelter beds. We know many shelters

02:25:41.298 --> 02:25:44.962
are inaccessible, unsafe or traumatizing, especially for

02:25:44.986 --> 02:25:48.790
women, 2SLGBTQ folks and people with disabilities.

02:25:49.290 --> 02:25:53.138
Schwaben is closed. The women's shelter has only 37

02:25:53.194 --> 02:25:56.844
beds. Across the region, fewer than 60 spaces

02:25:56.972 --> 02:25:59.196
serve women and gender diverse people.

02:25:59.348 --> 02:26:02.828
Meanwhile, more than 2,300 people

02:26:02.884 --> 02:26:06.444
are unhoused. This bylaw offers no alternatives,

02:26:06.492 --> 02:26:10.156
only removal and punishment. The language of the bylaw

02:26:10.188 --> 02:26:13.308
is not only inhumane, but punitive and carceral.

02:26:13.484 --> 02:26:17.020
It prohibits storing firewood, moving a tent within the site

02:26:17.060 --> 02:26:21.126
or having multiple tents in one area. These aren't minor restrictions,

02:26:21.238 --> 02:26:25.014
they criminalize basic survival. The $5,000 fine

02:26:25.062 --> 02:26:28.902
proposed is more than someone on Ontario works receives in

02:26:28.926 --> 02:26:32.390
an entire year. To pass this bylaw would not only

02:26:32.430 --> 02:26:36.102
be illegal or would be, Not only would be legal and

02:26:36.126 --> 02:26:39.878
an ethical failure, but it would be a moral one. Even before

02:26:39.934 --> 02:26:43.926
this bylaw is passed, we've seen intimidation and misinformation.

02:26:44.118 --> 02:26:47.782
Security are already telling residents they're in violation of a bylaw that

02:26:47.806 --> 02:26:50.768
doesn't even exist yet. Dumpsters have arrived.

02:26:50.864 --> 02:26:54.624
Residents are being mapped. Surveillance is ramping up, and residents

02:26:54.672 --> 02:26:58.560
are living in constant fear with no information, no transparency,

02:26:58.640 --> 02:27:01.984
and no meaningful communication with the region. I've spent

02:27:02.032 --> 02:27:05.856
time with the residents at 100 Vic. These are real people,

02:27:06.008 --> 02:27:09.344
many of whom have survived sexual violence, domestic abuse,

02:27:09.472 --> 02:27:12.832
myriad forms of trauma, acquired brain injuries, and profound

02:27:12.896 --> 02:27:16.192
systemic failure. Many live with chronic illness,

02:27:16.256 --> 02:27:20.050
mental health conditions or disabilities. For them, this encampment is

02:27:20.090 --> 02:27:23.410
not ideal, but it is safer than the unknown. And right

02:27:23.450 --> 02:27:27.218
now, it is the only option that they have. Meanwhile,

02:27:27.314 --> 02:27:31.202
$400,000 is being spent on motels. A temporary

02:27:31.266 --> 02:27:34.450
solution that expires in 2026. After that,

02:27:34.490 --> 02:27:38.162
what then? Where are these people supposed to go? Let's be

02:27:38.186 --> 02:27:41.362
honest. This bylaw is not about or this bylaw is

02:27:41.386 --> 02:27:45.490
about clearing land. It's about optics. It's not about safety. It's about

02:27:45.530 --> 02:27:49.128
pushing people out of sight Without adequate solutions. this bylaw

02:27:49.144 --> 02:27:53.256
will disproportionately harm those already marginalized, Especially Indigenous

02:27:53.288 --> 02:27:56.936
people who make up 12% of the region's chronically unhoused

02:27:56.968 --> 02:28:01.048
population. It contradicts the region's own plan to end chronic homelessness

02:28:01.144 --> 02:28:03.976
and ignores the wisdom of the people who help shape it.

02:28:04.128 --> 02:28:07.688
I'm urging you, do not vote to remove the encampment at 100

02:28:07.744 --> 02:28:11.144
Victoria. Instead, refer this issue back to the co-creators

02:28:11.192 --> 02:28:14.918
table of the plan to end chronic homelessness, A table that includes

02:28:15.024 --> 02:28:18.442
service providers and people with lived expertise and allow them

02:28:18.466 --> 02:28:22.282
to create an alternative that meets both the region's needs and its obligations to

02:28:22.306 --> 02:28:26.154
Metrolinx. The people at 100 Vic are not expendable.

02:28:26.282 --> 02:28:29.690
Their survival should not be sacrificed in the name of a transit hub

02:28:29.770 --> 02:28:33.274
or political convenience. Choose humanity, not just in words,

02:28:33.322 --> 02:28:36.750
but in action. Reject bylaw. Thank you. Jacara You have one minute remaining.

02:28:39.970 --> 02:28:42.902
Jacara, were you done? Okay,

02:28:42.966 --> 02:28:46.998
thanks. Next delegation is

02:28:47.054 --> 02:28:49.370
Heather Majaury from Kitchener. Heather,

02:28:55.710 --> 02:28:58.982
welcome. You have the floor. And you have five minutes. Thank you. I just

02:28:59.006 --> 02:29:02.374
got to check my phone here because I'm new on technology

02:29:02.462 --> 02:29:05.690
and using my phone instead. Okay, you guys ready?

02:29:12.920 --> 02:29:14.940
There we go. Yeah. There you go.

02:29:15.960 --> 02:29:19.472
My name's Heather Majaury. I'm delegating tonight as a private citizen.

02:29:19.536 --> 02:29:23.088
My partner and I live in Kitchener and we have the privilege of home

02:29:23.144 --> 02:29:26.432
ownership. I'm speaking as a concerned resident of

02:29:26.456 --> 02:29:30.128
our region because I live here. I also have

02:29:30.184 --> 02:29:33.888
lived experience with chronic housing precarity and at times

02:29:33.944 --> 02:29:37.596
hidden homelessness while being a single parent. I became

02:29:37.628 --> 02:29:40.780
a single mother the year Premier Harris began his reign of

02:29:40.820 --> 02:29:44.332
terror targeting single mothers in need of financial

02:29:44.436 --> 02:29:47.760
supports. So I know a bit about scapegoating.

02:29:48.580 --> 02:29:53.036
I'm speaking against the proposed 100 Victoria site specific bylaw

02:29:53.068 --> 02:29:56.440
and I actually question the need for this bylaw at all.

02:29:56.900 --> 02:30:00.600
The current approach is not currently consistent with human rights.

02:30:01.300 --> 02:30:04.940
I tend to support bylaws that are enforceable and

02:30:04.980 --> 02:30:08.742
reasonable. This is neither. It's nothing more than a

02:30:08.766 --> 02:30:12.070
neo vagrancy law being dressed up as a human rights approach,

02:30:12.190 --> 02:30:16.422
which it is not. How many people do you know

02:30:16.606 --> 02:30:20.086
experiencing abject poverty have

02:30:20.158 --> 02:30:24.250
$5,000 in the bank to pay your fines?

02:30:25.790 --> 02:30:29.174
I don't understand how this in any way supports

02:30:29.222 --> 02:30:33.334
recommendation 1.2, page 55 of Appendix

02:30:33.382 --> 02:30:37.480
A of your plan to end chronic homelessness.

02:30:37.980 --> 02:30:41.540
This bylaw simply criminalizes homelessness and increases our

02:30:41.580 --> 02:30:44.996
social propensity towards scapegoating.

02:30:45.188 --> 02:30:48.660
It wastes money on frivolous legal actions while

02:30:48.700 --> 02:30:52.292
encouraging harassment. I see the people in my

02:30:52.316 --> 02:30:56.612
ward who are experiencing chronic homelessness who are living in tents or structures

02:30:56.676 --> 02:30:59.800
made from found materials as my neighbors.

02:31:00.220 --> 02:31:03.924
I support the region funding needed housing for each and every resident of

02:31:03.932 --> 02:31:07.826
this encampment in a timely fashion if the process adheres

02:31:07.858 --> 02:31:11.954
to the goals, principles and values of the Plan to End Chronic Homelessness

02:31:12.082 --> 02:31:16.066
that you adopted last year. This bylaw

02:31:16.098 --> 02:31:19.826
as drafted, is working at cross purposes to the plan

02:31:19.898 --> 02:31:24.110
as adopted. Do you know what scapegoating is?

02:31:24.810 --> 02:31:28.190
For the most part, scapegoating is an unconscious process.

02:31:28.890 --> 02:31:32.870
It occurs in families, but also in larger social systems.

02:31:33.330 --> 02:31:36.650
It often leads to deep and profound injustice when it is

02:31:36.690 --> 02:31:39.990
emboldened, enabled and turned into law.

02:31:40.850 --> 02:31:44.298
We only need to look south of our border right now

02:31:44.354 --> 02:31:48.106
to see how this tactic is used for political gain and

02:31:48.178 --> 02:31:52.150
profit by those motivated by wealth and who claim power.

02:31:52.690 --> 02:31:56.314
And if unchecked, it is extremely dangerous to the protection

02:31:56.362 --> 02:31:59.110
of due process and human rights.

02:32:00.260 --> 02:32:03.788
There is a natural tendency to transfer blame and much

02:32:03.844 --> 02:32:06.880
motivation to do so if profits lay in the balance.

02:32:07.300 --> 02:32:09.484
Scapegoats are all around us.

02:32:09.652 --> 02:32:13.580
Unfortunately, all it takes for someone to stand out just

02:32:13.620 --> 02:32:16.844
a little bit to begin the process

02:32:16.932 --> 02:32:20.652
of scapegoating. Consider this. You are

02:32:20.676 --> 02:32:24.812
creating unnecessary trauma that criminalizes the most vulnerable

02:32:24.876 --> 02:32:28.680
people in this community using a scapegoating tactic through law.

02:32:29.460 --> 02:32:32.940
All of this while homelessness is increasing

02:32:33.020 --> 02:32:36.540
in our region by an average of 28% per year with

02:32:36.580 --> 02:32:39.840
an actual current loss of emergency shelter beds.

02:32:41.300 --> 02:32:44.892
Why do we scapegoat? Scapegoating feels

02:32:44.956 --> 02:32:48.252
good. It provides a moment of peace and

02:32:48.276 --> 02:32:52.044
relief. When we scapegoat, we think we are addressing

02:32:52.092 --> 02:32:55.958
the root of our problems. Somebody else pays

02:32:55.974 --> 02:32:59.622
the price for our sins and our weaknesses.

02:32:59.766 --> 02:33:03.686
Even systemically. imagining

02:33:03.718 --> 02:33:07.610
the residents of 100 Victoria as the sole cause of our current delays. Heather you have one minute 

02:33:07.950 --> 02:33:11.702
remaining. Thank you. Around Improved transit creates a convenient

02:33:11.766 --> 02:33:14.890
communal catharsis through criminalization.

02:33:15.790 --> 02:33:19.126
I can assure you that once you have eliminated one scapegoat,

02:33:19.238 --> 02:33:22.930
you always find another, until you get honest about

02:33:22.970 --> 02:33:25.110
the actual root of your problems.

02:33:26.730 --> 02:33:30.466
I am also someone who had a positive experience being housed and supported

02:33:30.498 --> 02:33:34.470
within the domestic abuse shelter system in my mid-20s.

02:33:34.810 --> 02:33:38.226
I will always be grateful for my time at Hiatus House in Windsor

02:33:38.258 --> 02:33:42.322
where I felt safe while processing my trauma. I felt

02:33:42.386 --> 02:33:45.682
seen, I felt heard and I felt

02:33:45.746 --> 02:33:49.500
protected. Please understand a human rights approach to

02:33:49.540 --> 02:33:52.680
encampments is also a trauma informed approach.

02:33:53.060 --> 02:33:56.700
And further entrenching criminalization into your local law

02:33:56.740 --> 02:34:00.440
enforcement apparatuses of control is not

02:34:00.980 --> 02:34:04.796
in any way compatible with a trauma informed

02:34:04.828 --> 02:34:08.620
approach to chronic homelessness. It certainly is no way

02:34:08.660 --> 02:34:10.760
to reach functional zero.

02:34:11.540 --> 02:34:15.622
Thank you. Thank you Heather. Next delegation

02:34:15.686 --> 02:34:18.370
is Laura Pin, Wilfrid Laurier University.

02:34:26.590 --> 02:34:29.750
I'm joining virtually. Am I able to start now or should

02:34:29.790 --> 02:34:33.062
I wait? No, you are. Thank you. I'll stop searching for you in the

02:34:33.086 --> 02:34:36.410
room and you go right ahead. You have the floor and you have five minutes.

02:34:36.830 --> 02:34:40.454
Thank you. Thank you Chair and councillors and apologies

02:34:40.502 --> 02:34:43.734
for not being there in person as I'm dealing with a health issue at

02:34:43.742 --> 02:34:46.946
the moment. Although I do also support Councillor

02:34:46.978 --> 02:34:50.866
Wolf's motion on Consumption and Treatment Services, I'm delegating today

02:34:50.938 --> 02:34:54.594
to encourage you to reject the proposal for site specific

02:34:54.642 --> 02:34:58.082
bylaw at 100 Victoria. I'm delegating

02:34:58.146 --> 02:35:01.922
today as an Assistant professor and researcher at Wilfrid Laurier

02:35:01.986 --> 02:35:05.830
University. Not on behalf of the university, but through my expertise

02:35:06.170 --> 02:35:09.586
in this role. I'm currently leading a multi year federally

02:35:09.618 --> 02:35:12.934
funded research project on municipal policy responses

02:35:12.982 --> 02:35:16.614
to encampments through a human rights lens. Some folks I think that

02:35:16.622 --> 02:35:19.330
are likely in the gallery or watching are part of that project.

02:35:19.790 --> 02:35:23.430
I'm also delegating as a member since the beginning of the

02:35:23.470 --> 02:35:26.742
co-creators table of the Plan to End chronic homelessness or

02:35:26.766 --> 02:35:30.326
PECH, which is a group of over 100 community organizations

02:35:30.358 --> 02:35:34.150
and individuals representing virtually all facets of the

02:35:34.190 --> 02:35:36.090
homelessness response locally.

02:35:38.440 --> 02:35:41.504
I strongly believe in collaborative work to solve problems in a

02:35:41.512 --> 02:35:46.112
fair and just manner and I understand the importance of moving forward with the KCTH

02:35:46.176 --> 02:35:49.824
work. However, the process by which this bylaw has been developed,

02:35:49.952 --> 02:35:53.488
as well as the content of the bylaw I find deeply concerning.

02:35:53.664 --> 02:35:58.100
I'm worried that this approach to move forward at 100 Victoria will be ineffective.

02:35:59.240 --> 02:36:03.056
The goal of having a vacant space by December, I'm also concerned

02:36:03.088 --> 02:36:06.580
that it undermines the trust that has been built with community partners.

02:36:06.970 --> 02:36:10.402
I also find it inconsistent, as several delegates have

02:36:10.426 --> 02:36:13.906
mentioned, with the principles of the Plan to End Chronic Homelessness

02:36:13.938 --> 02:36:17.602
or PECH, passed by Council last spring. And to

02:36:17.626 --> 02:36:21.186
be honest, it kind of boggles my mind that the PECH table was not consulted

02:36:21.218 --> 02:36:25.026
at all, which feels like a waste of the tremendous work that has happened

02:36:25.058 --> 02:36:28.722
to build up a collaborative policy infrastructure there, as well

02:36:28.746 --> 02:36:31.970
as the time and energy that service providers and lived experts have put

02:36:32.010 --> 02:36:34.790
into regularly engaging through that mechanism.

02:36:36.090 --> 02:36:39.950
With the time left, I want to outline a couple points of specific concern.

02:36:40.810 --> 02:36:44.850
First, this bylaw was developed in secret without any input from community members

02:36:44.890 --> 02:36:47.314
or organizations. Most importantly,

02:36:47.362 --> 02:36:51.026
no one at 100 Vic or anyone who regularly

02:36:51.138 --> 02:36:54.178
spends time at 100 Vic was consulted.

02:36:54.354 --> 02:36:58.146
People at 100 Vic were informed of the bylaw through the sudden

02:36:58.178 --> 02:37:02.050
presence of enhanced policing, Bobcats, dumpsters with no

02:37:02.090 --> 02:37:05.304
forewarning, which is neither a trauma informed

02:37:05.352 --> 02:37:09.288
approach nor conducive to building pathways towards

02:37:09.384 --> 02:37:12.792
housing with individuals. Building on

02:37:12.816 --> 02:37:16.584
David Alton's comments, I also spent some time at 100 Victoria yesterday

02:37:16.632 --> 02:37:19.736
evening speaking with six individuals experiencing homelessness

02:37:19.768 --> 02:37:23.864
who spend time there directly and nobody indicated,

02:37:23.912 --> 02:37:26.632
I asked them all, you know, has anyone from the region spoken with you about

02:37:26.656 --> 02:37:29.950
the bylaw, about the changes? And they said no.

02:37:30.330 --> 02:37:34.386
this is not meaningful engagement. It's not consistent with the emphasis on engagement

02:37:34.418 --> 02:37:38.050
in the PECH or human rights literature more broadly, or not

02:37:38.090 --> 02:37:41.522
even I would suggest, you know, solid policymaking in any aspect of

02:37:41.546 --> 02:37:45.410
policy. Second, while the

02:37:45.450 --> 02:37:48.962
consideration given to housing services within the staff report is

02:37:48.986 --> 02:37:52.626
encouraging, we know that there are not enough supportive housing spaces

02:37:52.658 --> 02:37:56.438
and subsidies available to house people excluding experiencing homelessness,

02:37:56.614 --> 02:37:59.250
and there will not be enough by the end of the year.

02:37:59.790 --> 02:38:03.686
Given what we know about the most recent point in time count where 2,300

02:38:03.758 --> 02:38:07.190
people were documented as experiencing homelessness in a context of

02:38:07.230 --> 02:38:10.358
fewer than 500 emergency shelter e=bed spaces locally.

02:38:10.454 --> 02:38:13.974
And those are the most recent numbers I have from staff. I'm concerned that if

02:38:13.982 --> 02:38:17.958
this bylaw is passed it will lead to a divisive, protracted and expensive

02:38:18.054 --> 02:38:21.972
legal battle in terms of the Valente ruling,

02:38:22.126 --> 02:38:26.024
because if anything, the context has worsened since that ruling was made which found that

02:38:26.032 --> 02:38:29.944
there were not adequate spaces. I can

02:38:29.952 --> 02:38:33.432
see the proposal to use motels as a stop gap

02:38:33.576 --> 02:38:37.016
in the absence of direct consultation with residents and service providers.

02:38:37.048 --> 02:38:40.264
I also cannot support this option because we know the barriers.

02:38:40.312 --> 02:38:43.580
And I can see I have one minute left. Yeah,

02:38:44.160 --> 02:38:47.512
significant barriers to accessing motels. And not the least

02:38:47.536 --> 02:38:51.870
of the problem with these is that they're temporary and not permanent housing solutions.

02:38:52.610 --> 02:38:55.706
Third, as other delegates have mentioned,

02:38:55.738 --> 02:38:59.674
the bylaw will criminalize survival activities of individuals at 100 Victoria

02:38:59.722 --> 02:39:02.670
as well as individuals providing survival assistance.

02:39:03.250 --> 02:39:06.826
It's a bit out of touch with how people navigate being housed.

02:39:07.018 --> 02:39:10.698
It prohibits anyone who was not present on April 16 from residing

02:39:10.714 --> 02:39:14.282
at 100 Victoria, a condition which is restrictive and in practice,

02:39:14.346 --> 02:39:18.276
impossible to enforce, I would argue. it also proposes fines

02:39:18.308 --> 02:39:21.972
of up to $5,000 for

02:39:21.996 --> 02:39:25.572
a variety of activities. And really,

02:39:25.596 --> 02:39:29.476
I've been grounding my response in human rights language because human rights language

02:39:29.508 --> 02:39:32.548
is the language of the plan to end chronic homelessness which was passed by this

02:39:32.604 --> 02:39:36.340
group. There's two good things about the staff report. Lest you think I'm just,

02:39:36.460 --> 02:39:39.604
you know, full of negativity, I think if there's a reasonable time, if I

02:39:39.612 --> 02:39:42.862
could have 10 seconds to finish up, I would appreciate that. Thank you.

02:39:42.966 --> 02:39:46.814
I think there's a reasonable timeline of 7 months to meet both the residents

02:39:46.862 --> 02:39:50.318
of 100 Vic as well as the region's needs. And I think there's resources.

02:39:50.494 --> 02:39:54.046
What I would like to see council do is harness those positives

02:39:54.078 --> 02:39:57.614
and direct staff to work with the plan to end chronic homelessness Co-creators

02:39:57.662 --> 02:40:01.582
table to create a realistic plan that can work with this timeframe that

02:40:01.606 --> 02:40:05.294
is consistent with the principles of PECH and will not harm any further

02:40:05.382 --> 02:40:08.502
marginalized folks. thank you for your time tonight. Thank you,

02:40:08.526 --> 02:40:12.278
Laura. Next delegation is

02:40:12.334 --> 02:40:14.490
John-Lee Bannister from Waterloo.

02:40:21.310 --> 02:40:24.370
You get to the podium and you get five minutes John.

02:40:27.310 --> 02:40:30.050
Okay, we're on.

02:40:30.910 --> 02:40:34.166
Good evening, neighbors, councillors and trusted friends. Before I begin,

02:40:34.198 --> 02:40:37.618
I just want to say happy birthday to Nick. But for those who don't

02:40:37.634 --> 02:40:40.578
know me, my name is John. I am the first vice president of the Waterloo

02:40:40.594 --> 02:40:44.034
Regional Labor Council. And I come before you today to speak to a

02:40:44.042 --> 02:40:46.914
demand from those whose lives are more laborious than most,

02:40:47.082 --> 02:40:50.802
whose lives are criminalized and demeaned, looked down upon

02:40:50.866 --> 02:40:54.546
and ridiculed. But as a neighbor to these people

02:40:54.618 --> 02:40:58.290
in this region, I must stand with them. as people who were

02:40:58.330 --> 02:41:02.002
once in the trades. For the people who without work,

02:41:02.106 --> 02:41:05.150
continue to work and put their lives at risk to do so.

02:41:05.950 --> 02:41:09.126
I ask that all who are able to stand with me for A moment

02:41:09.158 --> 02:41:13.142
of silence and mourning for all those who have been lost without shelter and

02:41:13.166 --> 02:41:14.930
those we lose even now.

02:41:39.560 --> 02:41:46.512
Thank you. for

02:41:46.536 --> 02:41:49.712
the lives at stake in this community. It's my privilege to share with all of

02:41:49.736 --> 02:41:52.816
you that the labor community, as I understand it, will support

02:41:52.888 --> 02:41:55.940
the endeavors of this community and its grassroots partners.

02:41:56.850 --> 02:42:00.266
I'll do this because in the House of Labor, we struggle for those whose labor

02:42:00.298 --> 02:42:03.850
goes unnoticed, whose struggles are forgotten, and the

02:42:03.890 --> 02:42:07.482
details of the lives of some people are cheapened by decisions like

02:42:07.506 --> 02:42:11.306
this council is proposing. Let's not quibble.

02:42:11.498 --> 02:42:15.194
The decisions to move in this direction do not come from kindnesses,

02:42:15.322 --> 02:42:18.230
from the outpouring of love to these people.

02:42:18.930 --> 02:42:20.190
It is out of greed.

02:42:22.540 --> 02:42:26.084
Council, whom I still regard in manners lowly,

02:42:26.212 --> 02:42:29.480
make my day, Prove me wrong.

02:42:30.380 --> 02:42:33.764
Handle this matter like your children's lives depend

02:42:33.812 --> 02:42:37.400
on it, like your family is inside those tents.

02:42:38.460 --> 02:42:42.532
Should something grievous occur in the face of this bylaw, it will be your greatest

02:42:42.596 --> 02:42:46.500
and most ruinous action. Maybe for

02:42:46.540 --> 02:42:50.450
individuals of this council, principles are worth setting aside.

02:42:51.110 --> 02:42:55.630
But perhaps you can grow a spine, your own spine,

02:42:55.790 --> 02:42:59.358
and demand that the people pushing for this bylaw change, who see these

02:42:59.414 --> 02:43:02.490
people's lives as red tape, confront the cost.

02:43:02.950 --> 02:43:06.526
Make them pay for the price of housing, these people that they have shown

02:43:06.558 --> 02:43:10.450
to clearly despise. Or we can simplify.

02:43:11.510 --> 02:43:13.730
and decriminalize public camping.

02:43:14.590 --> 02:43:18.330
However, I leave the council with this sentiment.

02:43:18.750 --> 02:43:22.310
In the House of Labor and in this community, we will take

02:43:22.350 --> 02:43:26.022
care of our own. We understand

02:43:26.126 --> 02:43:29.990
that more than this council ever could, that we keep

02:43:30.030 --> 02:43:34.006
us safe. We cannot

02:43:34.038 --> 02:43:37.686
keep safe those who show clearly who is

02:43:37.838 --> 02:43:39.530
or is not secure.

02:43:41.210 --> 02:43:44.706
Let the house you go to, the home you go to tonight

02:43:44.738 --> 02:43:46.150
be your moment of gratitude.

02:43:50.970 --> 02:43:54.370
Next delegation is Héline Chow from

02:43:54.410 --> 02:43:55.350
Waterloo.

02:43:57.930 --> 02:44:01.522
Is it Héline? Sorry. Welcome.

02:44:01.586 --> 02:44:05.522
You have the podium and have five minutes. Thank you. My name is Dr.

02:44:05.586 --> 02:44:08.642
Héline Chow, and I'm a candidate in this federal election. But today I

02:44:08.666 --> 02:44:12.534
come to to you as a resident of Waterloo. I've been meeting with Waterloo residents

02:44:12.582 --> 02:44:16.214
for the past four weeks to understand the issues they care about most. consistently,

02:44:16.262 --> 02:44:19.574
The rising cost of living, lack of affordable housing

02:44:19.702 --> 02:44:23.350
have been among the top issues on people's minds. This is no surprise.

02:44:23.430 --> 02:44:27.382
Since the pandemic, we've been living through highly unstable economic times, and the

02:44:27.406 --> 02:44:31.558
coming tariffs from the US Are only continuing this trend. In KW,

02:44:31.654 --> 02:44:34.870
we see the impacts of this instability through the rising demand for food

02:44:34.910 --> 02:44:38.926
banks and the increased rates of homelessness in the region. People in Waterloo

02:44:38.958 --> 02:44:42.670
are being stretched thin and pushed their financial limits. In this

02:44:42.710 --> 02:44:46.174
context, how can we be pushing For a bylaw that is focused on displacing our

02:44:46.182 --> 02:44:49.886
most vulnerable population. Two years ago, the region of Waterloo

02:44:49.918 --> 02:44:53.774
tried to obtain the right to evict the unhoused community at 100 Victoria Street.

02:44:53.942 --> 02:44:57.502
Rightfully, this eviction attempt was ruled illegal and in violation of the

02:44:57.526 --> 02:45:00.814
charter of rights and freedoms. So as long as the number of homeless

02:45:00.862 --> 02:45:04.730
persons exceeds the number of available accessible shelter beds in the region,

02:45:05.230 --> 02:45:08.742
now the region is once again trying to evict these residents, While the amount of

02:45:08.766 --> 02:45:12.598
resources to support the unhoused community remains woefully insufficient.

02:45:12.774 --> 02:45:16.854
In December 2024, the number of shelter beds in the region was quoted at

02:45:16.942 --> 02:45:20.358
roughly 550 beds, while a count of unhoused persons

02:45:20.374 --> 02:45:23.894
in the region just two months earlier found there were over 2,300 people that

02:45:23.902 --> 02:45:27.142
are unhoused. Though a judge can be the only one

02:45:27.166 --> 02:45:30.614
that rules on the legality of the proposed bylaw, it is clear to me that

02:45:30.622 --> 02:45:34.282
the number of unhoused people far exceeds the number of shelter beds. In fact,

02:45:34.306 --> 02:45:37.978
it is more than quadruple the number of beds. A huge deficit

02:45:37.994 --> 02:45:41.066
of shelter beds not only calls into question the legality of the bylaw,

02:45:41.098 --> 02:45:44.986
but indicates some of the negative consequences of it, considering there aren't

02:45:45.018 --> 02:45:48.490
nearly enough beds for the number of unhoused people in the region. If the 100

02:45:48.530 --> 02:45:52.458
Victoria encampment is cleared, where will these residents go? The plan

02:45:52.514 --> 02:45:56.122
suggests temporary motels and some supportive housing, but without the

02:45:56.146 --> 02:45:59.890
full budget required to support the unhoused community, the residents

02:45:59.970 --> 02:46:03.058
will be left high and dry when the motel funding runs out.

02:46:03.194 --> 02:46:06.626
The number of residents now is maybe 30 to 35,

02:46:06.778 --> 02:46:10.562
but these numbers tend to grow in the summer months to 70 or 90,

02:46:10.746 --> 02:46:13.986
making this funding proposal completely inadequate since it's meant

02:46:14.018 --> 02:46:17.170
to only cover the current residents and forbids any new tents or new people

02:46:17.210 --> 02:46:20.498
from moving in. The intent behind this bylaw

02:46:20.514 --> 02:46:24.162
is clear when no consultation was done with the actual people who

02:46:24.186 --> 02:46:28.050
are impacted by it. When dumpsters and equipment are brought on site without

02:46:28.090 --> 02:46:32.550
any warning as a threat. we cannot continue to criminalize poverty.

02:46:32.710 --> 02:46:37.130
Charging $5,000 fines to people who have no other options is completely unacceptable.

02:46:37.630 --> 02:46:41.382
While supports are put in place, People need a place to live where they

02:46:41.406 --> 02:46:44.966
are not under threat of all of their belongings being taken from them, over

02:46:45.038 --> 02:46:48.054
constant eviction and over policing. This is

02:46:48.062 --> 02:46:51.462
why I'm speaking you today to stand with people that are demanding that the

02:46:51.486 --> 02:46:54.940
region decriminalize public camping on regional land.

02:46:55.110 --> 02:46:58.912
If people can camp in other locations without the threat of eviction, there would be

02:46:58.936 --> 02:47:01.520
no need for them to use the Current site. There is no need to make

02:47:01.560 --> 02:47:04.220
this a transit site or their housing issue.

02:47:04.760 --> 02:47:08.112
Please listen to the people who are impacted by this decision, to the

02:47:08.136 --> 02:47:11.776
experts, and make sure you act in a manner that respects their fundamental

02:47:11.808 --> 02:47:13.420
rights and freedoms. Thank you.

02:47:14.920 --> 02:47:18.240
Thank you, Héline. The next delegation is Lili

02:47:18.320 --> 02:47:20.740
Berescu from Waterloo.

02:47:32.650 --> 02:47:35.670
Welcome. Lili, you have the floor and you have five minutes.

02:47:41.690 --> 02:47:45.490
hello. Instead of turning up the brightness, I turned up my

02:47:45.530 --> 02:47:47.320
volumes. So let me change that.

02:47:48.900 --> 02:47:52.236
And I thought I was not gonna cry,

02:47:52.268 --> 02:47:55.804
but who am I kidding? I'm gonna cry. But please don't let my tears dilute

02:47:55.852 --> 02:47:58.600
the importance of this.

02:47:59.140 --> 02:48:02.840
My name is Lili. I was born and raised in Waterloo region

02:48:03.220 --> 02:48:06.684
and I said I still live in Waterloo region. This has

02:48:06.692 --> 02:48:10.600
been my home all my life and I care about my community a lot.

02:48:11.140 --> 02:48:14.520
This is my first time speaking at a city council meeting.

02:48:14.900 --> 02:48:18.602
And despite having social anxiety, as you can tell, I try my

02:48:18.626 --> 02:48:22.490
best to speak up when it matters and the situation matters more than words can

02:48:22.530 --> 02:48:25.994
express. At the previous

02:48:26.082 --> 02:48:30.202
meeting I attended, there was a presentation on public health inspections

02:48:30.266 --> 02:48:33.450
for food safety, noting that they are not able to reach all

02:48:33.490 --> 02:48:37.030
food areas and therefore needing to prioritize higher risk.

02:48:37.330 --> 02:48:41.114
Well, what about the safety of people, our community members,

02:48:41.282 --> 02:48:44.914
living, breathing human beings? What about prioritizing

02:48:44.962 --> 02:48:48.850
those at higher risk? What does that look like, you might

02:48:48.890 --> 02:48:52.402
ask? It's having safe spaces for people to use drugs

02:48:52.546 --> 02:48:55.150
so people don't die before they can reach services.

02:48:55.930 --> 02:48:59.282
It was noted in the previous meeting by a council member that there are

02:48:59.306 --> 02:49:02.710
literally thousands of people who use drugs in our region alone.

02:49:03.770 --> 02:49:07.362
12 beds in an abstinence based rehab is not the act of

02:49:07.386 --> 02:49:10.440
prioritizing. Safe consumptions are.

02:49:10.740 --> 02:49:14.200
And let me remind you that ours closed on March 31.

02:49:14.820 --> 02:49:18.140
And if you aren't already aware, abstinence based programs have

02:49:18.180 --> 02:49:21.612
actually shown to increase mortality, risk of death,

02:49:21.796 --> 02:49:25.480
negating some of the benefits intended for this 12 bed program.

02:49:25.940 --> 02:49:29.420
I ask our city council, please do not ignore us.

02:49:29.540 --> 02:49:33.548
Please do not silence us. There were many folks that shared

02:49:33.724 --> 02:49:37.000
very valuable messages at the last meeting as well.

02:49:37.790 --> 02:49:41.046
Utilize the resources in your community. When the motion

02:49:41.078 --> 02:49:45.382
was delayed last meeting due to not having enough information for

02:49:45.406 --> 02:49:48.730
the council to make a decision on this motion.

02:49:49.630 --> 02:49:52.886
Members who were sitting here were practically jumping

02:49:52.918 --> 02:49:55.010
out of their seats to provide said information.

02:49:56.670 --> 02:49:57.530
Sorry.

02:49:59.870 --> 02:50:03.362
All this to say amplify the voices you are privileged to

02:50:03.406 --> 02:50:06.826
to listen to. This is your civic duty,

02:50:07.018 --> 02:50:09.910
not to pass on the interpretation of what you hear.

02:50:11.250 --> 02:50:14.666
The motion asks that you write a letter asking our provincial government

02:50:14.738 --> 02:50:18.390
to comply with the law. The judgment of the superior court.

02:50:19.330 --> 02:50:22.986
Any inclusion of information regarding safe consumption

02:50:23.018 --> 02:50:27.130
sites is merely objective and factual, not of opinion

02:50:27.290 --> 02:50:31.318
as there are literally decades of evidence and research proving the very thing

02:50:31.374 --> 02:50:34.918
our provincial government is not only actively denying but also

02:50:34.974 --> 02:50:38.678
lying about. And that is that safe consumption sites save lives

02:50:38.734 --> 02:50:42.150
and lead to safer communities as we have

02:50:42.190 --> 02:50:45.570
seen over these years as living proof in our very own community.

02:50:47.070 --> 02:50:51.030
And I was going to end this there, but while

02:50:51.070 --> 02:50:54.486
walking to this community I found out someone I knew passed

02:50:54.518 --> 02:50:57.620
away from overdose. His name was Gregory.

02:50:59.000 --> 02:51:02.432
On March 31, not only did we have our safe consumption

02:51:02.496 --> 02:51:06.380
site closed, we also had safer supply close and

02:51:07.080 --> 02:51:10.420
the King street shelter which had 100 beds.

02:51:10.920 --> 02:51:14.064
And I do remember over the winter hearing the news that

02:51:14.152 --> 02:51:17.936
someone that I knew there also passed away on the very steps of that shelter.

02:51:18.048 --> 02:51:21.904
So just echoing what others have said is that we do not have sufficient

02:51:21.952 --> 02:51:25.576
resources for folks. And I just want to leave it with

02:51:25.728 --> 02:51:29.860
how many times will we continue to displace people and remove services?

02:51:30.320 --> 02:51:33.560
How many more people need to die in order for action

02:51:33.680 --> 02:51:34.500
to happen?

02:51:36.880 --> 02:51:39.940
Thank you Lili. Actually Lili, stay at the podium please.

02:51:40.480 --> 02:51:44.072
Councillor Wolf has a question. through you

02:51:44.096 --> 02:51:47.576
Madam Chair, just really a comment. Thank you very much for coming in and

02:51:47.648 --> 02:51:50.320
having the courage to speak you. Thank you.

02:51:51.100 --> 02:51:52.200
Thank you Lili.

02:51:54.140 --> 02:51:57.560
The next delegation is Ashley Schuitema

02:51:59.180 --> 02:52:02.900
from Waterloo Regional Community Legal Services. Welcome Ashley,

02:52:02.980 --> 02:52:06.276
you have the floor and you have five minutes. Good evening

02:52:06.308 --> 02:52:09.860
everyone. I'm a lawyer and executive director at Waterloo Region Community

02:52:09.900 --> 02:52:13.684
Legal Services. I was also co-counsel for the Victoria street encampment

02:52:13.732 --> 02:52:17.236
litigation that began began in 2022. My comments

02:52:17.308 --> 02:52:21.012
tonight are without prejudice to any potential litigation that may come.

02:52:21.116 --> 02:52:24.212
And I would like to say just for one second that I do also support

02:52:24.316 --> 02:52:26.520
Councillor Wolf's motion around the CTS.

02:52:27.500 --> 02:52:31.060
I have to express my deep concern with the procedure the region is using

02:52:31.100 --> 02:52:34.388
to pass this bylaw and to skirt around the existing court

02:52:34.444 --> 02:52:38.020
order for this property. This site has an existing

02:52:38.100 --> 02:52:42.056
binding and in force court order that establishes constitutional

02:52:42.088 --> 02:52:45.320
violations related to evictions. Passing a new

02:52:45.360 --> 02:52:49.112
bylaw instead of following the procedure set out by

02:52:49.136 --> 02:52:52.088
the court in the existing order is improper.

02:52:52.264 --> 02:52:55.976
It has the badges commonly recognized by courts as a bylaw

02:52:56.008 --> 02:52:59.160
being passed in bad faith and I urge you not to pass

02:52:59.200 --> 02:53:02.408
this bylaw tonight. Justice Valente ordered

02:53:02.424 --> 02:53:06.392
that the Region could apply to him to terminate his previous declaration

02:53:06.536 --> 02:53:10.550
if it can satisfy the court that the bylaw no longer violates the the charter.

02:53:10.970 --> 02:53:14.594
The Region has the onus of returning to court and satisfying the

02:53:14.602 --> 02:53:18.098
court with a proper evidentiary record under the Code of Use

02:53:18.154 --> 02:53:21.490
bylaw that the circumstances have changed such

02:53:21.530 --> 02:53:24.870
that an eviction would no longer constitute a charter violation.

02:53:25.530 --> 02:53:29.778
This is not a typical situation where a municipality can just pass a bylaw.

02:53:29.954 --> 02:53:33.666
Trying to pass this bylaw without returning to court first could be viewed

02:53:33.698 --> 02:53:37.534
by a court again as acting in bad faith. This has all the indicia of

02:53:37.542 --> 02:53:41.726
a bylaw being enacted in bad faith, including improper motives,

02:53:41.838 --> 02:53:45.490
questionable timing, and keeping affected parties in the dark.

02:53:45.830 --> 02:53:48.942
Further, any evictions that take place prior to a

02:53:48.966 --> 02:53:52.782
new decision from the court could have the potential for charter damages

02:53:52.846 --> 02:53:56.846
being ordered against the region. It's our position that every person turned

02:53:56.878 --> 02:54:00.014
away from this property or told by security that they cannot set

02:54:00.022 --> 02:54:04.140
up a tent there because of this new bylaw is akin to an eviction

02:54:04.220 --> 02:54:06.960
and is putting the region at risk of charter damages.

02:54:07.780 --> 02:54:10.924
Now, all of that being said, about a year ago at a

02:54:10.932 --> 02:54:15.180
community meeting with Commissioner Peter Sweeney, I suggested mediation

02:54:15.260 --> 02:54:18.760
on this issue and I'm here now again to suggest this to council.

02:54:19.060 --> 02:54:22.588
We have the tools we need to resolve this outside of

02:54:22.644 --> 02:54:27.020
court in a way that is human rights and charter compliant.

02:54:27.180 --> 02:54:31.164
The region has the opportunity to be a true leader among municipalities

02:54:31.292 --> 02:54:35.120
and to do the right thing. And passing this bylaw is not the answer.

02:54:35.620 --> 02:54:39.228
Litigation is a blunt tool for settling disputes.

02:54:39.404 --> 02:54:41.680
It should be used as a last resort.

02:54:42.180 --> 02:54:45.372
Litigation is unpredictable, as those of you who are around the

02:54:45.396 --> 02:54:49.372
last round know that once you enter into litigation, you lose control.

02:54:49.556 --> 02:54:53.324
You no longer have control over the process, the outcome,

02:54:53.452 --> 02:54:56.732
the timeline or the costs, all of which

02:54:56.756 --> 02:54:58.990
are important factors to the region.

02:54:59.450 --> 02:55:03.350
Litigation has far reaching implications that no one can predict.

02:55:03.690 --> 02:55:07.362
Reputationally, litigation is risky for the region.

02:55:07.546 --> 02:55:11.442
The region will once again be seen as spending excessive resources to

02:55:11.466 --> 02:55:14.834
take homeless people, the most vulnerable people in our community,

02:55:14.922 --> 02:55:18.642
to court. The region is also risking the trust that they

02:55:18.666 --> 02:55:21.970
have worked very hard to rebuild in the community since

02:55:22.010 --> 02:55:25.612
the last round of litigation. And as you've heard from other people here that

02:55:25.636 --> 02:55:29.100
are part of the plan to end chronic homelessness, there is a serious risk of

02:55:29.140 --> 02:55:33.292
fracturing those relationships that have been built. Instead of spending

02:55:33.356 --> 02:55:36.556
hundreds of thousands of dollars taking encampment residents to court,

02:55:36.708 --> 02:55:41.004
you could approve an encampment in another similarly situated property

02:55:41.132 --> 02:55:44.396
and provide the services and protections there that currently exist

02:55:44.428 --> 02:55:47.692
at 100 Vic. Unfortunately, given the state of

02:55:47.716 --> 02:55:51.606
our housing crisis, encampments will continue to exist. regardless

02:55:51.638 --> 02:55:55.190
of what the province thinks, We are not going to enforce our way

02:55:55.230 --> 02:55:58.502
out of this crisis. We are regularly asked by

02:55:58.526 --> 02:56:01.702
people facing eviction if we can suggest somewhere they can go to set up a

02:56:01.726 --> 02:56:04.726
tent. Even if 100 Vic is cleared,

02:56:04.838 --> 02:56:09.062
another encampment will emerge. Wouldn't you rather have control

02:56:09.166 --> 02:56:12.290
over where it emerges? Ashley you have one minute remaining. Thank you.

02:56:12.910 --> 02:56:16.710
Wouldn't you rather proactively take care of issues like pests

02:56:16.790 --> 02:56:20.422
and garbage that will emerge by arranging these services in

02:56:20.446 --> 02:56:24.038
advance to mitigate these issues? And frankly,

02:56:24.214 --> 02:56:28.390
this will continue regardless of Ford's encampment eviction legislation,

02:56:28.470 --> 02:56:32.294
because people have nowhere to go. Sanctioned encampments

02:56:32.342 --> 02:56:36.038
are part of the housing solution continuum. As much as people don't

02:56:36.054 --> 02:56:39.370
want to hear it or see it or deal with it, it is a reality.

02:56:39.870 --> 02:56:43.662
Additionally, as a small community legal clinic, litigation will

02:56:43.686 --> 02:56:47.454
require us to use resources that we would otherwise use to represent people at the

02:56:47.462 --> 02:56:51.006
landlord and tenant board fighting eviction. This will undoubtedly

02:56:51.038 --> 02:56:54.382
lead to more inflow into homelessness. This is

02:56:54.406 --> 02:56:58.690
a direct cost that you do not account for in your financial implications assessment.

02:57:00.550 --> 02:57:04.318
There is a way around litigation and it's rejecting this bylaw.

02:57:04.414 --> 02:57:07.694
It's offering suitable alternative sanctioned encampment space for the

02:57:07.702 --> 02:57:11.022
people living at 100 Vic, and it's sending it back to the PECH co-creators

02:57:11.046 --> 02:57:14.916
to move this forward at Waterloo Region Community

02:57:14.988 --> 02:57:17.956
Legal Services. I'm almost done. We're reasonable people.

02:57:18.108 --> 02:57:21.604
We hope the region can be reasonable also. We would much rather

02:57:21.652 --> 02:57:24.772
be your allies and advocate together for the calls that are

02:57:24.796 --> 02:57:28.212
set out in the AMO report to actually solve this crisis than

02:57:28.236 --> 02:57:31.924
be adversaries. Thank you, Ashley.

02:57:31.972 --> 02:57:35.412
I have no questions. That's great. The next speaker is Jason

02:57:35.476 --> 02:57:37.240
Paul from Kitchener. Jason?

02:57:44.070 --> 02:57:45.850
is Jason not with us?

02:57:47.430 --> 02:57:50.974
Okay. The next delegation is Julian Ichim from

02:57:50.982 --> 02:57:54.130
Kitchener. Julian, you have the floor, and you have five minutes.

02:58:04.560 --> 02:58:08.744
Is the mic on? Yep. My name is Julian Ichim.

02:58:08.792 --> 02:58:12.808
I'm here on behalf of the Alan Ryan People's Community Defence Brigade.

02:58:12.984 --> 02:58:16.860
We were created when it became obvious

02:58:17.360 --> 02:58:20.536
that our comrades, our friends,

02:58:20.688 --> 02:58:24.380
our brothers and sisters are dying

02:58:24.800 --> 02:58:28.620
from poisoned drugs, drug overdoses,

02:58:29.100 --> 02:58:32.516
and Like freezing on the streets.

02:58:32.628 --> 02:58:36.004
Now, the thing I want to talk to you about is two Julius

02:58:36.052 --> 02:58:40.052
Streicher and the Nuremberg principles. What does Nuremberg

02:58:40.116 --> 02:58:44.020
and Julius Streicher have to do with the encampment eviction

02:58:44.180 --> 02:58:47.364
and the general war against poor people?

02:58:47.532 --> 02:58:51.300
Julius Streicher never killed

02:58:51.460 --> 02:58:55.238
a Romani or Jew during the Holocaust.

02:58:55.404 --> 02:58:58.786
But he drew cartoons that dehumanized

02:58:58.978 --> 02:59:01.670
Jewish people. And at Nuremberg,

02:59:02.410 --> 02:59:06.146
he was hung because he created the climate

02:59:06.338 --> 02:59:09.630
that allowed the Holocaust to happen.

02:59:10.090 --> 02:59:14.370
In Nuremberg, people were saying we were following

02:59:14.490 --> 02:59:17.710
the law, we were doing what we were told.

02:59:18.010 --> 02:59:21.796
And they were rightfully hung as well. Because it's

02:59:21.828 --> 02:59:25.396
not good enough to say I was told

02:59:25.468 --> 02:59:28.692
to. People are dying. That is

02:59:28.716 --> 02:59:33.240
a fact. What we are having right now is we're having an ideological

02:59:33.660 --> 02:59:37.492
as well as a physical attack

02:59:37.596 --> 02:59:41.400
on poor people. With the closure of the safe supply,

02:59:41.900 --> 02:59:45.924
the school board decision to

02:59:46.012 --> 02:59:49.390
put only the Canadian flag,

02:59:49.470 --> 02:59:53.438
which is a symbol of genocide, and the Ontario

02:59:53.534 --> 02:59:57.246
flag has nothing to do with flags, but it's attack

02:59:57.318 --> 03:00:00.526
on all lives matter, it's attack on pride, et cetera,

03:00:00.558 --> 03:00:03.790
et cetera, et cetera. So we're having the

03:00:03.830 --> 03:00:07.278
closure of the safe injection

03:00:07.374 --> 03:00:10.702
site, which is not just a place where people go

03:00:10.726 --> 03:00:14.220
and use drugs. It's one of the only place where homeless people can actually

03:00:14.350 --> 03:00:17.792
get medical services. We're having at

03:00:17.816 --> 03:00:21.424
a time when we're seeing xylazine and poison in the

03:00:21.432 --> 03:00:25.296
drug supply and more and more people are dying.

03:00:25.488 --> 03:00:29.392
We're shutting down the only place where they can test

03:00:29.496 --> 03:00:33.296
drugs to see if they're poisoned or not. They're shutting

03:00:33.328 --> 03:00:37.168
down the safe supply. And now they are

03:00:37.224 --> 03:00:41.086
closing the encampment or they want

03:00:41.238 --> 03:00:44.862
to close the encampment. This is a

03:00:44.886 --> 03:00:48.302
clear attack on poor people. And the fact that it

03:00:48.326 --> 03:00:52.238
will be done on December 1 means that

03:00:52.294 --> 03:00:54.782
people will freeze to death,

03:00:54.966 --> 03:00:59.166
particularly those with disabilities and

03:00:59.238 --> 03:01:03.010
those that will be affected by the courts.

03:01:03.350 --> 03:01:06.814
So what we're seeing here is we're

03:01:06.862 --> 03:01:10.734
seeing the region that entered into

03:01:10.822 --> 03:01:14.270
negotiations of good faith with the

03:01:14.310 --> 03:01:18.190
community to create the plan to end chronic homelessness.

03:01:18.350 --> 03:01:20.170
And then in secret,

03:01:20.710 --> 03:01:24.446
while Doug Ford is putting all these commercials

03:01:24.478 --> 03:01:28.638
about not wanting needles near playgrounds

03:01:28.734 --> 03:01:31.890
and not wanting all these tents and stuff,

03:01:32.390 --> 03:01:36.250
we're seeing the region

03:01:37.750 --> 03:01:41.102
help these attacks. And the people that are going to

03:01:41.126 --> 03:01:44.862
suffer are the most vulnerable.

03:01:45.006 --> 03:01:48.890
The people that are going to suffer are people

03:01:49.510 --> 03:01:52.574
that the Nazis were the first to kill. It will be

03:01:52.582 --> 03:01:56.078
the disabled, homeless people that will die and

03:01:56.134 --> 03:01:59.932
freeze first. It will be people that cannot access

03:02:00.126 --> 03:02:04.032
their pain medication or medical services because the

03:02:04.056 --> 03:02:06.300
safe injection site is shut down.

03:02:06.920 --> 03:02:10.340
It'll be people. Julian, you have one minute remaining.

03:02:11.560 --> 03:02:14.540
Yeah, that's fine. The fact is,

03:02:15.080 --> 03:02:18.784
whatever decision you make, history will judge you.

03:02:18.872 --> 03:02:22.688
People are going to be sitting later, maybe 20

03:02:22.744 --> 03:02:26.716
years down the line, and they're going to talk about the genocide

03:02:26.848 --> 03:02:30.548
against poor people, and they're going to talk about

03:02:30.684 --> 03:02:34.244
this decision here. They're going to talk about how people

03:02:34.332 --> 03:02:37.988
voted, and they're going to talk about the

03:02:38.044 --> 03:02:42.372
climate, the political climate in which this is going on.

03:02:42.556 --> 03:02:46.324
What side of history do you want to be on? Do you want to be

03:02:46.492 --> 03:02:50.520
one of those people that will be condemned at the new Nuremberg

03:02:51.180 --> 03:02:54.428
with your saying that all we were told to by

03:02:54.484 --> 03:02:58.780
the provincial government or Trump's tariffs forced

03:02:58.860 --> 03:03:01.852
us because we don't want to be seen as this and this. Or do you

03:03:01.876 --> 03:03:04.892
want to be seen as being on the side of the

03:03:04.916 --> 03:03:08.252
people that are being killed? Because a reckoning

03:03:08.316 --> 03:03:11.880
will come and people

03:03:12.340 --> 03:03:16.236
will hold you accountable for the decisions you make today

03:03:16.308 --> 03:03:19.840
here. Thank you, Julian. I have no questions.

03:03:20.430 --> 03:03:23.690
The next. The next delegate is Erin

03:03:24.030 --> 03:03:26.970
Dej from Cambridge.

03:03:27.950 --> 03:03:30.290
Erin, tell me how you say your last name.

03:03:31.870 --> 03:03:35.078
It's pronounced Day, but I don't hold anybody at fault

03:03:35.094 --> 03:03:38.630
for pronouncing it Dej. I pronounced it Dej until I married the man

03:03:38.750 --> 03:03:42.134
who gave me the last name. You have the floor and you have five minutes.

03:03:42.182 --> 03:03:44.934
Welcome. Thank you for not making that, Just talking about my last name, Be part

03:03:44.942 --> 03:03:48.492
of my five minutes. About a year ago, I and many

03:03:48.516 --> 03:03:52.092
of the people in this room came here to ask this council to

03:03:52.116 --> 03:03:54.880
endorse the plan to end chronic homelessness.

03:03:55.220 --> 03:03:58.988
At the time, I told you that in my 15 years of doing

03:03:59.044 --> 03:04:03.228
research in the homelessness sector, I have not seen such an ambitious

03:04:03.324 --> 03:04:06.620
and transformational approach to effectively

03:04:06.700 --> 03:04:10.300
respond to the homelessness crisis. I thank

03:04:10.380 --> 03:04:14.062
council for endorsing and investing in that plan and

03:04:14.086 --> 03:04:17.822
I continue to believe it is the best way forward for

03:04:17.846 --> 03:04:21.934
our community. The proposed 100 Victoria

03:04:21.982 --> 03:04:25.310
Street Code of Use bylaw does not adhere to

03:04:25.350 --> 03:04:28.734
that plan that you endorsed. As such,

03:04:28.822 --> 03:04:32.690
I humbly ask this council to reject the proposed bylaw.

03:04:33.350 --> 03:04:37.150
One of the reasons the plan is so exceptional is because

03:04:37.190 --> 03:04:41.008
it outlines both the process and the outcomes

03:04:41.104 --> 03:04:44.640
to addressing homelessness. The bylaw in front

03:04:44.680 --> 03:04:49.232
of you fails on both these counts. in

03:04:49.256 --> 03:04:52.336
terms of process, The co-creators table,

03:04:52.448 --> 03:04:56.208
of which I am a member and which is meant to oversee the rollout

03:04:56.224 --> 03:05:00.160
of the plan to end chronic homelessness, was not consulted on how best

03:05:00.200 --> 03:05:04.020
to approach the future of the 100 Victoria street encampment.

03:05:04.850 --> 03:05:08.682
While the plan grounds itself in a human rights approach, the residents

03:05:08.746 --> 03:05:12.298
of 100 Vic were not informed about what was happening

03:05:12.394 --> 03:05:16.106
until hours after dumpsters and construction material were brought

03:05:16.138 --> 03:05:19.898
on site. Those intervening hours

03:05:20.034 --> 03:05:23.790
were filled with fear, stress and chaos,

03:05:24.290 --> 03:05:27.738
all of which were avoidable if appropriate

03:05:27.834 --> 03:05:30.350
communication protocols had been followed.

03:05:31.500 --> 03:05:35.908
The erosion of trust that has occurred from these actions undermines

03:05:36.004 --> 03:05:39.080
some of the well intentioned elements of the bylaw.

03:05:39.820 --> 03:05:43.880
I appreciate the six month window to support people to find housing,

03:05:44.300 --> 03:05:49.124
although when the region's shelter capacity is at about 21%

03:05:49.212 --> 03:05:52.676
of the homeless population, I doubt six months is enough

03:05:52.748 --> 03:05:56.212
time. but the staff's plan is to

03:05:56.236 --> 03:06:01.236
use the same trailer that was dropped off last week without communication

03:06:01.428 --> 03:06:05.396
to work on a housing plan. This trailer,

03:06:05.508 --> 03:06:09.560
a symbol of fear and chaos and exclusion,

03:06:09.900 --> 03:06:14.052
is now meant to be the site of support and resources for

03:06:14.076 --> 03:06:17.476
residents. The second

03:06:17.548 --> 03:06:20.900
part of the plan is a focus on positive outcomes to

03:06:20.940 --> 03:06:23.280
help end chronic homelessness in the region.

03:06:24.310 --> 03:06:27.998
The 100 Victoria Street Code of Use bylaw undermines those

03:06:28.054 --> 03:06:30.878
efforts. First of all,

03:06:31.014 --> 03:06:34.334
47% of the proposed site support

03:06:34.422 --> 03:06:38.046
budget for this bylaw is for temporary motels,

03:06:38.238 --> 03:06:42.970
which the report clarifies will not extend past 2026.

03:06:43.990 --> 03:06:47.854
This means that in just over a year, people who cannot find affordable

03:06:47.902 --> 03:06:52.088
and supportive housing because there is no vacancy

03:06:52.264 --> 03:06:55.944
will be back on the street. In this way,

03:06:56.032 --> 03:06:59.820
the bylaw is a stall tactic, not a solution.

03:07:00.960 --> 03:07:04.940
In fact, I strongly suspect this approach will make things worse.

03:07:05.440 --> 03:07:09.080
I am a researcher and so I can't help but cite research and

03:07:09.120 --> 03:07:13.192
two recent peer reviewed studies showed that encampment evictions

03:07:13.336 --> 03:07:17.186
increased health risks for residents and precipitated

03:07:17.298 --> 03:07:20.834
violence. This approach will make the community

03:07:21.002 --> 03:07:22.390
less safe.

03:07:23.770 --> 03:07:27.026
I was particularly disappointed that the proposed bylaw

03:07:27.058 --> 03:07:30.706
includes a sanction for up to $5,000 for someone

03:07:30.778 --> 03:07:34.418
who continues to occupy the space past December 1st or

03:07:34.474 --> 03:07:38.230
someone who provides support to someone in that time, like mutual aid.

03:07:38.970 --> 03:07:43.364
to write in a fine at all, let alone an amount like $5,000,

03:07:43.412 --> 03:07:47.060
I see a minute, tells me that this plan and bylaw

03:07:47.140 --> 03:07:50.532
were not written with community input or thought to

03:07:50.556 --> 03:07:54.452
the impact of that kind of sanction. By way

03:07:54.476 --> 03:07:57.924
of comparison, last year the Ontario Superior

03:07:57.972 --> 03:08:01.348
Court of Justice struck down multiple sections

03:08:01.444 --> 03:08:04.884
of the Ontario Safe Streets act, which the fine

03:08:04.932 --> 03:08:08.830
for panhandling was at most $500.

03:08:09.890 --> 03:08:14.090
The impact of this kind of ticketing, even at much lower amounts,

03:08:14.170 --> 03:08:17.450
is harsh and further entrenches people in

03:08:17.490 --> 03:08:21.130
homelessness. In the vast majority of

03:08:21.170 --> 03:08:24.810
Ontario Safe Streets Act tickets, people are convicted for

03:08:24.850 --> 03:08:28.602
not paying their fine because, as Heather so clearly mentioned, we are fining people who

03:08:28.626 --> 03:08:32.070
are homeless as a way of sanctioning them.

03:08:32.780 --> 03:08:36.676
The accumulated debt that people receive for unpaid tickets is sent to consumer

03:08:36.708 --> 03:08:40.900
reporting, making access to private market housing nearly impossible

03:08:41.060 --> 03:08:44.760
and in some cases leads to jail time for unpaid fines.

03:08:45.500 --> 03:08:48.644
To sum up, Oh, I won't do my sum up paragraph. I will leave it

03:08:48.652 --> 03:08:52.100
there. Can you sum up in a couple sentences? Yeah, it is. okay.

03:08:52.180 --> 03:08:55.668
To sum up, the bylaw does not align with the process

03:08:55.724 --> 03:08:59.062
and outcomes outlined by the plan that was endorsed by council.

03:08:59.236 --> 03:09:03.154
The bylaw has already caused harm and it hasn't been adopted.

03:09:03.282 --> 03:09:06.898
It will continue to cause harm in the months to come. I ask

03:09:06.954 --> 03:09:10.642
council to reject the bylaw and to direct staff to work with the

03:09:10.666 --> 03:09:14.082
community on a plan and process that doesn't rely on punitive

03:09:14.146 --> 03:09:17.714
techniques and instead works in the best interests of encampment

03:09:17.762 --> 03:09:21.394
Residents and the community at large. Thank you for those extra seconds.

03:09:21.442 --> 03:09:25.820
Erin, Councillor Wolf has a question. through

03:09:25.860 --> 03:09:29.420
you, Madam Chair, and again a comment. And I just wanted to thank you because

03:09:29.460 --> 03:09:33.052
you're from Cambridge and out of 27 delegates we

03:09:33.076 --> 03:09:36.812
have one from Cambridge and you represented us very well. Oh boy. No pressure.

03:09:36.876 --> 03:09:39.640
Thank you. Thank you.

03:09:41.620 --> 03:09:45.880
Now we will welcome Meagan Snyder, Unsheltered Campaign.

03:09:47.780 --> 03:09:51.014
Meagan, welcome. You have the floor in it. You have five minutes.

03:09:51.172 --> 03:09:54.994
Thank you. Yes, I am here representing Unsheltered

03:09:55.042 --> 03:09:58.482
Campaign tonight. But I hope they will forgive me a bit of

03:09:58.506 --> 03:10:01.150
a personal roundabout way into it.

03:10:01.850 --> 03:10:05.858
In my day job, I am an early childhood pedagogical consultant

03:10:05.954 --> 03:10:09.522
and I am a mother of a 7 year old. And a few weeks ago

03:10:09.626 --> 03:10:13.538
my 7 year old and I were very happy to participate in

03:10:13.594 --> 03:10:16.882
an event put on by the Children Youth and Planning table and their

03:10:16.906 --> 03:10:20.440
Child Voice project called Building Our Communities

03:10:20.520 --> 03:10:24.072
of Care. And this was at the KPL. It was a wonderful event

03:10:24.256 --> 03:10:27.816
where children and families were making their voices heard

03:10:27.928 --> 03:10:31.880
about what it looks like for them, what it means to them to have

03:10:32.000 --> 03:10:35.380
a caring community. And 

03:10:36.160 --> 03:10:39.752
The project asked us to think about what it looks like to

03:10:39.776 --> 03:10:43.180
have a community of care across four lenses.

03:10:43.510 --> 03:10:47.310
Community, allyship, equity, and face

03:10:47.350 --> 03:10:51.870
to face connections. If we want to

03:10:51.910 --> 03:10:55.470
build these communities of care for our children, it has

03:10:55.510 --> 03:10:59.582
to start now, with action. And it

03:10:59.606 --> 03:11:02.830
doesn't only start out there at schools and

03:11:02.870 --> 03:11:06.478
at libraries and childcare centers, in interactions with

03:11:06.534 --> 03:11:10.236
children. It starts here in this room.

03:11:10.388 --> 03:11:13.596
It starts with every analysis of every

03:11:13.748 --> 03:11:17.180
proposed bylaw, every presentation that is

03:11:17.220 --> 03:11:20.956
put in front of you all and analyzing all of this

03:11:21.028 --> 03:11:24.652
through the lenses of community, allyship,

03:11:24.796 --> 03:11:27.360
equity, and face to face connection.

03:11:28.980 --> 03:11:32.204
As I said, I am here tonight representing Unsheltered

03:11:32.252 --> 03:11:36.382
Campaign. The Unsheltered Campaign is a group of local community members

03:11:36.476 --> 03:11:41.034
who are housed and unhoused and who work with people experiencing unsheltered

03:11:41.082 --> 03:11:43.430
homelessness to advocate for change.

03:11:44.450 --> 03:11:47.978
Having listened to the delegations before me, I'm struck by

03:11:48.034 --> 03:11:51.402
the incredibly rich expertise about homelessness

03:11:51.466 --> 03:11:54.858
in this room and in this region and these residents

03:11:54.954 --> 03:11:58.202
generosity in sharing this expertise in the name of

03:11:58.226 --> 03:12:02.032
their caring community, their community's well being.

03:12:02.186 --> 03:12:06.356
What an incredible asset in building an innovative human

03:12:06.428 --> 03:12:10.132
rights based approach to homelessness. I know that

03:12:10.156 --> 03:12:13.780
the region of Waterloo has put processes in place to make sure

03:12:13.820 --> 03:12:16.980
you're accessing this local expertise, both lived and

03:12:17.020 --> 03:12:20.660
learned, as part of your own plan to end chronic homelessness.

03:12:20.820 --> 03:12:24.564
And I find this proposed bylaw and we do at Unsheltered Campaign to

03:12:24.572 --> 03:12:28.342
be incongruent with that collaborative innovative approach.

03:12:28.516 --> 03:12:32.162
And I hope what you've heard tonight from the delegates before me serves as an

03:12:32.186 --> 03:12:35.938
opening, an invitation, an opportunity to get that

03:12:35.994 --> 03:12:39.570
back on track on that path that you as a council have

03:12:39.610 --> 03:12:43.058
laid out with support from your own constituents, which is

03:12:43.114 --> 03:12:46.882
so powerful. Tonight We are

03:12:46.906 --> 03:12:50.562
asking you obviously to reject the proposed bylaw respecting the use

03:12:50.586 --> 03:12:54.002
of 100 Victoria Street North Kitchener. Not only the

03:12:54.026 --> 03:12:58.032
bylaw in and of itself, but also the approach the bylaw represents

03:12:58.096 --> 03:13:01.760
are harmful to Those sheltering at 100 Victoria and

03:13:01.800 --> 03:13:05.664
deeply concerning to us as a group of advocates, neighbors and service

03:13:05.752 --> 03:13:09.408
providers. The bylaw was created and put forward without any

03:13:09.464 --> 03:13:12.992
consultation with people living at 100 Victoria or with the

03:13:13.016 --> 03:13:16.560
service providers, your community partners working with

03:13:16.600 --> 03:13:20.256
the residents. Like I said, you have put mechanisms

03:13:20.288 --> 03:13:23.714
into place to make sure this type of engagement happens,

03:13:23.842 --> 03:13:27.990
including your own plan to end chronic homelessness co-creators table.

03:13:28.570 --> 03:13:32.402
but the co-creators table as we've heard, was not consulted and the

03:13:32.426 --> 03:13:36.242
bylaw was announced to residents of 100 Victoria by bringing

03:13:36.306 --> 03:13:40.270
police, heavy equipment and dumpsters on site without any

03:13:40.650 --> 03:13:44.194
communication or information. I invite

03:13:44.242 --> 03:13:47.370
you to think about the symbols of belonging and

03:13:47.410 --> 03:13:51.002
symbols of caring and symbols of the opposite of

03:13:51.026 --> 03:13:54.074
that in our region. I see One minute. Meagan,

03:13:54.122 --> 03:13:55.910
you have one minute left. Thank you.

03:13:57.810 --> 03:14:01.562
Instead of approving this flawed and inhumane bylaw, tonight we are

03:14:01.586 --> 03:14:04.510
asking you to consider one of the following options.

03:14:04.930 --> 03:14:08.730
One, do not remove the encampment from 100 Victoria and

03:14:08.770 --> 03:14:12.122
explore other ways for the region to meet its obligations to

03:14:12.146 --> 03:14:15.790
method Metrolinx. We can be imaginative. We can

03:14:15.910 --> 03:14:18.770
open ourselves up to other possibilities.

03:14:19.190 --> 03:14:22.862
Two, Work with people at 100 Victoria to designate an

03:14:22.886 --> 03:14:26.846
alternative location for camping that is mutually acceptable and

03:14:26.918 --> 03:14:30.942
in close proximity to necessary life saving services,

03:14:31.126 --> 03:14:34.734
life affirming services with the same legal protections

03:14:34.782 --> 03:14:38.622
as 100 Victoria. Three, refer the issue back

03:14:38.646 --> 03:14:42.676
to the plan to end chronic homelessness co-creators table and direct

03:14:42.748 --> 03:14:46.916
this table which includes people who work directly with residents and lived

03:14:46.948 --> 03:14:50.820
experts to create an alternate plan to meet the region's needs for

03:14:50.860 --> 03:14:55.044
the property using the budget associated with the proposed bylaw.

03:14:55.172 --> 03:14:58.372
Unsheltered campaign has included this and more details,

03:14:58.436 --> 03:15:01.748
many more details in a letter to you all which in less

03:15:01.804 --> 03:15:05.444
than in only about 12 hours has gained signatures

03:15:05.492 --> 03:15:08.910
from 616 other agencies and individuals

03:15:08.990 --> 03:15:12.926
from the co-creators table. So I please urge you all to

03:15:12.998 --> 03:15:16.702
read that letter it has been sent out and take it very seriously.

03:15:16.766 --> 03:15:20.270
Thank you so much. Thank you, Meagan. I have no questions.

03:15:20.430 --> 03:15:24.370
The next delegation is Tara Jones from Waterloo.

03:15:28.630 --> 03:15:32.330
Welcome to the podium. You have five minutes. Thank you.

03:15:32.710 --> 03:15:36.318
Thanks so much for the opportunity to speak Tonight, I'm coming to you

03:15:36.454 --> 03:15:39.662
not only as a planning student in the University of

03:15:39.686 --> 03:15:44.350
Waterloo, but also someone who has experienced homelessness firsthand.

03:15:44.430 --> 03:15:47.886
So this is not only an academic issue for me, but like a deeply personal

03:15:47.958 --> 03:15:51.278
one. This is my first time delegating

03:15:51.454 --> 03:15:54.782
to this regional council, so I wanted to be sure that I

03:15:54.806 --> 03:15:58.010
fully understood the council's role in this decision.

03:15:58.550 --> 03:16:01.694
Within your code of conduct, I found that guiding principle

03:16:01.742 --> 03:16:05.742
2.2 commits council members to honor, support and

03:16:05.766 --> 03:16:09.770
employ regional values as outlined in the region's strategic plan.

03:16:10.310 --> 03:16:13.902
This of course led me to the strategic plan which envisions the

03:16:13.926 --> 03:16:17.550
region as a compassionate community that cares for all people

03:16:17.670 --> 03:16:21.374
wherein everyone has an opportunity to live a good life. Tonight I

03:16:21.382 --> 03:16:24.810
wish to outline how approving the proposed bylaw

03:16:24.990 --> 03:16:28.190
will directly contradict the region's strategic plan.

03:16:29.130 --> 03:16:32.626
The strategic plan outlines the region's responsibility to ensure

03:16:32.698 --> 03:16:35.714
people have access to services they need when,

03:16:35.802 --> 03:16:39.250
where and how they need them most. The encampment at 100

03:16:39.290 --> 03:16:42.834
Victoria provides stability to residents by reducing

03:16:42.882 --> 03:16:45.986
transiency and critical access

03:16:46.058 --> 03:16:49.362
to downtown Kitchener's amenities. If this bylaw were

03:16:49.386 --> 03:16:53.428
to come into effect, it would cause the displacement of encampment residents,

03:16:53.604 --> 03:16:57.780
hindering outreach workers abilities to locate them and serve them.

03:16:57.900 --> 03:17:01.620
It would also limit residents abilities to access much

03:17:01.660 --> 03:17:05.284
needed services. Further, the strategic plan commits

03:17:05.332 --> 03:17:09.188
the region to deliver new models of service through community collaboration

03:17:09.284 --> 03:17:13.364
and co-design. The report attached to the proposed bylaw

03:17:13.412 --> 03:17:17.314
states that individuals currently residing at 100 Victoria north

03:17:17.492 --> 03:17:21.158
are being informed about the proposed bylaw. I would like to note to council

03:17:21.214 --> 03:17:25.446
members that informing is not the same as consultation and is certainly

03:17:25.478 --> 03:17:28.918
not a collaborative process or a process of co-design.

03:17:28.974 --> 03:17:32.486
Informing residents is an important first step,

03:17:32.558 --> 03:17:36.166
but it is ultimately tokenistic without a responsive channel

03:17:36.198 --> 03:17:40.742
for feedback. True partnership with citizens would require negotiation

03:17:40.886 --> 03:17:44.132
and shared decision making power yielded by the region

03:17:44.236 --> 03:17:48.036
to those affected by the proposed bylaw. As council

03:17:48.108 --> 03:17:51.828
members, I also understand you all to be advocates for the public process

03:17:51.964 --> 03:17:56.676
who promote public consultation and involvement in decision making processes.

03:17:56.868 --> 03:18:00.484
As stated by guiding principle 2.3 of your code of conduct,

03:18:00.612 --> 03:18:04.500
I urge you to uphold this principle by ensuring meaningful engagement before

03:18:04.540 --> 03:18:08.068
you move forward with this bylaw. The strategic plan

03:18:08.124 --> 03:18:11.950
focuses on the provision of safe and permanent housing.

03:18:12.290 --> 03:18:15.482
The homes for all goal outlined in the

03:18:15.506 --> 03:18:19.034
strategic plan specifically highlights the regional objective

03:18:19.082 --> 03:18:22.990
to eliminate reliance on traditional emergency shelter models.

03:18:23.410 --> 03:18:26.810
Many residents of the encampment are being offered motel stays

03:18:26.890 --> 03:18:29.530
to encourage them to vacate 100 Victoria.

03:18:29.690 --> 03:18:32.954
However, according to the report, these motels

03:18:33.002 --> 03:18:37.190
are temporary fixes for which funding will end in 2027.

03:18:37.500 --> 03:18:40.612
Further, the budget for Annualized supportive housing is not set

03:18:40.636 --> 03:18:44.292
to increase in 2027. This means that those exiting the

03:18:44.316 --> 03:18:47.556
motel program provided by the region will no longer

03:18:47.588 --> 03:18:51.348
be supported in 2027. In passing this bylaw, the region

03:18:51.404 --> 03:18:55.060
will be acting in direct opposition of their strategic plan by

03:18:55.100 --> 03:18:58.772
failing to provide permanence and safety to the individuals who will be

03:18:58.796 --> 03:19:02.628
displaced not only by their removal from the encampment, but also

03:19:02.684 --> 03:19:05.080
their expulsion from supportive housing programs.

03:19:06.210 --> 03:19:09.530
In summary, this bylaw undermines the region's commitments

03:19:09.610 --> 03:19:12.550
to Compassion, Equity, and Homes for all.

03:19:12.930 --> 03:19:16.090
I encourage council to reject it or

03:19:16.130 --> 03:19:20.714
at a minimum, delay, until meaningful co-design has occurred.

03:19:20.842 --> 03:19:24.250
Thanks so much. Thank you very much, Tara. I see no

03:19:24.290 --> 03:19:28.058
questions. The next delegation is Martin

03:19:28.234 --> 03:19:31.720
Asling, Waterloo Region Yes in My Backyard.

03:19:41.820 --> 03:19:45.060
Welcome Martin. You have the podium and you have five minutes.

03:19:45.220 --> 03:19:49.092
Thank you. I'll also be speaking on

03:19:49.116 --> 03:19:52.852
the 100 Victoria encampment. Thank you for letting me speak on

03:19:52.876 --> 03:19:56.264
this important topic. In 2024,

03:19:56.412 --> 03:19:59.616
the Region of Waterloo approved the plan to end chronic homelessness.

03:19:59.728 --> 03:20:03.120
An ambitious and important plan that not only sets out what

03:20:03.160 --> 03:20:06.432
to do, but how to do it. The details are important so

03:20:06.456 --> 03:20:10.384
I'll quote them at length. The plan states we will establish

03:20:10.432 --> 03:20:14.656
a whole of community leadership model that includes lived

03:20:14.688 --> 03:20:18.368
experts, equity owed groups, service providers, system leaders

03:20:18.424 --> 03:20:22.192
and area municipalities and region of Waterloo staff. The goal of

03:20:22.216 --> 03:20:26.036
establishing establishing community driven system leadership

03:20:26.148 --> 03:20:29.652
is to disseminate system decision making power to

03:20:29.676 --> 03:20:33.172
increase transparency and trust and responsibility to

03:20:33.196 --> 03:20:36.612
ensure that the system is built to be accountable to the needs of

03:20:36.636 --> 03:20:40.180
those experiencing homelessness. Later on, the plan further

03:20:40.220 --> 03:20:43.560
outlines what kind of relationship this entails.

03:20:44.060 --> 03:20:47.924
This is more, This is more than an amplification

03:20:47.972 --> 03:20:51.324
of voices at that as that suggests that we are maintaining

03:20:51.372 --> 03:20:54.476
systems of oppression. We need to completely redesign

03:20:54.588 --> 03:20:57.436
how we include interest holders in this work.

03:20:57.588 --> 03:21:01.340
Advancing a whole of community approach where lived living expertise of

03:21:01.380 --> 03:21:04.940
chronic homelessness, Racial equity, and social justice are

03:21:04.980 --> 03:21:06.920
central in decision making.

03:21:08.660 --> 03:21:12.332
Funding choices and policy creation will ensure the homelessness

03:21:12.396 --> 03:21:15.896
system will be culturally competent, inclusive and proactive

03:21:16.028 --> 03:21:19.136
in addressing systemic harm. For this to succeed,

03:21:19.248 --> 03:21:23.200
traditional power holders also need to let power transfer

03:21:23.280 --> 03:21:26.416
to others. This is an important plan,

03:21:26.568 --> 03:21:29.888
but it's even more important that all aspects of it are followed through

03:21:29.944 --> 03:21:33.872
on. In a comparative study of different cities

03:21:33.936 --> 03:21:37.376
homelessness plans, Kerry Doberstein finds that a crucial

03:21:37.408 --> 03:21:40.784
ingredient of any homelessness strategy is throughput

03:21:40.832 --> 03:21:45.000
legitimacy which reflects the ability to follow through on engagement.

03:21:45.500 --> 03:21:49.556
The region which is without

03:21:49.628 --> 03:21:53.892
its strategies can fall apart completely. The region of Waterloo

03:21:53.956 --> 03:21:57.332
invested time, money and good faith in engaging with

03:21:57.356 --> 03:22:00.884
the lived experts through the plan to end chronic homelessness.

03:22:01.012 --> 03:22:04.644
It is vital that they are involved in every important aspect of our homelessness

03:22:04.692 --> 03:22:08.078
strategy and actions. Unfortunately,

03:22:08.174 --> 03:22:12.094
this bylaw was not preceded by the type of engagement necessitated

03:22:12.142 --> 03:22:16.142
by the plan to end chronic homelessness. While the region has been in contact with

03:22:16.166 --> 03:22:19.930
homeless advocates through the plan, they were only

03:22:20.230 --> 03:22:23.646
even made aware of these plans recently and the bylaw

03:22:23.678 --> 03:22:27.230
was certainly not informed by their input. Both residents,

03:22:27.310 --> 03:22:31.022
volunteers who provide mutual aid, and a range of advocates who are

03:22:31.126 --> 03:22:34.794
readily available to communicate with regional staff were scrambling

03:22:34.842 --> 03:22:38.362
to react when police and Bobcats showed up. The process has

03:22:38.386 --> 03:22:42.410
been top down and not at all reflective of the spirit or letter

03:22:42.490 --> 03:22:44.750
of the plan to end chronic homelessness.

03:22:45.570 --> 03:22:49.242
Furthermore, the region has not yet increased the supply of

03:22:49.266 --> 03:22:53.178
affordable housing to the extent needed to match the increased need among

03:22:53.234 --> 03:22:57.338
our unsheltered population. The proposed bylaw acknowledges

03:22:57.434 --> 03:23:01.058
the Ontario Court of Justice decision which found that evicting persons

03:23:01.074 --> 03:23:04.354
from encampments without adequate access to shelter violates Section

03:23:04.402 --> 03:23:08.242
7 rights in the charter. However, they suggest

03:23:08.346 --> 03:23:11.810
that this may no longer apply. And more

03:23:11.850 --> 03:23:15.154
recently, Peter Sweeney, Commissioner of Community Services, said that

03:23:15.162 --> 03:23:18.546
we now have 515 shelter beds in Waterloo Region compared

03:23:18.578 --> 03:23:21.390
to 358 in 2020. However,

03:23:22.010 --> 03:23:25.202
over this period, the recorded need in the community has

03:23:25.226 --> 03:23:28.522
more than doubled from the number that Justice Valente had

03:23:28.546 --> 03:23:32.122
to go by when making his decision. If one compares the 2021

03:23:32.146 --> 03:23:35.386
point time count of 1,085

03:23:35.538 --> 03:23:40.550
with the 2024 point in time count of 2,371.

03:23:40.850 --> 03:23:45.306
Waterloo Region NIMBY has consistently opposed encampment evictions because without

03:23:45.378 --> 03:23:49.002
adequate amounts and degrees of alternative housing, encampment evictions will

03:23:49.026 --> 03:23:52.532
push people further. Martin you have one minute remaining. Thank you. Onto the

03:23:52.556 --> 03:23:56.196
streets and further removed from supports.

03:23:56.308 --> 03:24:00.292
This could lead to a greater risk of victimization, a greater

03:24:00.436 --> 03:24:04.004
threat of drug overdose or poisoning, As experts warn

03:24:04.052 --> 03:24:07.556
us. this threat is even more dire with the closure of the kitchener consumption

03:24:07.588 --> 03:24:11.540
and treatment services site. However, even if the region rejects this

03:24:11.580 --> 03:24:15.508
above view, it is still vital for the region to closely follow

03:24:15.644 --> 03:24:19.800
the engagement requirements set out in the plan to end chronic homelessness.

03:24:20.100 --> 03:24:23.772
In place of this bylaw, we urge regional staff to come back to

03:24:23.796 --> 03:24:27.560
council with a new proposal that follows the whole of community approach

03:24:28.100 --> 03:24:31.596
in collaboration with the lived experts involved with the plan to end chronic

03:24:31.628 --> 03:24:34.908
homelessness and the people at the 100 Victoria encampment.

03:24:35.004 --> 03:24:38.140
Thank you. Thank you, Martin. I see no questions.

03:24:38.300 --> 03:24:40.444
The next delegation is Shannon Down,

03:24:40.532 --> 03:24:41.600
Waterloo.

03:24:49.310 --> 03:24:52.650
Welcome, Shannon. The floor is yours and you have five minutes.

03:24:53.790 --> 03:24:57.942
Thank you. Good evening members of Council, Regional Chair Redman.

03:24:58.086 --> 03:25:01.638
My name is Shannon Down. I was the former Executive Director

03:25:01.694 --> 03:25:04.290
of Waterloo Region Community Legal Services.

03:25:04.910 --> 03:25:08.998
And I was co-counsel on the regional municipality

03:25:09.014 --> 03:25:12.380
of Waterloo and persons unknown

03:25:12.510 --> 03:25:16.544
and to be ascertained case. I retired in December

03:25:16.592 --> 03:25:19.700
from that role. So I am here tonight as a concerned resident.

03:25:20.600 --> 03:25:23.344
While I'm not working directly on these issues anymore,

03:25:23.392 --> 03:25:26.528
professionally, I remain very passionate about the problem

03:25:26.584 --> 03:25:30.320
of homelessness and I want to see the region where I

03:25:30.360 --> 03:25:34.900
live be a leader in taking a human rights based approach to housing.

03:25:35.640 --> 03:25:39.402
Let's talk about competing needs. The region says it

03:25:39.426 --> 03:25:43.002
needs the property for a lay down site for materials for

03:25:43.026 --> 03:25:46.746
a transit hub. People living in the encampment

03:25:46.858 --> 03:25:50.442
have needs. They need to be able to shelter themselves

03:25:50.506 --> 03:25:52.910
from the elements while they remain homeless.

03:25:53.970 --> 03:25:58.218
I'm going to talk about some basic facts about encampments that

03:25:58.274 --> 03:26:02.186
any of the people who are frontline workers who I see here

03:26:02.338 --> 03:26:05.882
or staff at the region or one of the many agencies that have

03:26:05.906 --> 03:26:09.770
been working so hard to support people experiencing homelessness

03:26:09.850 --> 03:26:12.922
could also tell you. People who end up in

03:26:12.946 --> 03:26:17.098
the encampments, could be someone who has been chronically homeless,

03:26:17.274 --> 03:26:20.750
They may have spent years going in and out of shelter,

03:26:21.170 --> 03:26:24.670
facing uncertainty, constant displacement,

03:26:25.170 --> 03:26:27.950
violence, loss of belongings,

03:26:28.450 --> 03:26:31.310
and they are looking for some stability and safety.

03:26:32.020 --> 03:26:34.920
Their tent at the encampment is their home.

03:26:36.180 --> 03:26:39.852
They would prefer to live in an actual home, but until that happens,

03:26:39.916 --> 03:26:43.132
the tent where they have some belongings and can count on being

03:26:43.156 --> 03:26:46.520
able to return to it is the best they have.

03:26:47.860 --> 03:26:51.244
Newly homeless people who cannot face the prospect

03:26:51.292 --> 03:26:54.540
of living in congregate space shelters may

03:26:54.580 --> 03:26:57.280
turn to an encampment for some privacy,

03:26:57.660 --> 03:27:00.900
particularly if they have special needs or are a couple or

03:27:00.940 --> 03:27:05.236
have a pet. Drug users who need some safety

03:27:05.348 --> 03:27:08.900
and who need people around them to keep them from overdosing

03:27:09.060 --> 03:27:11.960
if they're alone may end up at the encampment.

03:27:12.300 --> 03:27:16.160
It's safer for them than being isolated in a motel room.

03:27:17.180 --> 03:27:20.852
The Region's plan to remove the encampment at 100 Vic and replace it with

03:27:20.876 --> 03:27:24.750
shelter beds and motel rooms does not meet those needs

03:27:24.870 --> 03:27:28.190
and many others that I do not have the time to detail In five

03:27:28.230 --> 03:27:32.414
minutes. there needs to be a place like 100 Victoria

03:27:32.462 --> 03:27:35.930
street that can meet those needs. And the region

03:27:36.230 --> 03:27:39.614
should designate land for that purpose. You're probably

03:27:39.662 --> 03:27:43.022
thinking, well, Shannon, we don't want to do that because

03:27:43.046 --> 03:27:46.670
we don't want any encampments. But we know that while the

03:27:46.710 --> 03:27:50.382
number of homeless people in our region exceeds the number of shelter beds by a

03:27:50.406 --> 03:27:53.200
factor of four to five, and it's getting worse,

03:27:53.860 --> 03:27:57.372
then the reality is that there are going to be encampments around for a

03:27:57.396 --> 03:28:01.228
long time. We know from the last point in time

03:28:01.284 --> 03:28:05.212
count that the number of people experiencing homelessness in our region has more

03:28:05.236 --> 03:28:09.200
than doubled since the time that the encampment case was argued.

03:28:09.700 --> 03:28:13.004
The situation is worse. This plan

03:28:13.092 --> 03:28:16.924
just means that there will be more scattered encampments with fewer

03:28:16.972 --> 03:28:20.328
supports and the people living there will face

03:28:20.384 --> 03:28:23.140
frequent displacements, putting them at greater risk.

03:28:24.720 --> 03:28:27.928
I want you as councillors to

03:28:27.984 --> 03:28:31.480
ask some hard questions about this plan. Does it really meet

03:28:31.520 --> 03:28:35.528
the needs of the residents of Waterloo region who are currently living at

03:28:35.584 --> 03:28:38.936
100 Victoria Street. Does it meet the needs

03:28:39.008 --> 03:28:42.632
of the over 2,300 people experiencing homelessness in our

03:28:42.656 --> 03:28:46.202
region? Or does it just meet the needs of the

03:28:46.226 --> 03:28:48.710
Region of Waterloo Transit Hub plan?

03:28:49.650 --> 03:28:53.114
Are the charter rights of the people at the encampment being breached

03:28:53.162 --> 03:28:56.778
by the proposed plan? Is this bylaw?

03:28:56.874 --> 03:29:00.586
You have one minute left, Shannon. Thank you. Is this bylaw

03:29:00.618 --> 03:29:04.590
consistent with taking a human rights based approach to homelessness?

03:29:05.330 --> 03:29:08.650
How does this plan move the needle on the plan to end

03:29:08.690 --> 03:29:12.204
chronic homeless? I'm asking

03:29:12.252 --> 03:29:16.028
you as a council to prioritize the safety and health

03:29:16.084 --> 03:29:19.400
of the most vulnerable residents of our region.

03:29:20.100 --> 03:29:22.400
Thank you for listening. Those are my remarks.

03:29:23.220 --> 03:29:25.840
Thank you very much, Shannon. I see No questions.

03:29:26.260 --> 03:29:30.080
The next delegation is Pranav Seetharaman.

03:29:40.870 --> 03:29:44.606
Welcome. You have the floor and you have five minutes. Okay. I probably won't

03:29:44.638 --> 03:29:45.770
end up using that.

03:29:53.990 --> 03:29:56.850
Sorry. I'm really nervous. I actually might step out. I'm sorry.

03:29:59.270 --> 03:30:01.090
Yeah, I think I'm going to step out. I'm sorry.

03:30:11.310 --> 03:30:14.710
Okay, thank you. If you want to send us something

03:30:14.750 --> 03:30:18.050
in writing, we'd be happy to receive it. Thank you.

03:30:19.070 --> 03:30:22.450
The next delegation is Lynn Intini.

03:30:32.040 --> 03:30:34.580
Welcome Lynn. You have the floor. You have five minutes.

03:30:37.000 --> 03:30:40.960
I attended the co-creators meeting last Tuesday because

03:30:41.000 --> 03:30:44.896
I was promised that regional staff was interested in consulting

03:30:44.928 --> 03:30:48.480
with us about a renoviction bylaw. This now

03:30:48.520 --> 03:30:51.952
feels a bit disingenuous. I appreciate

03:30:52.016 --> 03:30:57.932
staff who listened to us, but when

03:30:57.956 --> 03:31:02.700
I've brought to your attention the

03:31:02.740 --> 03:31:06.236
ways in which a municipal renoviction bylaw could address

03:31:06.308 --> 03:31:09.960
the giant loophole in the Residential Tenancies Act,

03:31:10.420 --> 03:31:14.668
the provincial law that governs tenants rights which essentially

03:31:14.764 --> 03:31:18.460
begs profit driven landlords to displace tenants paying below market

03:31:18.500 --> 03:31:22.030
rent, You certainly empathized with

03:31:22.070 --> 03:31:25.902
me and condemned the landlords for their despicable behavior,

03:31:26.046 --> 03:31:29.422
for not acting in good faith, for not upholding their obligations

03:31:29.486 --> 03:31:33.054
as housing providers, for attempting to erode our currently

03:31:33.142 --> 03:31:37.250
existing affordable rental housing stock by displacing

03:31:37.670 --> 03:31:40.782
long standing tenants in favor of people paying unsustainably

03:31:40.846 --> 03:31:44.382
high rents. What I'm offered is

03:31:44.406 --> 03:31:47.594
a solution to my asks is that you've advocated

03:31:47.642 --> 03:31:51.514
to the province and it's that thing you

03:31:51.522 --> 03:31:54.710
won't even do for the CTS right now.

03:31:55.810 --> 03:31:59.690
I would like you to do that. But I also get

03:31:59.730 --> 03:32:03.354
suggestions that if only tenants knew their rights,

03:32:03.522 --> 03:32:07.098
then they could protect themselves from their landlord. If they knew

03:32:07.114 --> 03:32:10.350
all the steps, they wouldn't fall prey to misleading offers.

03:32:11.820 --> 03:32:14.868
As if knowing your rights is a panacea for

03:32:14.924 --> 03:32:18.640
navigating a very convoluted system that's weighted against you.

03:32:19.580 --> 03:32:21.760
The system here,

03:32:22.460 --> 03:32:25.604
the way this proposed bylaw came about,

03:32:25.772 --> 03:32:27.920
is not any better.

03:32:29.660 --> 03:32:33.124
This. This tonight is an eviction

03:32:33.172 --> 03:32:36.340
hearing. It's not only an

03:32:36.380 --> 03:32:40.226
eviction hearing for the current residents of 100

03:32:40.298 --> 03:32:43.442
Vic, but for those who may have had the

03:32:43.466 --> 03:32:47.682
privilege of crashing on someone's couch for the last week and

03:32:47.706 --> 03:32:51.522
for those who have been gathering the courage and hoping for better weather

03:32:51.586 --> 03:32:55.234
before the evening that they finally must flee

03:32:55.362 --> 03:32:59.042
an abusive situation towards the

03:32:59.066 --> 03:33:02.882
only place that they know to be available because it's visible

03:33:02.946 --> 03:33:06.098
and known. A place where service providers and

03:33:06.154 --> 03:33:09.282
community members offering mutual aid will be available to

03:33:09.306 --> 03:33:13.594
them. The disgusting way this proposal

03:33:13.642 --> 03:33:16.890
was written to be retroactive to a provision

03:33:16.970 --> 03:33:20.870
of notice which was only available online.

03:33:23.490 --> 03:33:27.402
Pardon? Where was the post? Where was the

03:33:27.426 --> 03:33:31.066
posted notice of a site plan application notifying

03:33:31.098 --> 03:33:34.234
the neighborhood of exactly what day they could show up to oppose

03:33:34.282 --> 03:33:36.750
or request modifications to this proposal?

03:33:37.340 --> 03:33:41.044
Where was the notice of hearing that a tenant would get from the landlord tenant

03:33:41.092 --> 03:33:44.260
board? keeping it quiet in order to

03:33:44.300 --> 03:33:47.620
minimize the number of people who would be offered

03:33:47.700 --> 03:33:51.892
anything at all? That is scuzzy landlord

03:33:51.956 --> 03:33:55.908
logic. Today you are being asked

03:33:55.964 --> 03:33:59.588
to vote for a bylaw that would essentially have you signing off

03:33:59.644 --> 03:34:01.960
on an attempted bad faith eviction.

03:34:03.110 --> 03:34:06.846
You have the opportunity to vote

03:34:06.878 --> 03:34:09.890
against this bylaw as it is proposed.

03:34:10.230 --> 03:34:13.454
You get to decide that this landlord,

03:34:13.582 --> 03:34:16.942
the region of Waterloo, will not tell tenants

03:34:17.006 --> 03:34:20.670
that they have to leave the property until truly suitable

03:34:20.750 --> 03:34:25.010
alternative accommodations which provide security of tenure

03:34:26.470 --> 03:34:30.142
and which meet their needs are found. Accommodations that

03:34:30.166 --> 03:34:33.830
the residents can provide informed consent to.

03:34:35.010 --> 03:34:38.954
You can demonstrate to your constituents and your voting base

03:34:39.002 --> 03:34:41.994
that you will do what you said. Lynn you've got one minute remaining.

03:34:42.122 --> 03:34:46.030
Vote against this bylaw. Send it back to PECH,

03:34:47.010 --> 03:34:49.510
which you agreed to last year.

03:34:50.930 --> 03:34:54.314
You have the opportunity to do better than a worst

03:34:54.362 --> 03:34:55.950
of the worst landlord.

03:34:58.460 --> 03:35:02.132
Thank you, Lynn. The next delegation is Noah Helsby from

03:35:02.156 --> 03:35:03.080
Kitchener.

03:35:06.860 --> 03:35:10.640
Good evening, Madam Chair. My name is Aaron Price. I'm speaking in Noah's place.

03:35:11.660 --> 03:35:14.932
So first things first. I want to start off by saying you

03:35:14.956 --> 03:35:18.244
guys cannot go and close down the site for the

03:35:18.252 --> 03:35:22.068
fact that it goes against all charter of rights and 

03:35:22.124 --> 03:35:26.502
the reasons why I listed in these in

03:35:26.526 --> 03:35:29.702
my speech that I'm going to say right now. Hi, my name is

03:35:29.726 --> 03:35:31.850
Aaron. I reside at 100 Vic.

03:35:32.990 --> 03:35:36.710
The tent city is

03:35:36.750 --> 03:35:40.694
more than just a makeshift shelters. There are vibrant communities

03:35:40.822 --> 03:35:46.742
where people find support and solidarity and a

03:35:46.766 --> 03:35:49.962
sense of belonging. For many residents of those communities

03:35:50.086 --> 03:35:53.826
are a lifeline, offering a network of peers who understand each other's

03:35:53.858 --> 03:35:57.026
rights and struggles and provide mutual aid.

03:35:57.138 --> 03:36:00.738
Removing tent city without providing adequate alternatives

03:36:00.834 --> 03:36:04.786
can be traumatic and pushing vulnerable individuals further

03:36:04.858 --> 03:36:06.150
into the margins.

03:36:08.490 --> 03:36:12.146
Exasperating issues like mental health and addiction

03:36:12.258 --> 03:36:15.720
as well. Rather than tearing down communities,

03:36:15.850 --> 03:36:19.948
you should invest in improving

03:36:20.044 --> 03:36:22.760
conditions and providing essential services,

03:36:23.060 --> 03:36:26.252
Working towards solutions that prioritize dignity and

03:36:26.276 --> 03:36:30.252
humanity. And one more thing, If you guys pass this

03:36:30.356 --> 03:36:33.840
bylaw, Karen Redman, I will be tenting on your front lawn.

03:36:42.910 --> 03:36:46.422
Next delegation is Tanner Bergsma

03:36:46.566 --> 03:36:49.286
from Waterloo. Tanner,

03:36:49.398 --> 03:36:50.810
you have three minutes.

03:36:56.110 --> 03:37:00.118
Good afternoon, chair and councillors. My name is Tanner Bergsma.

03:37:00.214 --> 03:37:02.850
I'm autistic and 22 years old.

03:37:03.310 --> 03:37:07.078
I am the co-chair of the Kitchener 2051 community working group

03:37:07.134 --> 03:37:10.316
and the co founder of two international movements. But tonight

03:37:10.348 --> 03:37:13.548
I'm not speaking on behalf of either of these. Tonight I'm

03:37:13.564 --> 03:37:17.324
speaking as someone who used to be homeless. And more than that, I'm speaking

03:37:17.372 --> 03:37:20.700
for every single unhoused person in this city whose voices

03:37:20.780 --> 03:37:23.932
you have silenced, whose humanity the

03:37:23.956 --> 03:37:27.132
region has ignored, whose pain has chosen not to

03:37:27.156 --> 03:37:31.084
see. The region has not spoken to the homeless populations,

03:37:31.132 --> 03:37:35.466
And now you are here to vote on bylaw 25-021,

03:37:35.548 --> 03:37:39.102
a motion to repurpose 100 Victoria Street north for the

03:37:39.126 --> 03:37:42.462
Kitchener central transit hub. You call it development, you call it

03:37:42.486 --> 03:37:45.742
infrastructure. But let's stop pretending. this is not

03:37:45.766 --> 03:37:49.310
about transit. This could be perceived as a direct attack on

03:37:49.350 --> 03:37:52.974
humanity and global unity. It is a calculated effort to eliminate

03:37:53.022 --> 03:37:56.254
one of the last places where unhoused people can exist in peace.

03:37:56.382 --> 03:38:00.558
It offers no housing, no care, no support, just removal,

03:38:00.654 --> 03:38:04.022
displacement and eraser. This is not a plan. It is

03:38:04.046 --> 03:38:08.070
an eviction notice. Not from a home, but from public life itself.

03:38:08.230 --> 03:38:12.166
and violates section 7 of our charter and article 3 of the United Nations

03:38:12.198 --> 03:38:15.622
Declaration of Human Rights. The right to liberty, life and security of

03:38:15.726 --> 03:38:19.286
person. So let's call it what it is. You're voting

03:38:19.318 --> 03:38:22.598
to strip people of their legal rights because their presence makes you uncomfortable.

03:38:22.694 --> 03:38:26.390
You're voting to disappear the most vulnerable because their

03:38:26.430 --> 03:38:30.660
pain doesn't fit your development plans. You're voting to prioritize property

03:38:30.740 --> 03:38:34.516
over people. Do you think that this is in the best interest of our community

03:38:34.668 --> 03:38:38.036
and do you think this is progress? I have been there.

03:38:38.108 --> 03:38:41.924
I know what it feels like to be invisible. What I needed most wasn't to

03:38:41.932 --> 03:38:46.080
be removed, but to be seen, to be helped and

03:38:47.180 --> 03:38:50.580
And to be treated as human. instead

03:38:50.740 --> 03:38:53.972
You're offered tents taken down, belongings confiscated and

03:38:53.996 --> 03:38:57.282
lives destroyed, all while hiding behind a motion number.

03:38:57.386 --> 03:39:00.830
Tanner, you have one minute remaining. And the most

03:39:01.210 --> 03:39:04.786
horrifying part, you don't even ask the people this affects.

03:39:04.818 --> 03:39:07.970
You don't talk to the community. You don't even ask the committees who are working

03:39:08.010 --> 03:39:11.554
on inclusion and equity. You don't talk to a single person,

03:39:11.642 --> 03:39:14.770
even on the outside. This is not consultation. This is

03:39:14.810 --> 03:39:18.402
exclusion. This is not leadership. This is abandonment. This is

03:39:18.426 --> 03:39:21.950
not how a just society behaves. The region and the world

03:39:21.990 --> 03:39:25.870
is watching. And one day history will ask what you chose to value.

03:39:25.990 --> 03:39:29.390
Will it be convenience or courage? Will it be silence or justice?

03:39:29.470 --> 03:39:34.222
I ask that the region do not vote for this bylaw,

03:39:34.366 --> 03:39:37.934
because if the region votes in favor of this bylaw, the region is deliberately

03:39:37.982 --> 03:39:41.726
telling the people of our region that the region values profit

03:39:41.758 --> 03:39:45.086
over community, greed over integrity, and power over people.

03:39:45.238 --> 03:39:48.752
Please reject bylaw, the bylaw. Please stand up for

03:39:48.776 --> 03:39:52.640
human dignity, uphold the charter, and most

03:39:52.680 --> 03:39:56.416
importantly, listen to the voices you have tried so hard not to hear,

03:39:56.568 --> 03:39:59.660
because tonight I am speaking to them. Thank you.

03:40:00.200 --> 03:40:04.464
Thank you, Tanner. The next delegation is Ashley Hynd from Kitchener.

03:40:04.512 --> 03:40:05.220
Ashley,

03:40:12.040 --> 03:40:15.816
you have the floor, and you have three minutes. I requested to smudge

03:40:15.848 --> 03:40:19.816
before speaking, actually, so I'd like to do that, please, without cutting

03:40:19.848 --> 03:40:23.704
into my time. Am I

03:40:23.712 --> 03:40:26.632
not allowed to smudge in regional buildings according to the smudge policy?

03:40:26.816 --> 03:40:30.540
We certainly do smudge, but usually not in the middle of a delegation.

03:40:31.120 --> 03:40:33.460
Sorry, can I smudge them?

03:40:36.640 --> 03:40:39.420
I would suggest that you do your delegation.

03:40:40.410 --> 03:40:43.030
So you're telling me I can't smudge the ground myself?

03:40:44.250 --> 03:40:47.650
I think, Ashley, if we had had a previous notice of this,

03:40:47.770 --> 03:40:51.058
it could have been accommodated. But you're one of

03:40:51.114 --> 03:40:54.230
what, about 29 delegations tonight.

03:40:54.810 --> 03:40:58.274
No, that's okay. You just told an Indigenous person they can't smudge the

03:40:58.282 --> 03:41:00.350
ground themselves before speaking. Thank you.

03:41:04.090 --> 03:41:07.314
My name is Ashley. I have been a resident of this region for my entire

03:41:07.362 --> 03:41:10.820
life. Until recently, I worked as an outreach worker supporting people

03:41:10.860 --> 03:41:14.244
across the entire region, including people at 100 Vic.

03:41:14.372 --> 03:41:18.228
And I have experience with invisibleized homelessness several

03:41:18.284 --> 03:41:21.540
times in my life. I'm going to echo a lot of what has been said

03:41:21.580 --> 03:41:25.396
tonight, which to me shows you that the people living

03:41:25.428 --> 03:41:29.060
in our region, the people who voted for you and

03:41:29.100 --> 03:41:32.132
who you are supposed to represent, we are in

03:41:32.156 --> 03:41:34.550
agreement that this bylaw is not what we want.

03:41:35.330 --> 03:41:38.906
this bylaw not only goes against the commitment this very council

03:41:38.978 --> 03:41:42.266
made to the plan to end chronic homelessness, it also puts

03:41:42.298 --> 03:41:45.674
undue stress on the entire region. It impacts taxpayers

03:41:45.722 --> 03:41:49.946
with the waste of their dollars. It impacts frontline workers who are already stretched

03:41:49.978 --> 03:41:53.306
way too thin. And most importantly, it impacts all

03:41:53.378 --> 03:41:56.990
unhoused community members, not just those at 100 Vic.

03:41:57.890 --> 03:42:01.870
There are no homes available. Insufficient shelter spaces and

03:42:01.910 --> 03:42:05.278
motels are not housing. They are a tiny

03:42:05.374 --> 03:42:08.574
band aid that this region has used on a gaping wound

03:42:08.622 --> 03:42:11.982
for way too long. My mother always taught me that

03:42:12.006 --> 03:42:15.182
we are only ever as good as our support. Meaning that

03:42:15.206 --> 03:42:18.462
it doesn't matter how hard one tries, if they are

03:42:18.486 --> 03:42:22.610
not met with the support they need, then they will get nowhere.

03:42:23.270 --> 03:42:27.534
So I am asking you as my representatives to stop punishing

03:42:27.582 --> 03:42:30.250
people for your lack of support.

03:42:31.350 --> 03:42:35.102
Reject this bylaw, defer the situation to the plan to end

03:42:35.126 --> 03:42:38.542
chronic homelessness and show your constituents that

03:42:38.566 --> 03:42:43.006
you actually do represent us. Miigwech. Anyone

03:42:43.038 --> 03:42:45.890
want my minute twenty? Thank you Ashley.

03:42:46.230 --> 03:42:49.486
The next delegation is Chris Varga.

03:42:49.678 --> 03:42:52.786
And Chris, you, welcome to the podium

03:42:52.818 --> 03:42:56.226
and you have three minutes. Everybody that's getting three minutes

03:42:56.338 --> 03:42:59.906
registered after the deadline. Go ahead Chris.

03:43:00.018 --> 03:43:02.510
What we have here is a failed state.

03:43:03.450 --> 03:43:07.138
One in four Canadians are food insecure. One third of food bank

03:43:07.194 --> 03:43:10.562
clients are children. One in four Canadians can't afford

03:43:10.626 --> 03:43:14.290
the necessary items to achieve an acceptable

03:43:14.370 --> 03:43:17.712
standard of living. A growing number of people are unhoused.

03:43:17.866 --> 03:43:21.604
Tenant protections have eroded to the point that most

03:43:21.692 --> 03:43:24.388
low income persons have no secure housing.

03:43:24.564 --> 03:43:28.420
Astronomical grocery bills added onto

03:43:28.500 --> 03:43:31.876
astronomical rental rates have forced people to turn

03:43:31.948 --> 03:43:35.220
to food banks. And those with the least in

03:43:35.260 --> 03:43:37.920
resources are forced into the street,

03:43:38.300 --> 03:43:42.388
At which point social assistance cuts their housing allowance

03:43:42.484 --> 03:43:45.480
and forces people into long term homelessness.

03:43:46.690 --> 03:43:50.970
At the same time that we have this dire level

03:43:51.010 --> 03:43:54.410
of need, One in three food banks in Canada ran out of

03:43:54.450 --> 03:43:57.962
food in the past year and were forced to cut back and

03:43:57.986 --> 03:44:01.962
ration food. Shelters are at capacity as

03:44:01.986 --> 03:44:06.186
a newly homeless are arriving on the streets due to lack of public policy

03:44:06.338 --> 03:44:10.282
to create the type of housing needed the most. In the

03:44:10.306 --> 03:44:14.162
past seven years we have had a building boom locally, but

03:44:14.186 --> 03:44:18.002
the number of housing units built for those with the greatest need has

03:44:18.026 --> 03:44:21.830
been negligible. Where are our priorities?

03:44:23.050 --> 03:44:27.234
Whether it is by design or whether it is through negligence,

03:44:27.362 --> 03:44:31.202
we are facing the prospect of a shamefully large and growing

03:44:31.266 --> 03:44:35.186
homeless population which is pushed beyond the protections of government

03:44:35.258 --> 03:44:39.224
and social services, A population which is being stripped

03:44:39.322 --> 03:44:43.676
of the means of survival and which is rapidly being criminalized

03:44:43.788 --> 03:44:47.320
due to the actions or inactions of government.

03:44:48.100 --> 03:44:51.980
These people who are deserving of our support are

03:44:52.020 --> 03:44:54.880
now being pushed further to the margins.

03:44:55.940 --> 03:44:59.580
As the social safety net is failing. We are turning on

03:44:59.620 --> 03:45:03.260
the homeless instead of leading with compassion. Chris, you have 1 minute remaining.

03:45:03.420 --> 03:45:06.768
Public investments have not trickled down to those in need.

03:45:06.884 --> 03:45:11.144
The billion dollar ION funding has not allowed those without transportation

03:45:11.272 --> 03:45:14.680
to access the trains to travel, including homeless people in

03:45:14.720 --> 03:45:18.760
need of access to shelter. Public beautification campaigns have

03:45:18.800 --> 03:45:22.392
been at the expense of those who are forced to

03:45:22.416 --> 03:45:26.184
live rough but out of sight. Million dollar security

03:45:26.272 --> 03:45:29.784
guards at the Victoria Weber encampment are there to serve

03:45:29.912 --> 03:45:32.620
and protect adjacent businesses.

03:45:33.040 --> 03:45:35.832
Tax breaks have been given to local developers,

03:45:35.976 --> 03:45:39.928
none of which have welcomed the homeless. Shelters and motels are not

03:45:39.984 --> 03:45:42.580
measures that homeless people have been asking for.

03:45:43.280 --> 03:45:46.664
Finally we have arrived at the moment where as government

03:45:46.752 --> 03:45:50.088
has failed, The government also insists that

03:45:50.144 --> 03:45:53.528
others, namely the public and community groups, are not

03:45:53.584 --> 03:45:57.288
to step up to assist those in need. We are at a point

03:45:57.344 --> 03:46:00.614
now that we are instituting bylaws to prevent

03:46:00.742 --> 03:46:04.390
the public from assisting those who have been neglected and abandoned by

03:46:04.430 --> 03:46:08.326
public policy. Does failed state sound

03:46:08.358 --> 03:46:12.390
like hyperbole to you? Well, that all depends on

03:46:12.430 --> 03:46:16.050
where you stand on the basic. Chris If you could just sum up.

03:46:16.510 --> 03:46:20.662
Do not have housing? Do you not have access to food and life saving

03:46:20.726 --> 03:46:24.390
necessities such as safe supply? If you don't have

03:46:24.430 --> 03:46:28.210
access to to the necessities of life then it is not a stretch.

03:46:28.710 --> 03:46:32.286
Now we will criminalize you because your suffering goes unnoticed

03:46:32.318 --> 03:46:35.438
and unattended. The question before us here

03:46:35.494 --> 03:46:38.750
today is not what corner of this region can we

03:46:38.790 --> 03:46:41.690
disperse or push homeless persons into Next. Chris I'm going to ask you to sum up, your three minutes

03:46:42.310 --> 03:46:46.142
is up, Chris. Today there is an opportunity to stand against

03:46:46.166 --> 03:46:50.206
human rights by opposing a bylaw change that allows

03:46:50.238 --> 03:46:54.282
the region region to prevent camping despite a January

03:46:54.386 --> 03:46:58.138
2025 court ruling safeguarding this human right.

03:46:58.194 --> 03:46:58.950
Thank you.

03:47:02.690 --> 03:47:05.802
We're going to take a 10 minute

03:47:05.946 --> 03:47:09.530
bio break and then we'll resume with our meeting. Thank you all delegations

03:47:09.610 --> 03:47:11.190
for coming and for your.

03:58:36.000 --> 03:58:37.140
03:58:41.600 --> 03:58:44.632

I'll now entertain a motion to approve the

03:58:44.656 --> 03:58:48.680
minutes from previous meetings. They're listed 10.1 to 10.9.

03:58:48.720 --> 03:58:52.274
If I could have a mover, moved by Councillor Salonen, Seconded by Councillor

03:58:52.322 --> 03:58:55.430
Foxton. Please use your eScribe to vote.

03:59:33.540 --> 03:59:37.772
Colleagues that is carried. Under Communications items 11.1

03:59:37.796 --> 03:59:41.196
to 11.2, These have been received for information

03:59:41.348 --> 03:59:44.762
as well as council has been circulated further correspondence which

03:59:44.786 --> 03:59:48.282
was received following the publishing publishing of

03:59:48.306 --> 03:59:52.270
the addendum agenda. They will be attached to the official minutes.

03:59:56.290 --> 03:59:59.658
Next I would entertain a motion for the Committee

03:59:59.714 --> 04:00:03.418
of the whole to go into the committee of whole to consider reports.

04:00:03.474 --> 04:00:07.498
If I could have a mover. Moved by Councillor Rodrigues. Seconded by Councillor McCabe.

04:00:07.594 --> 04:00:11.108
Please use your eScribe to vote and that is that

04:00:11.164 --> 04:00:25.380
Council will go into committee of the whole to consider reports.

04:00:25.420 --> 04:00:26.360
04:00:36.470 --> 04:00:40.944

Colleagues The first report is the library committee summary of April 1,

04:00:41.060 --> 04:00:44.382
2025. If I could have a mover and a seconder. Moved by

04:00:44.406 --> 04:00:47.490
Councillor Salonen. Seconded by Councillor Foxton.

04:00:49.990 --> 04:00:53.886
We're voting on a recommendation that the regional municipality of Waterloo authorize

04:00:53.918 --> 04:00:57.582
the manager of library services to enter into a reciprocal borrowing

04:00:57.646 --> 04:01:01.278
arrangements with other public libraries from time to time on behalf

04:01:01.294 --> 04:01:04.878
of the region of Waterloo library, which forms part of the regional municipality

04:01:04.894 --> 04:01:08.302
of Waterloo with such agreements to the satisfaction of the

04:01:08.326 --> 04:01:25.966
regional solicitor. Colleagues

04:01:25.998 --> 04:01:29.566
That is carried. The next item is a vote to approve

04:01:29.598 --> 04:01:33.750
the summary which is listed on the agenda for sustainability,

04:01:33.910 --> 04:01:37.836
Infrastructure, and development committee from April 8,

04:01:38.035 --> 04:01:41.638
2025. Moved by Councillor,

04:01:41.734 --> 04:01:44.982
You have, you're moving it and you have

04:01:45.006 --> 04:01:48.050
a question. Do I have a seconder?

04:01:49.470 --> 04:01:53.254
Okay, so it's moved by Councillor Vrbanovic, Seconded by Councillor

04:01:53.302 --> 04:01:57.094
Rodrigues. And I'll go back to Councillor Vrbanovic.

04:01:57.142 --> 04:02:00.630
You have a question? Actually, just more a comment.

04:02:00.930 --> 04:02:03.978
I just want to again, as I did at committee,

04:02:04.034 --> 04:02:07.350
thank staff for the work that they did on the

04:02:07.730 --> 04:02:10.954
GRT plan and also want to thank Mr.

04:02:11.002 --> 04:02:14.346
Spooner and his team for coming to our council

04:02:14.418 --> 04:02:18.858
meeting recently. I know council really appreciated the presentation

04:02:18.954 --> 04:02:22.202
that they got. They had an opportunity to ask some

04:02:22.226 --> 04:02:26.122
questions, provide some, Provide some input and I

04:02:26.146 --> 04:02:29.770
think we look forward to seeing how it rolls out in the, In the years

04:02:29.810 --> 04:02:32.750
ahead. That's great. Councillor Rodrigues.

04:02:33.170 --> 04:02:36.442
Yeah, thank you, chair. And through you, I just want to thank staff as well

04:02:36.546 --> 04:02:40.202
for some discussions over the last couple weeks on the levels of service for

04:02:40.226 --> 04:02:43.882
asset management report, some work underway to include some

04:02:43.906 --> 04:02:47.230
of our assets that weren't listed in there, including trails.

04:02:47.650 --> 04:02:51.160
It's a growing network of, you know, both unpaved and paved trails

04:02:51.250 --> 04:02:54.044
