04:10:44.474 --> 04:10:47.970
We have an update. I would ask Dr. Wang, Commissioner of Public Health

04:10:48.010 --> 04:10:51.540
and Paramedic Services as well as Medical Officer of Health to provide

04:10:51.580 --> 04:10:55.332
a verbal update and this is being received for information.

04:10:55.516 --> 04:10:58.900
Welcome, Dr. Wang. Thank you Chair Redman and good evening members

04:10:58.940 --> 04:11:02.932
of Council. Thank you for the opportunity to present to

04:11:02.956 --> 04:11:06.356
the Board of Health an update with respect to measles

04:11:06.548 --> 04:11:11.040
and our annual enforcement of the Immunization of School Pupils Act.

04:11:11.980 --> 04:11:16.452
First, regarding measles, There has been an increased measles

04:11:16.516 --> 04:11:19.864
activity locally and throughout the province.

04:11:19.992 --> 04:11:24.504
As of Tuesday, April 22, we have 31

04:11:24.592 --> 04:11:28.808
confirmed cases locally. All cases here

04:11:28.864 --> 04:11:32.424
continue to be among those who are unvaccinated

04:11:32.472 --> 04:11:36.647
or under immunized. As of April 17,

04:11:36.912 --> 04:11:40.392
924 cases of measles have

04:11:40.416 --> 04:11:44.380
been reported across 15 local public health agencies

04:11:44.740 --> 04:11:47.852
with 109 new cases reported in

04:11:47.876 --> 04:11:51.148
the last week. Huron, Perth,

04:11:51.244 --> 04:11:55.052
Grand Erie and Southwestern public health units have been identified

04:11:55.116 --> 04:11:58.764
as areas of concern by the Ministry of Health,

04:11:58.852 --> 04:12:02.284
With a high number of confirmed cases and outbreaks

04:12:02.412 --> 04:12:04.480
which they are actively managing.

04:12:05.700 --> 04:12:09.484
measles can cause serious illness and death. Infants under

04:12:09.572 --> 04:12:13.690
one year of age, unimmunized pregnant individuals

04:12:13.770 --> 04:12:17.114
and people with weakened immune systems are at increased

04:12:17.162 --> 04:12:20.970
risk of complications. Measles symptoms

04:12:21.050 --> 04:12:25.290
begin 7 to 21 days after infection and

04:12:25.330 --> 04:12:29.690
may include high fever, cough, runny nose,

04:12:29.850 --> 04:12:33.818
red watery eyes and a red rash lasting four to seven

04:12:33.874 --> 04:12:37.514
days. There are steps residents can take to

04:12:37.522 --> 04:12:39.790
protect themselves and their families.

04:12:40.520 --> 04:12:44.096
One, ensure you are up to date with measles vaccinations.

04:12:44.288 --> 04:12:48.064
Residents who are unvaccinated are at high risk of contracting measles

04:12:48.112 --> 04:12:51.680
if exposed. and two, monitor yourself and your

04:12:51.720 --> 04:12:54.180
family for signs and symptoms of measles,

04:12:54.680 --> 04:12:58.480
especially after returning from international travel

04:12:58.640 --> 04:13:01.696
or areas experiencing measles outbreaks.

04:13:01.888 --> 04:13:05.584
Public Health will continue to provide information and recommendations

04:13:05.632 --> 04:13:09.476
on our website. We have added a self assessment tool

04:13:09.548 --> 04:13:13.124
for people to use for recommendations if they think they have been exposed

04:13:13.172 --> 04:13:16.724
to measles. We will also continue to add exposure

04:13:16.772 --> 04:13:20.040
sites and times if they occur locally.

04:13:22.780 --> 04:13:26.260
And finally, an update about the Immunization of School Pupils act,

04:13:26.300 --> 04:13:30.292
this time for secondary students. So as of April 17,

04:13:30.356 --> 04:13:33.936
there were approximately 2,873

04:13:34.008 --> 04:13:37.408
secondary students still not up to date

04:13:37.424 --> 04:13:41.376
with their immunization records. Parents and guardians have

04:13:41.448 --> 04:13:44.580
two weeks to ensure their children's records are updated

04:13:45.000 --> 04:13:49.440
either by submitting the records, receiving the required vaccines,

04:13:49.600 --> 04:13:52.020
or submitting an exemption.

04:13:52.600 --> 04:13:55.920
Secondary students with, excuse me,

04:13:55.960 --> 04:13:59.460
without updated records will be suspended On May 8.

04:14:00.610 --> 04:14:04.474
parents began receiving letters of notification for incomplete

04:14:04.522 --> 04:14:08.474
immunization information from Public Health In November

04:14:08.522 --> 04:14:12.730
of last year. there were 7,028

04:14:12.770 --> 04:14:14.910
letters of notification issued.

04:14:15.730 --> 04:14:19.322
So the numbers that we see today in terms of

04:14:19.426 --> 04:14:23.550
records still outstanding align with what we have seen historically

04:14:25.380 --> 04:14:29.040
based on the number of initial notification letters.

04:14:29.620 --> 04:14:32.972
And just a reminder that parents and guardians need

04:14:32.996 --> 04:14:36.680
to report their child's vaccinations to public health as

04:14:37.060 --> 04:14:40.796
healthcare providers do not report these vaccinations

04:14:40.908 --> 04:14:44.252
to us. And finally, students or

04:14:44.276 --> 04:14:48.172
parents can submit immunization records or provide notification

04:14:48.236 --> 04:14:51.942
of an upcoming vaccination appointment at

04:14:52.126 --> 04:14:57.030
RegionofWaterloo.ca/vaccines.

04:14:57.190 --> 04:15:00.870
Thank you. Thank you, Dr. Wang. I see

04:15:00.910 --> 04:15:04.422
