Do recognize, again, I want to acknowledge the feedback we heard about,

04:39:37.231 --> 04:39:40.489
you know, a specific element of that. We do know

04:39:40.529 --> 04:39:44.041
that very, very temporary locations

04:39:44.105 --> 04:39:47.625
are exactly that and should be that they need to come with the social supports

04:39:47.657 --> 04:39:51.097
and resources that we've built into this. And they,

04:39:51.233 --> 04:39:55.465
you know, the intention behind the way the financial

04:39:55.537 --> 04:39:59.109
implications were structured here today was to actually build in,

04:39:59.729 --> 04:40:03.289
you know, the mechanisms to ensure that those individuals who

04:40:03.329 --> 04:40:06.290
may choose that option in the short term,

04:40:06.670 --> 04:40:10.886
we don't end up in a situation where folks are in those locations

04:40:10.998 --> 04:40:14.582
for longer than they need to be. We recognize that that's the case

04:40:14.686 --> 04:40:17.766
and really trying to build in that flexibility within the overall system.

04:40:17.838 --> 04:40:21.142
So there may be investments made in one area that actually offset and

04:40:21.166 --> 04:40:25.014
create a space for somebody to support through. But this is really,

04:40:25.182 --> 04:40:28.310
the work of the Housing Stability System happens every

04:40:28.350 --> 04:40:31.418
single day in this community, as challenging as that is.

04:40:31.474 --> 04:40:35.162
And this is just some additional resources, some specific time for

04:40:35.186 --> 04:40:38.842
a specific group of individuals who we

04:40:38.866 --> 04:40:43.082
now know this will no longer be a viable option as of December

04:40:43.146 --> 04:40:46.938
1st. Thank you. That's all.

04:40:47.074 --> 04:40:49.310
That's great. Thank you. Councillor Erb.

04:40:52.130 --> 04:40:55.514
Thank you, Madam Chair. First, I'd like to thank

04:40:55.562 --> 04:40:59.140
all of the folks who delegated this evening.

04:41:01.080 --> 04:41:04.500
There are a lot of strong convictions in what you shared.

04:41:04.920 --> 04:41:08.860
Many of you made yourselves vulnerable. And for that,

04:41:09.320 --> 04:41:12.944
thank you. And I think the convictions

04:41:12.992 --> 04:41:16.352
that we heard this evening from the delegates are no different than those of

04:41:16.376 --> 04:41:20.380
us around this council table. Perhaps where we

04:41:20.760 --> 04:41:24.432
will differ is that for us we have to look at the

04:41:24.456 --> 04:41:27.744
implications of the effects for a broader

04:41:27.792 --> 04:41:28.380
community.

04:41:30.840 --> 04:41:34.272
For me, the first and most important part

04:41:34.296 --> 04:41:38.208
of this conversation has always been about the safety and

04:41:38.264 --> 04:41:41.408
the well being of the residents that live at 100

04:41:41.464 --> 04:41:45.728
Vic. and I know that's front and center for

04:41:45.784 --> 04:41:48.950
staff, for community partners and for members of council.

04:41:49.730 --> 04:41:53.930
And since this encampment began from

04:41:53.970 --> 04:41:57.450
day one, our staff and community partners have been on

04:41:57.490 --> 04:42:00.986
site daily offering support and alternate

04:42:01.018 --> 04:42:04.490
living arrangements for those. And I know that will continue

04:42:04.610 --> 04:42:08.314
if this bylaw is passed to secure housing

04:42:08.362 --> 04:42:11.962
for those folks. I think it's important

04:42:12.146 --> 04:42:15.536
for the community and council to remember the work

04:42:15.608 --> 04:42:20.048
our staff and community partners just completed in

04:42:20.104 --> 04:42:23.632
finding alternate accommodation for those that were living at

04:42:23.656 --> 04:42:26.860
the King Street Shelter or formerly the Schwaben Club.

04:42:27.960 --> 04:42:30.700
Since March 1st of this year,

04:42:31.320 --> 04:42:34.640
100 residents who were living at King Street Shelter were

04:42:34.680 --> 04:42:37.540
all offered alternative living accommodations,

04:42:37.960 --> 04:42:40.820
and over 90% of the residents accepted.

04:42:41.270 --> 04:42:45.070
And the really good news that is 29 of those residents are now

04:42:45.110 --> 04:42:49.342
living in permanent housing. The work

04:42:49.526 --> 04:42:53.438
done by staff and our community partners at the King street site are

04:42:53.574 --> 04:42:56.930
reassuring to me as we consider this bylaw.

04:42:57.590 --> 04:43:01.502
With the experience of the King street shelter and

04:43:01.526 --> 04:43:05.972
the ability to develop trusted relationships with residents,

04:43:06.166 --> 04:43:09.864
there are opportunities in the community to find alternate living

04:43:09.912 --> 04:43:13.848
arrangements for those at 100 Vic, which advances

04:43:13.944 --> 04:43:16.780
the plan to end chronic homelessness.

04:43:19.120 --> 04:43:23.096
The community as a whole, and especially the neighbors of 100 Victoria

04:43:23.128 --> 04:43:26.600
and the city of Kitchener have been very patient with this

04:43:26.640 --> 04:43:30.060
location and some of the challenges this site has presented.

04:43:30.640 --> 04:43:34.684
And I think the time has come that given the opportunity we now have to

04:43:34.772 --> 04:43:38.476
develop the property as part of the Kitchener central transit

04:43:38.508 --> 04:43:41.852
hub, And also respecting the

04:43:41.876 --> 04:43:45.804
challenges that has been presented for the neighbor that has been present for

04:43:45.812 --> 04:43:49.772
the neighborhood, the city, and the region. I'm going

04:43:49.796 --> 04:43:51.440
to support this bylaw.

04:43:52.420 --> 04:43:55.740
and in doing so, I have complete faith in our

04:43:55.780 --> 04:43:59.404
staff and community partners that they'll fulfill

04:43:59.452 --> 04:44:03.860
the intent of this bylaw with the best interests of current residents in mind,

04:44:04.640 --> 04:44:08.792
being respectful of the human rights of the individuals affected and

04:44:08.816 --> 04:44:12.312
understanding the dynamics of this population so

04:44:12.336 --> 04:44:15.864
that they're treated with respect, kindness, and understanding

04:44:15.912 --> 04:44:19.896
what an unconventional lifestyle these folks have been living.

04:44:20.088 --> 04:44:23.352
Thank you. Thank you.

04:44:23.376 --> 04:44:24.700
Councillor Vrbanovic.

04:44:26.160 --> 04:44:30.060
Thanks very much, Chair Redman. And I do have some

04:44:30.100 --> 04:44:33.084
questions of staff, but before I ask them,

04:44:33.252 --> 04:44:36.348
I do want to begin by thanking all of the delegations who

04:44:36.484 --> 04:44:39.772
came in this evening, as well as all of those

04:44:39.796 --> 04:44:43.196
who have taken the time to write to us in recent

04:44:43.268 --> 04:44:47.052
days. There have been a significant number of

04:44:47.076 --> 04:44:51.200
people and clearly we heard from folks

04:44:51.940 --> 04:44:54.760
with both recent and past lived experience,

04:44:55.070 --> 04:44:58.998
those who are involved in serving these

04:44:59.054 --> 04:45:03.062
residents, as well as just other everyday citizens

04:45:03.126 --> 04:45:06.530
who, quite frankly, are part of the

04:45:06.990 --> 04:45:10.710
caring nature of what this region has

04:45:10.750 --> 04:45:13.730
been known for for many years.

04:45:14.350 --> 04:45:16.730
My question to Mr. Sweeney,

04:45:17.390 --> 04:45:20.290
Before I make my final comments.

04:45:21.720 --> 04:45:25.024
A couple questions, Mr. Sweeney, I'm wondering if you

04:45:25.032 --> 04:45:29.232
