04:47:56.010 --> 04:47:59.170
beds within that. We also have

04:47:59.210 --> 04:48:03.070
two of our waterloo regional housing redevelopment projects coming

04:48:03.110 --> 04:48:06.622
on stream later this year as well.

04:48:06.806 --> 04:48:10.238
And I think that's the

04:48:10.374 --> 04:48:13.822
list that you pointed to and that's coming

04:48:13.846 --> 04:48:17.982
to my memory. But I can certainly get council some more updated and

04:48:18.006 --> 04:48:21.790
accurate numbers. Those are just what I can share with you this evening.

04:48:21.870 --> 04:48:25.726
Well, and I think that's helpful. But I guess that

04:48:25.878 --> 04:48:29.668
to me demonstrates, and I understand there's

04:48:29.684 --> 04:48:33.460
not a direct correlation of, you know, one person potentially from

04:48:33.500 --> 04:48:37.300
100 Vic to one of these spots. But overall the system is

04:48:37.340 --> 04:48:40.724
going to go up, you know, by the end

04:48:40.732 --> 04:48:44.234
of this year based on the numbers you talked about, by about 65,

04:48:44.358 --> 04:48:47.460
70 units and then another 100 at some point in

04:48:47.500 --> 04:48:50.996
2026, plus the other ones that you talked

04:48:51.028 --> 04:48:54.532
about. And then that gives you flexibility as you

04:48:54.556 --> 04:48:57.790
work with different clients to different residents to move

04:48:57.830 --> 04:49:01.422
them, to move people where the appropriate

04:49:01.566 --> 04:49:05.230
housing may be for them, whether it's Erbs street, whether it's one of these

04:49:05.270 --> 04:49:09.022
buildings or something like that. Is that correct? That's how the

04:49:09.046 --> 04:49:13.022
system works? Yeah. That's the idea and the

04:49:13.046 --> 04:49:16.014
intent behind the plan that we've put forward. Yes.

04:49:16.142 --> 04:49:20.174
Okay. Thank you. So, Madam Chair, if I can just make a brief

04:49:20.222 --> 04:49:24.010
comment then, and thank you to staff for those questions and for the work

04:49:24.990 --> 04:49:28.022
that's been done on this. I think all

04:49:28.046 --> 04:49:31.670
of us around this horseshoe understand the

04:49:31.710 --> 04:49:35.462
significance of this issue and the

04:49:35.486 --> 04:49:39.490
commitment that this council as a whole has had for some time

04:49:39.950 --> 04:49:43.542
towards addressing the housing and

04:49:43.566 --> 04:49:46.710
homelessness issue and the commitment that this

04:49:46.750 --> 04:49:50.374
council and our staff, working with community

04:49:50.462 --> 04:49:54.450
partners, have had in terms of trying to

04:49:54.830 --> 04:49:58.710
address the overall situation

04:49:58.790 --> 04:50:02.150
around homelessness, together with our provincial and federal partners.

04:50:02.310 --> 04:50:05.830
And I know many of us have been pushing on these issues even

04:50:05.950 --> 04:50:09.094
as recently as the current provincial and federal elections,

04:50:09.142 --> 04:50:12.902
about the importance of continued investment in

04:50:12.926 --> 04:50:16.130
these areas. I will say that,

04:50:17.110 --> 04:50:20.830
like Councillor Erb, one of the things that has concerned me has

04:50:20.870 --> 04:50:24.318
been the safety of the situation. And we heard

04:50:24.334 --> 04:50:27.662
this from a number of the

04:50:27.686 --> 04:50:30.830
delegations. And certainly there is a sense of community that

04:50:30.870 --> 04:50:34.286
has developed at 100 Vic and some safety,

04:50:34.318 --> 04:50:37.534
But I think we also need to understand that there are components

04:50:37.582 --> 04:50:41.214
that have been challenging for residents as well.

04:50:41.382 --> 04:50:45.050
And I can share that In 2023,

04:50:46.830 --> 04:50:51.542
I know there was five fire calls and 16 EMS,

04:50:51.686 --> 04:50:55.090
Sixteen times that fire responded to

04:50:55.870 --> 04:50:59.766
a tiered response medical call. I'm not sure what the EMS numbers

04:50:59.798 --> 04:51:04.710
are. I'm sure our staff could provide those. In 2024,

04:51:04.830 --> 04:51:08.902
those responses went from 5 to 16 for

04:51:08.926 --> 04:51:12.476
fire calls and medical calls that were a tiered response

04:51:12.508 --> 04:51:16.460
that fire responded to went from 16 to 26. All that to

04:51:16.500 --> 04:51:20.360
say that those fire calls went up by about 320%

04:51:20.900 --> 04:51:24.920
and the tiered medical calls went up by 62.5%.

04:51:25.540 --> 04:51:28.988
And I do know that in 2025, we've seen a further

04:51:29.044 --> 04:51:32.668
increase in the fire calls. And so I raise that

04:51:32.724 --> 04:51:36.236
because it demonstrates to me that

04:51:36.388 --> 04:51:40.156
as much as there's a strong sense of community and supports

04:51:40.188 --> 04:51:43.852
that are there, there are also some real safety issues for the

04:51:43.876 --> 04:51:47.324
residents that concern me. And quite frankly, as a

04:51:47.332 --> 04:51:50.040
community, we need to do better. And,

04:51:50.900 --> 04:51:54.972
you know, this bylaw, in my view, is trying to address the situation

04:51:55.036 --> 04:51:58.444
at 100 Vic and, you know,

04:51:58.532 --> 04:52:02.556
over a period of time, and we have eight months now to work

04:52:02.628 --> 04:52:05.948
collaboratively with our working

04:52:06.004 --> 04:52:10.040
group, with the residents, and with others

04:52:10.500 --> 04:52:14.028
in order to make sure that we, you know,

04:52:14.084 --> 04:52:17.960
everybody who wants to can find

04:52:18.260 --> 04:52:21.340
a place that's appropriate for them with the right supports

04:52:21.500 --> 04:52:24.636
for better outcomes. And so I will be supporting this bylaw

04:52:24.668 --> 04:52:28.332
this evening. Thank you. I have three more speakers and then I'm going to call

04:52:28.356 --> 04:52:32.114
the question. Councillor Craig. well, thank you, Madam Chair.

04:52:32.202 --> 04:52:35.314
I do appreciate the comments I've heard from my fellow

04:52:35.362 --> 04:52:39.378
councillors. And I can state unequivocally since I've

04:52:39.394 --> 04:52:43.602
been here on regional council that this is a council that does care

04:52:43.706 --> 04:52:47.762
